window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"21 animated films, level Spirits 2":"21 部動畫影片，烈酒二級","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Spirits 2 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過烈酒二級考試的學習路徑，只需要回答 5 個簡短的問題。","Spirits 2 exam":"烈酒二級考試","All of Spirits 2":"烈酒二級全部內容","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Spirits 2 syllabus.":"課程、字卡和錯題：只包含烈酒二級的課程大綱。","Spirits 2 games":"烈酒二級遊戲","Short games on Spirits 2 questions and terms.":"以烈酒二級題目和術語為主的小遊戲。","Raw materials and fermentation":"原料與發酵","How distillation works":"蒸餾如何運作","After distillation":"蒸餾之後","Fruit spirits: Cognac and Armagnac":"水果烈酒：Cognac 與 Armagnac","Calvados, Grappa and Pisco":"Calvados、Grappa 與 Pisco","Irish, Canadian and Japanese whisky":"愛爾蘭、加拿大與日本威士忌","Tequila and Mezcal":"Tequila 與 Mezcal","Other flavoured spirits":"其他調味烈酒","Liqueurs":"利口酒","Aromatised wines: vermouth":"加味葡萄酒：香艾酒","Workstation, tools and glassware":"工作檯、工具與杯具","Ingredients and balance":"材料與平衡","Tasting and judging spirits":"品飲與評判烈酒","Spirits production":"烈酒的生產","The principal spirits":"主要烈酒","Flavoured spirits, liqueurs, aromatised wines":"調味烈酒、利口酒、加味葡萄酒","f3":"f3","The bar and cocktails":"酒吧與調酒","What is the correct order of the four stages of spirit production?":"烈酒生產四個階段的正確順序是什麼？","Fermentation, raw material, distillation, compulsory ageing":"發酵、原料、蒸餾、強制陳年","Raw material, fermentation, post-distillation, distillation":"原料、發酵、蒸餾後處理、蒸餾","A sugary liquid is made first, then fermented, distilled and finally prepared for sale.":"先製作含糖液體，再發酵、蒸餾，最後做好上市前的準備。","You cannot distil a liquid that does not yet contain alcohol, so fermentation must come before distillation. Post-distillation steps such as dilution or filtration come last. Ageing is not a compulsory stage for every spirit: many are never aged.":"還不含酒精的液體無法蒸餾，所以發酵一定在蒸餾之前。稀釋或過濾等蒸餾後處理排在最後。陳年並不是每種烈酒都必經的階段：許多烈酒從不陳年。","Which two things does a raw material provide to a distiller?":"原料為蒸餾師提供哪兩樣東西？","Carbohydrates and congeners":"碳水化合物和同屬物","Yeast and carbon dioxide":"酵母和二氧化碳","Colour and sweetness ready for the bottle":"可直接裝瓶的顏色和甜味","Alcohol and enzymes":"酒精和酵素","The raw material offers a carbohydrate store for yeast and a set of flavours, the congeners.":"原料提供給酵母的碳水化合物儲備，以及一組風味，也就是同屬物。","Carbohydrates are yeast food; congeners are the flavour compounds. Yeast is added by the producer and carbon dioxide is created during fermentation. Alcohol is not in the raw material: the yeast makes it.":"碳水化合物是酵母的食物；同屬物是風味化合物。酵母由生產者添加，二氧化碳則在發酵過程中產生。原料裡沒有酒精：酒精是酵母製造的。","What are the compounds responsible for a spirit's aromas and flavours called?":"為烈酒帶來香氣和風味的化合物叫做什麼？","Congeners":"同屬物","Starches":"澱粉","Congeners are the compounds that give aroma and taste.":"同屬物是帶來香氣和味道的化合物。","Some congeners come from the raw material, others form during fermentation or maturation. Enzymes convert starch into sugar; they do not provide aroma. Starch is a carbohydrate yeast cannot use directly.":"有些同屬物來自原料，有些在發酵或熟成過程中形成。酵素把澱粉轉化為糖，並不提供香氣。澱粉是酵母無法直接利用的碳水化合物。","Which of these raw materials already contains sugars that yeast can use straight away?":"下列哪一種原料本身就含有酵母可以立刻利用的糖？","Freshly harvested raw agave":"剛採收的生龍舌蘭","Sugar cane, like grapes, stores simple sugars.":"甘蔗和葡萄一樣，儲存的是單醣。","Barley and potatoes store starch, which has to be converted with enzymes. Agave stores inulin, which only becomes sugar when cooked: raw, it is not ready for yeast.":"大麥和馬鈴薯儲存的是澱粉，必須用酵素轉化。龍舌蘭儲存的是菊糖，要烹煮後才會變成糖：生的時候酵母無法利用。","In what form does agave store its carbohydrates?":"龍舌蘭以什麼形式儲存碳水化合物？","Inulin":"菊糖","Starch":"澱粉","Sucrose ready to ferment":"可直接發酵的蔗糖","Esters":"酯類","The heart of the agave keeps its reserves as inulin.":"龍舌蘭的心以菊糖的形式保存養分。","Inulin is a complex carbohydrate, like starch, but it is typical of agave; cooking turns it into sugars. Starch is found in grains and potatoes. Esters are not carbohydrates at all: they are fruity congeners formed in fermentation.":"菊糖和澱粉一樣是複雜的碳水化合物，但它是龍舌蘭特有的；烹煮會把它變成糖。澱粉存在於穀物和馬鈴薯中。酯類根本不是碳水化合物：它們是發酵中形成的果香同屬物。","During malting, what does the sprouting barley produce?":"製麥過程中，發芽的大麥會產生什麼？","Enzymes that can turn starch into sugar":"能把澱粉轉化為糖的酵素","Alcohol, which is later concentrated in the still":"酒精，之後在蒸餾器中濃縮","Inulin, which makes the grains sweeter":"菊糖，讓穀粒變得更甜","Natural yeast ready for fermentation":"可直接用來發酵的天然酵母","The young plant releases enzymes that are later used to convert starch.":"幼芽釋放出酵素，之後用來轉化澱粉。","Dampened, warm grains sprout and produce enzymes; heat then stops the growth. When the malted barley is ground and mixed with warm water, the enzymes turn starch into sugar. No alcohol forms at this stage, and yeast is added later.":"浸濕且保持溫暖的穀粒會發芽並產生酵素；接著用熱停止生長。把麥芽大麥磨碎並與溫水混合後，酵素就把澱粉轉化為糖。這個階段不會產生酒精，酵母是之後才加入的。","A producer uses corn and wheat. What is usually done to convert their starch?":"一位生產者使用玉米和小麥。通常怎麼轉化它們的澱粉？","Cooks them in water, then adds malted barley or enzymes":"先在水中烹煮，再加入麥芽大麥或酵素","Ferments them whole with no preparation at all":"完全不經處理，整粒直接發酵","Distils them straight away to extract the sugar":"立刻蒸餾以萃取糖分","Smokes them over peat to dissolve the starch":"用泥煤煙燻以溶解澱粉","Cooking makes the starch soluble, then enzymes turn it into sugar.":"烹煮讓澱粉變得可溶，接著酵素把它轉化為糖。","Grains other than barley are usually cooked rather than malted; the enzymes come from a little malted barley or bought-in preparations. Yeast cannot eat starch, so there is no fermentation without conversion. Distillation does not extract sugar, and peat only adds smoky aroma.":"大麥以外的穀物通常是烹煮而不是製麥；酵素來自少量麥芽大麥或外購的酵素製劑。酵母吃不了澱粉，所以沒有轉化就沒有發酵。蒸餾不會萃取糖分，泥煤只會增添煙燻香氣。","How is the inulin in agave turned into sugar?":"龍舌蘭中的菊糖如何變成糖？","By cooking the piña":"烹煮 piña","By malting the leaves":"把葉片拿去製麥","By adding malted barley to the raw juice":"在生汁液中加入麥芽大麥","By distilling the raw heart":"蒸餾生的龍舌蘭心","The heat of cooking converts inulin into sugars.":"烹煮的熱度把菊糖轉化為糖。","The spiky leaves are cut off and discarded: only the heart, the piña, is used; it is cooked and then crushed to release the sweet juice. Malted barley is for grain starch, not agave. Distilling before fermentation would not produce a spirit.":"帶刺的葉片會被切除丟棄：只使用心部，也就是 piña；它先經烹煮，再壓碎以釋出甜汁。麥芽大麥是用於穀物澱粉的，不是龍舌蘭。在發酵前蒸餾不會得到烈酒。","What is the heart of the agave used for spirits called?":"用來製作烈酒的龍舌蘭心叫做什麼？","Green malt":"綠麥芽","Wort":"麥汁","Pomace":"果渣","The piña is the hard core left once the leaves are removed.":"piña 是切除葉片後留下的堅硬核心。","The piña is where the plant stores its inulin, which is why it is the valuable part. Green malt is sprouted barley before it is heated. Wort is the sweet liquid made from grains, and pomace is what is left of grapes after pressing.":"piña 是植株儲存菊糖的地方，所以它是有價值的部分。綠麥芽是加熱前的發芽大麥。麥汁是用穀物製成的甜液，果渣則是葡萄壓榨後剩下的東西。","What does yeast produce during alcoholic fermentation?":"酒精發酵過程中，酵母會產生什麼？","Alcohol, carbon dioxide and congeners":"酒精、二氧化碳和同屬物","Sugar, oxygen and colour":"糖、氧氣和顏色","Starch, water and large amounts of enzymes":"澱粉、水和大量酵素","Pure ethanol only, with nothing else":"只有純乙醇，沒有別的","Yeast consumes sugar and creates alcohol, carbon dioxide and flavours.":"酵母消耗糖，並產生酒精、二氧化碳和風味。","Sugar is the yeast's food, so it is used up, not produced. Besides ethanol, other alcohols and many congeners such as fruity esters are formed: you never get pure ethanol. Carbon dioxide is a waste product that escapes into the air.":"糖是酵母的食物，所以是被消耗掉，而不是被製造出來。除了乙醇，還會形成其他醇類和許多同屬物，例如帶果香的酯類：永遠不會得到純乙醇。二氧化碳是廢棄產物，會散逸到空氣中。","In a fermentation vat the liquid bubbles as if boiling. What causes this?":"發酵槽裡的液體冒著泡，看起來像在沸騰。原因是什麼？","Carbon dioxide released by the yeast":"酵母釋放的二氧化碳","Ethanol vapour evaporating from the surface":"從表面蒸發的乙醇蒸氣","Heat added to speed up the fermentation":"為了加快發酵而加的熱","Oxygen produced by the malt enzymes":"麥芽酵素產生的氧氣","The bubbles are carbon dioxide, a waste product of fermentation.":"氣泡是二氧化碳，也就是發酵的廢棄產物。","An active fermentation looks as if it is boiling, but the liquid is not actually boiling: it is gas rising to the surface. The ethanol stays in the liquid until it is heated in a still. Enzymes do not produce oxygen.":"旺盛的發酵看起來像在沸騰，但液體其實沒有沸騰：那是氣體升到表面。乙醇會留在液體中，直到在蒸餾器中加熱。酵素不會產生氧氣。","What is the typical alcoholic strength of the liquid at the end of fermentation?":"發酵結束時，液體的酒精濃度通常是多少？","Around 8–10% abv":"大約 8–10% abv","Around 25–30% abv":"大約 25–30% abv","Around 40% abv, ready to bottle":"大約 40% abv，可直接裝瓶","Around 1–2% abv":"大約 1–2% abv","Distillers usually aim for a fermented liquid of about 8–10% abv.":"蒸餾師通常以大約 8–10% abv 的發酵液為目標。","25–30% abv is the strength of low wines after a first pot-still distillation. 40% is a typical bottling strength, reached only after distillation and dilution. Fermentation alone cannot reach these levels.":"25–30% abv 是壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾後低度酒的濃度。40% 是典型的裝瓶濃度，要經過蒸餾和稀釋才能達到。光靠發酵無法達到這些濃度。","When does alcoholic fermentation end?":"酒精發酵什麼時候結束？","When all the sugar has been converted":"所有的糖都被轉化之後","When the liquid reaches 40% abv":"液體達到 40% abv 時","After exactly twenty-four hours in every distillery":"在每一家蒸餾廠都是剛好二十四小時後","When starch begins to form":"澱粉開始形成時","Once the sugar is gone, the yeast has nothing left to convert.":"糖一用完，酵母就沒有東西可以轉化了。","Fermentation stops when the yeast's food runs out, usually at around 8–10% abv. 40% abv cannot be reached by fermentation. There is no fixed duration shared by everyone, and starch does not form during fermentation.":"酵母的食物耗盡時發酵就停止，通常在 8–10% abv 左右。發酵無法達到 40% abv。沒有大家通用的固定時間，發酵過程中也不會形成澱粉。","Which alcohol makes up by far the largest part of the fermented liquid?":"在發酵液中，哪一種醇所占的比例遠高於其他？","Ethanol":"乙醇","Methanol":"甲醇","Fusel alcohols":"雜醇","Ethanol accounts for the vast majority of the alcohol volume.":"乙醇占了酒精體積的絕大部分。","Methanol and fusel alcohols are present, but in much smaller amounts. Ethanol is the alcohol that distillation concentrates most and that gives a spirit its strength. Glycerol is not one of the key alcohols discussed here.":"甲醇和雜醇也存在，但量少得多。乙醇是蒸餾時濃縮最多、並賦予烈酒酒精濃度的醇。甘油不屬於這裡討論的主要醇類。","Which group of congeners, formed in fermentation, has a fruity smell?":"哪一類在發酵中形成的同屬物帶有果香？","Inulins":"菊糖","Caramels":"焦糖","Esters are fruity-smelling congeners created in fermentation.":"酯類是發酵中產生、帶果香的同屬物。","Enzymes turn starch into sugar and inulin is agave's carbohydrate: neither is an aroma. Caramel is a colouring added after distillation, not a product of fermentation.":"酵素把澱粉轉化為糖，菊糖是龍舌蘭的碳水化合物：兩者都不是香氣。焦糖色是蒸餾後添加的色素，不是發酵的產物。","Why do nearly all distillers use selected yeast?":"為什麼幾乎所有蒸餾師都使用選育酵母？","To get the same congeners every time":"為了每次都得到相同的同屬物","To reach over 20% abv during fermentation":"為了在發酵時達到 20% abv 以上","To avoid having to distil the liquid twice":"為了不必把液體蒸餾兩次","To convert starch without needing enzymes":"為了不靠酵素就能轉化澱粉","Selected yeast gives a reliable, consistent result batch after batch.":"選育酵母能一批又一批帶來可靠、一致的結果。","Many congeners are formed in fermentation, and an aroma missing after fermentation cannot appear in the spirit. That is why consistent yeast is essential. Yeast does not convert starch and does not change how many distillations are needed.":"許多同屬物在發酵中形成，發酵後缺少的香氣不可能出現在烈酒中。所以穩定一致的酵母至關重要。酵母不會轉化澱粉，也不會改變需要蒸餾的次數。","A desired aroma is missing from the fermented liquid. What will happen after distillation?":"發酵液中缺少一種想要的香氣。蒸餾後會怎麼樣？","It will also be missing from the new spirit":"新酒中同樣不會有","It will appear thanks to the heat of the still":"蒸餾器的熱會讓它出現","It will form in the heads, during the first cut of the second distillation":"它會在酒頭中形成，也就是第二次蒸餾的第一次切取時","It will develop if distilled to a higher strength":"蒸餾到更高濃度就會發展出來","Distillation can only select and concentrate what is already present.":"蒸餾只能篩選並濃縮原本就存在的東西。","The still does not create new aromas: it separates and concentrates existing ones. Distilling to a higher strength actually reduces the number of congeners. The heads contain volatile, solvent-smelling compounds, not new aromas appearing from nowhere.":"蒸餾器不會創造新的香氣：它只是分離並濃縮現有的香氣。蒸餾到更高的濃度其實會減少同屬物的數量。酒頭含有易揮發、帶溶劑氣味的化合物，而不是憑空出現的新香氣。","A US label says 90 proof. What strength is that?":"一張美國酒標上寫著 90 proof。這是多少濃度？","45% abv":"45% abv","90% abv":"90% abv","30% abv":"30% abv","60% abv":"60% abv","Two degrees proof equal 1% abv, so 90 proof = 45% abv.":"2 度 proof 等於 1% abv，所以 90 proof = 45% abv。","Simply halve the proof figure. Mixing up proof and abv would suggest 90%, the strength of a near-neutral spirit. The word 'overproof' seen on some rum labels belongs to a different, historic system that is no longer used.":"只要把 proof 的數字除以二。把 proof 和 abv 搞混會以為是 90%，那是接近中性烈酒的濃度。某些蘭姆酒酒標上的「overproof」一詞屬於另一套已不再使用的舊制度。","Which spirit is the exception because nearly all congeners are removed?":"哪一種烈酒是例外，因為幾乎所有同屬物都被去除？","Rhum agricole":"Rhum agricole","In vodka, the producer removes almost all congeners, so the raw material shows little.":"在伏特加中，生產者去除了幾乎所有同屬物，所以原料的特色不太明顯。","Tequila, Cognac and rhum agricole aim instead to keep raw-material character: Tequila, for instance, always shows earthy, peppery blue-agave notes. Vodka is designed to be almost neutral.":"Tequila、Cognac 和 rhum agricole 則力求保留原料特色：例如 Tequila 總是帶有藍色龍舌蘭的土壤和胡椒氣息。伏特加的設計就是要近乎中性。","Why can a small flaw in the raw material spoil a spirit?":"為什麼原料的小瑕疵會毀掉一款烈酒？","Because distillation concentrates it":"因為蒸餾會把它濃縮","Because yeast always turns it into pure methanol":"因為酵母總會把它變成純甲醇","Because it blocks starch conversion":"因為它會阻礙澱粉轉化","Because it darkens the spirit during final bottling":"因為它會在最後裝瓶時讓烈酒顏色變深","Distillation concentrates aromas, faulty ones included.":"蒸餾會濃縮香氣，有瑕疵的香氣也不例外。","As in a reduced sauce, something barely noticeable becomes obvious. That is why a quality spirit needs quality raw materials. The other answers describe effects that have nothing to do with concentration.":"就像收汁的醬汁一樣，原本幾乎察覺不到的東西會變得明顯。所以優質烈酒需要優質原料。其他答案描述的效果都與濃縮無關。","For a potato vodka, how is the starch converted into sugar?":"製作馬鈴薯伏特加時，澱粉如何轉化為糖？","Cooking in water, then bought-in enzymes":"先在水中烹煮，再加入外購的酵素","Malting the potatoes in a warm room":"把馬鈴薯放在溫暖的房間裡製麥","Direct fermentation of raw, chopped potatoes":"把生馬鈴薯切塊後直接發酵","Slow cooking in brick ovens, as for agave":"像龍舌蘭一樣在磚爐中慢慢烹煮","Cooked potatoes become a liquid full of dissolved starch, then enzymes turn it into sugar.":"煮過的馬鈴薯變成充滿溶解澱粉的液體，接著酵素把澱粉轉化為糖。","It is a two-step process: cooking makes the starch soluble and enzymes convert it. Potatoes are not malted, and raw they cannot ferment because yeast does not eat starch. With agave, heat alone works because inulin behaves differently from starch.":"這是兩步驟的過程：烹煮讓澱粉可溶，酵素再加以轉化。馬鈴薯不會製麥，生的也無法發酵，因為酵母不吃澱粉。龍舌蘭只靠熱就行，是因為菊糖的性質和澱粉不同。","Which statement about the sugary liquid a spirit starts from is true?":"關於烈酒起點的含糖液體，下列哪一項正確？","It can come from any farm product with carbohydrates":"可以來自任何含碳水化合物的農產品","It can only come from grapes or other fruit":"只能來自葡萄或其他水果","It must always contain at least 10% alcohol before fermentation":"發酵前一定要含有至少 10% 的酒精","It is made only from malted grains":"只能用麥芽穀物製成","Grapes, grains, cane, potatoes, agave: all that is needed is carbohydrate.":"葡萄、穀物、甘蔗、馬鈴薯、龍舌蘭：只需要有碳水化合物。","The whole aim of the first stage is to turn carbohydrates into a sugary liquid. There is no alcohol before fermentation, so the third option is impossible. Fruit and malted grains are only some of the many possible raw materials.":"第一階段的目標就是把碳水化合物變成含糖液體。發酵前沒有酒精，所以第三個選項不可能成立。水果和麥芽穀物只是眾多可用原料中的一部分。","In what form do grains store their carbohydrates?":"穀物以什麼形式儲存碳水化合物？","Simple sugars ready for the yeast":"酵母可直接利用的單醣","Inulin, like agave":"菊糖，和龍舌蘭一樣","Grains store starch, which must be turned into sugar before fermentation.":"穀物儲存的是澱粉，發酵前必須先轉化為糖。","Barley, corn, wheat and rye hold starch, which yeast cannot feed on directly. Inulin is agave's store, not that of grains. Esters are fruity congeners made during fermentation, not a plant's reserve.":"大麥、玉米、小麥和黑麥含有澱粉，酵母無法直接利用。菊糖是龍舌蘭的儲備，不是穀物的。酯類是發酵中產生的果香同屬物，不是植物的養分儲備。","Which pair of raw materials needs its carbohydrates converted before fermentation?":"哪一組原料必須先轉化碳水化合物才能發酵？","Grains and agave":"穀物和龍舌蘭","Grapes and sugar cane":"葡萄和甘蔗","Freshly picked and pressed apples and pears":"剛採收並壓榨的蘋果和梨","Grapes and molasses":"葡萄和糖蜜","Grains (starch) and agave (inulin) hold complex carbohydrates that must become sugars.":"穀物（澱粉）和龍舌蘭（菊糖）含有複雜的碳水化合物，必須先變成糖。","Grapes, fruit, cane juice and molasses already hold sugars the yeast can use. Grains need enzymes, and agave needs its piña cooked. That is why raw-material processing differs so much between spirits.":"葡萄、水果、甘蔗汁和糖蜜本來就含有酵母可以利用的糖。穀物需要酵素，龍舌蘭則需要烹煮 piña。這就是為什麼不同烈酒的原料處理方式差別這麼大。","What is the aim of the stage of selecting and processing the raw material?":"挑選和處理原料這個階段的目標是什麼？","To obtain a sugary liquid":"得到含糖液體","To obtain an already alcoholic liquid of about 10% abv":"得到已含酒精、約 10% abv 的液體","To remove all the congeners":"去除所有同屬物","The aim is to use the raw material's carbohydrates to create a sugary liquid.":"目標是利用原料的碳水化合物製作出含糖液體。","The roughly 10% alcoholic liquid only appears later, with fermentation. The raw material's congeners are often valuable, so they are not removed at this stage. Colour comes after distillation.":"約 10% 的含酒精液體要到之後發酵時才出現。原料的同屬物往往很有價值，所以這個階段不會去除。顏色是蒸餾之後才有的。","What does 'abv' mean?":"「abv」是什麼意思？","The percentage of the liquid's volume that is alcohol":"酒精占液體體積的百分比","The weight of alcohol in grams per litre":"每公升所含酒精的公克數","The proof system used in the USA":"美國使用的 proof 制度","The amount of sugar left after fermentation":"發酵後剩下的糖量","abv stands for alcohol by volume: 10% abv means a tenth of the liquid is alcohol.":"abv 代表酒精體積百分比（alcohol by volume）：10% abv 表示液體的十分之一是酒精。","It is a volume measure, not a weight. Proof is a different US scale: two degrees proof equal 1% abv. Residual sugar is irrelevant: by the end of fermentation it has all been used up.":"它是體積的度量，不是重量。proof 是美國另一套標度：2 度 proof 等於 1% abv。殘糖與此無關：發酵結束時糖已全部用完。","Which product of fermentation is treated as waste?":"發酵的哪一種產物被視為廢棄物？","The fruity-smelling esters":"帶果香的酯類","The congeners the distiller will later select in the still":"蒸餾師之後會在蒸餾器中篩選的同屬物","The CO₂ escapes: the distiller is interested in the alcohol and congeners.":"CO₂ 會散逸：蒸餾師感興趣的是酒精和同屬物。","Ethanol, esters and other congeners are exactly what distillation will select and concentrate. Carbon dioxide, by contrast, leaves the liquid as bubbles and plays no part in the spirit.":"乙醇、酯類和其他同屬物正是蒸餾要篩選並濃縮的東西。二氧化碳則以氣泡的形式離開液體，與烈酒毫無關係。","Besides ethanol, which important alcohols are found in the fermented liquid?":"除了乙醇，發酵液中還有哪些重要的醇類？","Methanol and fusel alcohols":"甲醇和雜醇","Esters and inulin":"酯類和菊糖","None: ethanol is the only alcohol yeast produce":"沒有：乙醇是酵母產生的唯一一種醇","Sugar and starch":"糖和澱粉","Alongside ethanol, by far the main one, there are methanol and fusel alcohols.":"除了占絕大多數的乙醇，還有甲醇和雜醇。","Yeast make many different alcohols, even though ethanol takes up almost all the alcohol volume. Esters are congeners and inulin is an agave carbohydrate. Sugar and starch are not alcohols.":"酵母會製造許多不同的醇，雖然乙醇幾乎占了全部的酒精體積。酯類是同屬物，菊糖是龍舌蘭的碳水化合物。糖和澱粉不是醇。","Where do the congeners in a fermented liquid come from?":"發酵液中的同屬物來自哪裡？","Partly from the raw material, partly from fermentation":"部分來自原料，部分來自發酵","Only from the raw material":"只來自原料","Only from the still, which creates them by heating the liquid":"只來自蒸餾器，由加熱液體而產生","Only from the oak barrel":"只來自橡木桶","Some congeners come straight from the raw material, others are created during fermentation.":"有些同屬物直接來自原料，有些則在發酵過程中產生。","Fruity esters, for instance, are made by yeast. The still invents no aromas: it selects and concentrates those already there. Oak adds further congeners, but only after distillation.":"例如帶果香的酯類就是酵母製造的。蒸餾器不會發明任何香氣：它只篩選並濃縮原有的香氣。橡木會再增添同屬物，但那是蒸餾之後的事。","All Tequilas share earthy, peppery notes. Where do they come from?":"所有 Tequila 都帶有土壤和胡椒氣息。它們來自哪裡？","From the raw material, blue agave":"來自原料藍色龍舌蘭","From the barrels Tequila must legally age in":"來自 Tequila 依法必須陳年的桶","From peat smoke used in cooking":"來自烹煮時使用的泥煤煙","From flavourings added after distillation":"來自蒸餾後添加的調味料","These aromas come with the raw material: an example of how much the ingredient matters.":"這些香氣隨原料而來：這個例子說明了原料有多重要。","A raw material gives two things: carbohydrates and its own set of flavours. Tequila need not be aged, peat concerns malted barley, and no added flavourings are needed for these notes.":"原料提供兩樣東西：碳水化合物和它自己的一組風味。Tequila 不一定要陳年，泥煤與麥芽大麥有關，這些氣息也不需要添加調味料。","Why are some distillers not free to choose their raw material?":"為什麼有些蒸餾師不能自由選擇原料？","Local laws set it for certain styles":"當地法律為某些類型規定了原料","Because selected yeasts work with only one sugar":"因為選育酵母只對一種糖起作用","Because column stills only accept grains":"因為柱式蒸餾器只能處理穀物","Because each country grows only one farm raw material":"因為每個國家只種植一種農業原料","Anyone making a protected style, such as Tequila, must follow its raw-material rules.":"製作受保護類型（例如 Tequila）的人，都必須遵守它的原料規定。","In principle a spirit can be made from any farm product with carbohydrates. The limits come from the law for that type of spirit. Neither yeast nor stills restrict the choice to one raw material.":"原則上，任何含碳水化合物的農產品都能製成烈酒。限制來自該類烈酒的法規。酵母和蒸餾器都不會把選擇限制在單一原料。","Which of these is NOT produced by yeast during fermentation?":"下列哪一項不是酵母在發酵過程中產生的？","Fruity-smelling esters":"帶果香的酯類","Carbon dioxide rising to the surface":"升到表面的二氧化碳","Starch is a starting carbohydrate in some raw materials, not something yeast make.":"澱粉是某些原料中起始的碳水化合物，不是酵母製造的東西。","Yeast consume sugars and produce alcohols, congeners such as esters, and carbon dioxide. Starch, by contrast, must be turned into sugar before fermentation can even start.":"酵母消耗糖，並產生醇類、酯類等同屬物和二氧化碳。澱粉則必須先變成糖，發酵才能開始。","Why is the green malt heated during malting?":"製麥過程中為什麼要加熱綠麥芽？","To stop growth once the enzymes have been made":"在酵素產生後停止生長","To ferment the grains directly":"讓穀粒直接發酵","To destroy the enzymes, which would spoil the sugar":"破壞會損害糖分的酵素","To caramelise the starch and colour the future whisky":"讓澱粉焦糖化，為日後的威士忌上色","After a few days the young plant has done its job: heat kills it and ends malting.":"幾天後幼芽已完成任務：熱把它殺死，製麥就此結束。","The enzymes are needed afterwards, when the ground malted barley is mixed with warm water to turn starch into sugar. Fermentation needs a sugary liquid and yeast, not whole grains. Whisky's colour does not come from this step.":"之後還需要酵素：把磨碎的麥芽大麥與溫水混合時，要靠它們把澱粉轉化為糖。發酵需要的是含糖液體和酵母，不是整粒穀物。威士忌的顏色不是來自這個步驟。","A distillery switches to a different yeast strain. What is most likely?":"一家蒸餾廠換用不同的酵母菌株。最可能發生什麼事？","The new spirit's aromas will change":"新酒的香氣會改變","Nothing, because distillation erases any difference":"什麼都不會變，因為蒸餾會抹去所有差異","Only the spirit's colour will change":"只有烈酒的顏色會改變","Fermentation will no longer exceed 2% abv":"發酵將無法超過 2% abv","Yeast create many congeners: a different strain changes the liquid's aroma profile and so the spirit's.":"酵母會產生許多同屬物：換一種菌株會改變液體的香氣輪廓，烈酒也就跟著改變。","That is exactly why most distillers use reliable, selected yeast. Distillation concentrates what is there; it does not erase differences. The distillate is colourless anyway, and a new yeast does not stop fermentation at such a low level.":"這正是大多數蒸餾師使用可靠的選育酵母的原因。蒸餾會濃縮現有的東西，不會抹去差異。餾出液反正是無色的，新的酵母也不會讓發酵停在這麼低的濃度。","Which statement about raw materials is FALSE?":"關於原料，下列哪一項是錯誤的？","Only grains and grapes may be used":"只能使用穀物和葡萄","They provide food for the yeast":"它們為酵母提供食物","They can give the spirit its own flavours":"它們能賦予烈酒本身的風味","They must be top quality, as flaws get concentrated":"必須品質優良，因為瑕疵會被濃縮","A spirit can be made from any farm product that contains carbohydrates.":"任何含碳水化合物的農產品都能製成烈酒。","The other three statements are true: the raw material feeds the yeast, brings its own aromatic character and must be sound, since distillation amplifies flaws too. Cane, agave, potatoes and fruit are examples beyond grains and grapes.":"其他三項都正確：原料餵養酵母、帶來自己的香氣特色，而且必須完好，因為蒸餾也會放大瑕疵。除了穀物和葡萄，甘蔗、龍舌蘭、馬鈴薯和水果都是例子。","What is the correct order of steps to make wort from barley?":"用大麥製作麥汁，正確的步驟順序是什麼？","Sprouting, heating, grinding, warm water":"發芽、加熱、磨碎、溫水","Grinding, warm water, sprouting, heating":"磨碎、溫水、發芽、加熱","Heating, sprouting, yeast, grinding":"加熱、發芽、酵母、磨碎","Sprouting, yeast, heating, warm water":"發芽、酵母、加熱、溫水","First the barley sprouts and makes enzymes, then heat stops it; next it is ground and mixed with warm water.":"大麥先發芽並產生酵素，接著用熱讓它停止；然後磨碎並與溫水混合。","In the warm water the enzymes turn starch into sugar and wort is formed. Yeast only come in afterwards, once the sweet liquid is ready. Heating before sprouting would prevent the enzymes from forming.":"在溫水中，酵素把澱粉轉化為糖，形成麥汁。酵母要等甜液準備好之後才加入。在發芽前加熱會讓酵素無法形成。","Which of these is a congener?":"下列哪一項是同屬物？","A fruity-smelling ester":"帶果香的酯類","The starch stored in cereal grains":"儲存在穀粒中的澱粉","Congeners are the compounds responsible for aromas and flavours, such as fruity esters.":"同屬物是帶來香氣和風味的化合物，例如帶果香的酯類。","Water is the main component of the fermented liquid but gives no aroma. Carbon dioxide is a waste product that escapes. Starch is a carbohydrate to be converted, not an aroma compound.":"水是發酵液的主要成分，但不帶來香氣。二氧化碳是會散逸的廢棄產物。澱粉是有待轉化的碳水化合物，不是香氣化合物。","Which statement about esters is correct?":"關於酯類，下列哪一項正確？","They are fruity congeners made in fermentation":"它們是發酵中產生的果香同屬物","They are agave's stored carbohydrates":"它們是龍舌蘭儲存的碳水化合物","They come only from the oak barrel":"它們只來自橡木桶","They are the cheesy, plastic-smelling compounds typical of the tails":"它們是酒尾典型的、帶乳酪和塑膠氣味的化合物","Esters are an important group of fruity-smelling congeners formed during fermentation.":"酯類是發酵過程中形成的一類重要的果香同屬物。","Agave's carbohydrate is inulin. Oak brings other aromas such as vanilla and spice. Cheesy, plastic notes belong to the less volatile congeners of the tails.":"龍舌蘭的碳水化合物是菊糖。橡木帶來的是香草和香料等其他香氣。乳酪和塑膠氣息屬於酒尾中較不易揮發的同屬物。","What do grain starch and agave inulin have in common?":"穀物的澱粉和龍舌蘭的菊糖有什麼共同點？","They are complex carbohydrates yeast cannot use directly":"它們是酵母無法直接利用的複雜碳水化合物","They are simple sugars ready to ferment":"它們是可直接發酵的單醣","They are fruity congeners":"它們是果香同屬物","They are alcohols formed while raw materials are cooked":"它們是烹煮原料時形成的醇類","Both are stores of complex carbohydrate that must be turned into sugars before fermentation.":"兩者都是複雜碳水化合物的儲備，發酵前必須先變成糖。","Starch needs enzymes (malted barley or bought-in enzymes), inulin needs the piña cooked. They are neither ready sugars, congeners nor alcohols: alcohol only appears with yeast.":"澱粉需要酵素（麥芽大麥或外購酵素），菊糖需要烹煮 piña。它們既不是現成的糖，也不是同屬物或醇：酒精要有酵母才會出現。","What do yeast feed on during alcoholic fermentation?":"酒精發酵過程中，酵母以什麼為食？","Unconverted starch, with no processing needed":"未經轉化的澱粉，不需任何處理","Yeast consume the sugars in the liquid and produce alcohols, congeners and carbon dioxide.":"酵母消耗液體中的糖，並產生醇類、同屬物和二氧化碳。","Ethanol and carbon dioxide are what yeast produce, not what they eat. Starch must first become sugar, which is why grains and potatoes need enzymes.":"乙醇和二氧化碳是酵母的產物，不是它們的食物。澱粉必須先變成糖，所以穀物和馬鈴薯才需要酵素。","Why does a spirit need distillation if fermentation already makes alcohol?":"既然發酵已經產生酒精，為什麼烈酒還需要蒸餾？","Fermentation only reaches about 8–10% abv":"發酵只能達到大約 8–10% abv","Fermentation only makes methanol":"發酵只會產生甲醇","Distillation is mainly there to add colour":"蒸餾主要是為了上色","Fermentation already gives 75% abv, but the liquid is cloudy and only needs clearing":"發酵已經能達到 75% abv，只是液體混濁，需要澄清而已","The fermented liquid is around 8–10% abv; distillation concentrates the ethanol and selects the congeners.":"發酵液大約是 8–10% abv；蒸餾會濃縮乙醇並篩選同屬物。","Ethanol, not methanol, is by far the main alcohol of fermentation. Newly made spirit is colourless. A level like 75% is only reached by distillation.":"發酵產生的醇以乙醇占絕大多數，不是甲醇。新酒是無色的。75% 這樣的濃度只有靠蒸餾才能達到。","Do most distillers grow their own raw material?":"大多數蒸餾師自己種植原料嗎？","No: most buy it in":"不：大多數是買進的","Yes, the law requires it everywhere":"是的，各地法律都這樣規定","Yes, all except vodka producers":"是的，除了伏特加生產者以外都是","No: they only ever buy finished spirit from others":"不：他們一律只向別人購買成品烈酒","Only a very few grow their raw material, such as some small Cognac distillers; most buy it in.":"只有極少數人自己種植原料，例如 Cognac 的一些小型蒸餾師；大多數是買進的。","There is no general obligation to grow your own. Those who start from a raw material ferment and distil it; others buy in spirit, but that is not the rule for everyone.":"沒有必須自己種植的普遍規定。從原料開始做的人會自行發酵和蒸餾；也有人買進烈酒，但這並不是所有人的做法。","A brandy distiller uses grape juice. Must any carbohydrates be converted before fermenting?":"一位白蘭地蒸餾師使用葡萄汁。發酵前需要轉化碳水化合物嗎？","No: grape juice already holds fermentable sugars":"不需要：葡萄汁本來就含有可發酵的糖","Yes, it must be malted like barley":"需要，必須像大麥一樣製麥","Yes, it must be cooked like an agave piña":"需要，必須像龍舌蘭的 piña 一樣烹煮","Yes, bought-in enzymes are needed as grapes are mostly starch":"需要，因為葡萄主要是澱粉，要用外購酵素","Grapes store their carbohydrate as sugars, so fermentation can begin straight away.":"葡萄以糖的形式儲存碳水化合物，所以可以立刻開始發酵。","Malting, cooking and enzymes are for starch and inulin, meaning grains, potatoes and agave. Grapes contain no starch to convert.":"製麥、烹煮和酵素是用來處理澱粉和菊糖的，也就是穀物、馬鈴薯和龍舌蘭。葡萄不含需要轉化的澱粉。","Which of these is NOT one of the four key production stages?":"下列哪一項不屬於四個主要生產階段？","Ageing in the bottle":"瓶中陳年","Selecting and processing the raw material":"挑選和處理原料","The four stages are raw material, fermentation, distillation and post-distillation operations.":"四個階段是原料、發酵、蒸餾和蒸餾後處理。","Bottle ageing is not part of this framework: maturation, when there is any, takes place in barrels or inert vessels, among the post-distillation operations.":"瓶中陳年不在這個架構內：如果有熟成，是在桶中或惰性容器中進行，屬於蒸餾後處理。","At which of the four stages does the distiller make choices that shape style and quality?":"蒸餾師在四個階段中的哪一個做出影響風格和品質的選擇？","At all four":"四個階段都有","Only at distillation":"只在蒸餾時","Only after distillation":"只在蒸餾之後","Only in choosing the raw material, since the rest is set by law":"只在選擇原料時，因為其他都由法律規定","At every stage, from raw material to finishing, the distiller has choices to make.":"從原料到收尾處理，每個階段蒸餾師都有選擇要做。","The laws for some spirits can limit these choices but do not remove them. Yeast, cuts, barrels and blending are all examples of decisions that change the result.":"某些烈酒的法規會限制這些選擇，但不會讓選擇消失。酵母、切取、桶和調和，都是會改變結果的決定。","What is the liquid mostly made of at the end of fermentation?":"發酵結束時，液體主要由什麼組成？","Water and alcohols":"水和醇類","Almost pure ethanol":"幾乎純的乙醇","Esters and other congeners, with very little water":"酯類和其他同屬物，水很少","The fermented liquid is mostly water and alcohols, chiefly ethanol.":"發酵液主要是水和醇類，其中以乙醇為主。","By the end of fermentation the sugar is used up. At 8–10% abv the ethanol is far from pure. Congeners matter hugely for aroma but are a small part of the volume.":"發酵結束時糖已經用完。8–10% abv 的乙醇離純還很遠。同屬物對香氣極為重要，但只占體積的一小部分。","Which of these could NOT be the raw material for a spirit?":"下列哪一項不可能作為烈酒的原料？","Sea salt":"海鹽","Rice":"米","Dates, rich in natural sugars":"富含天然糖分的椰棗","A spirit needs a farm product containing carbohydrates; salt is neither agricultural nor a source of sugar.":"烈酒需要含碳水化合物的農產品；鹽既不是農產品，也不是糖的來源。","Potatoes and rice hold starch to convert, dates ready sugars: all could in principle become a spirit. Without carbohydrates, yeast would have nothing to turn into alcohol.":"馬鈴薯和米含有待轉化的澱粉，椰棗含有現成的糖：原則上都能製成烈酒。沒有碳水化合物，酵母就沒有東西可以轉化為酒精。","Malting barley, cooking agave and pressing fruit: which stage do these belong to?":"大麥製麥、烹煮龍舌蘭、壓榨水果：這些屬於哪個階段？","Post-distillation operations, before bottling":"裝瓶前的蒸餾後處理","These are all ways of getting a sugary liquid to ferment from the raw material.":"這些都是從原料得到可發酵含糖液體的方法。","Fermentation only starts afterwards, when yeast is added to the sugary liquid. Distillation and later steps work on an already alcoholic liquid.":"發酵要到之後才開始，也就是在含糖液體中加入酵母時。蒸餾和之後的步驟處理的是已含酒精的液體。","One litre of fermented liquid at 10% abv: how much alcohol does it contain?":"一公升 10% abv 的發酵液含有多少酒精？","About 100 ml":"大約 100 ml","About 10 ml":"大約 10 ml","About 200 ml, since it is counted in proof":"大約 200 ml，因為是用 proof 計算","About 10 grams of unconverted sugar":"大約 10 公克未轉化的糖","10% of the volume is alcohol: in 1,000 ml that is about 100 ml.":"體積的 10% 是酒精：1,000 ml 中大約有 100 ml。","abv is a percentage of volume, not a weight or a sugar measure. Proof is another way of writing it (10% abv = 20 proof), but it does not change the real amount of alcohol.":"abv 是體積百分比，不是重量，也不是糖的度量。proof 是另一種寫法（10% abv = 20 proof），但不會改變實際的酒精量。","From about 10% after fermentation to about 75% after distillation: roughly how much is the ethanol concentrated?":"從發酵後約 10% 到蒸餾後約 75%：乙醇大約被濃縮了多少倍？","About seven and a half times":"大約七倍半","About twice":"大約兩倍","About a hundred times":"大約一百倍","It is not concentrated: only the liquid's colour changes":"沒有濃縮：只有液體的顏色改變","Going from 10% to 75% means concentrating the ethanol about 7.5 times.":"從 10% 到 75% 表示乙醇被濃縮了大約 7.5 倍。","This concentrating effect also applies to the congeners kept, and to any flaws in the raw material, which is why sound ingredients matter. Newly made spirit stays colourless.":"這種濃縮效果也適用於保留下來的同屬物，以及原料的任何瑕疵，所以完好的原料很重要。新酒仍然是無色的。","To select and concentrate parts of the liquid":"篩選並濃縮液體中的某些部分","To turn sugar into alcohol using heat":"用熱把糖變成酒精","To give colour and sweetness to the fermented liquid before sale":"在上市前為發酵液增添顏色和甜味","To remove all the alcohol except water":"去除所有酒精，只留下水","Distillation picks out certain parts, mainly ethanol and wanted congeners, and leaves others behind.":"蒸餾挑出某些部分，主要是乙醇和想要的同屬物，並把其他部分留下。","Sugar becomes alcohol during fermentation, not in the still. A newly made spirit is colourless and dry: colour and sweetness only come later. Water is precisely the part that is largely discarded.":"糖是在發酵時變成酒精的，不是在蒸餾器中。新酒無色且不甜：顏色和甜味都是之後才有的。水正是大部分被捨棄的部分。","Why is the vapour from a boiling fermented liquid more alcoholic than the liquid?":"為什麼發酵液沸騰時的蒸氣比液體本身含更多酒精？","Ethanol boils at a lower temperature than water":"乙醇的沸點比水低","Water boils at a lower temperature than ethanol":"水的沸點比乙醇低","The copper in the still turns water into alcohol":"蒸餾器的銅把水變成酒精","The yeast keeps fermenting inside the hot still":"酵母在高溫的蒸餾器裡繼續發酵","Ethanol is more volatile, so a larger share of it goes into the vapour.":"乙醇更容易揮發，所以有更大比例進入蒸氣。","Pure ethanol boils at about 78 °C and water at 100 °C: that difference is what makes separation possible. Copper does not create alcohol, and yeast does not survive boiling.":"純乙醇大約在 78 °C 沸騰，水在 100 °C：這個差異讓分離成為可能。銅不會產生酒精，酵母也無法在沸騰中存活。","What are the individual parts of a liquid to be distilled called?":"待蒸餾液體中的各個組成部分叫做什麼？","Fractions":"餾分","Cuts":"切取點","Plates":"蒸餾板","Low wines":"低度酒","Each component with its own boiling point is called a fraction.":"每個有自己沸點的成分稱為一個餾分。","A cut is the moment the flow is redirected. Plates are parts of a column still. Low wines are the liquid from the first pot-still distillation.":"切取點是把酒液流向改道的時刻。蒸餾板是柱式蒸餾器的零件。低度酒是壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾得到的液體。","At roughly what temperature does pure ethanol boil?":"純乙醇大約在幾度沸騰？","Pure ethanol boils at about 78 °C, below water.":"純乙醇大約在 78 °C 沸騰，低於水。","100 °C is the boiling point of water. It is precisely because ethanol boils lower that the vapour becomes richer in alcohol. The other temperatures match neither substance.":"100 °C 是水的沸點。正因為乙醇的沸點較低，蒸氣中的酒精才會變多。其他溫度與這兩種物質都不相符。","Which statement about newly made spirits is true?":"關於新酒，下列哪一項正確？","They are colourless and dry":"無色且不甜","They are golden and slightly sweet":"金黃色且略帶甜味","They already have their bottled colour, but are dry":"已有裝瓶時的顏色，但不甜","They are colourless but hold residual sugar from the fruit":"無色，但含有來自水果的殘糖","Every spirit leaves the still clear as water and without sugar.":"所有烈酒離開蒸餾器時都像水一樣清澈，而且不含糖。","Sugar is not volatile and does not pass into the vapour, so it stays in the still. Colour comes from oak or from colouring added after distillation. Even fruit spirits therefore come off dry.":"糖不具揮發性，不會進入蒸氣，所以留在蒸餾器中。顏色來自橡木或蒸餾後添加的色素。因此就連水果烈酒蒸餾出來時也是不甜的。","Which part of the distillate has a marked solvent smell?":"餾出液的哪個部分帶有明顯的溶劑氣味？","The heads":"酒頭","The heart":"酒心","The tails":"酒尾","The liquid waste":"廢液","The heads hold the most volatile, solvent-smelling compounds.":"酒頭含有最易揮發、帶溶劑氣味的化合物。","The heads come off first precisely because they boil before ethanol. The tails, which come last, smell more of cheese and plastic. The heart carries ethanol and pleasant aromas, while the waste is mostly water.":"酒頭最先流出，正是因為它們比乙醇更早沸騰。最後流出的酒尾聞起來比較像乳酪和塑膠。酒心帶有乙醇和宜人的香氣，廢液則大部分是水。","Which part of the distillate becomes the spirit that is sold?":"餾出液的哪個部分會成為販售的烈酒？","The heads, because they are the most alcoholic":"酒頭，因為酒精濃度最高","The tails, because they have more aroma":"酒尾，因為香氣更多","The liquid left at the bottom of the still":"留在蒸餾器底部的液體","The heart holds the ethanol and the congeners that give the wanted character.":"酒心含有乙醇，以及帶來所需特色的同屬物。","Heads and tails contain too many unpleasant compounds, solvent-like and cheesy or plastic respectively. The liquid at the bottom is mostly water and is thrown away.":"酒頭和酒尾含有太多令人不悅的化合物，分別帶溶劑味以及乳酪或塑膠味。底部的液體大部分是水，會被丟棄。","Which aromas signal that the tails are arriving?":"哪些香氣代表酒尾即將出現？","Cheesy and plastic notes":"乳酪和塑膠氣息","Very sharp solvent and nail-varnish notes":"非常刺鼻的溶劑和指甲油氣息","Fresh, fruity ester notes":"清新的果香酯類氣息","Tails bring less volatile compounds that smell cheesy and plastic.":"酒尾帶來較不易揮發、聞起來像乳酪和塑膠的化合物。","A solvent smell is typical of the heads, at the start. Fruity esters are among the welcome aromas of the heart. Vanilla and coconut come from oak, so after distillation.":"溶劑氣味是開頭的酒頭的典型特徵。帶果香的酯類是酒心中受歡迎的香氣之一。香草和椰子來自橡木，所以是蒸餾之後才有的。","In what order do the parts of the distillate come off the still?":"餾出液的各個部分依什麼順序流出蒸餾器？","Heads, heart, tails":"酒頭、酒心、酒尾","Heart, heads, tails":"酒心、酒頭、酒尾","Tails, heart, heads":"酒尾、酒心、酒頭","Heads, tails, heart":"酒頭、酒尾、酒心","The most volatile compounds come first, then ethanol, then the least volatile.":"最易揮發的化合物最先出來，然後是乙醇，最後是最不易揮發的。","The order follows boiling points: heads boil before ethanol, the heart centres on ethanol, and tails boil after. Water, the least volatile, remains mostly as waste.":"順序依沸點而定：酒頭比乙醇先沸騰，酒心以乙醇為中心，酒尾則在之後沸騰。最不易揮發的水大部分留下來成為廢液。","What is left as liquid waste at the end of distillation?":"蒸餾結束時，留下來的廢液是什麼？","Mostly water":"大部分是水","Mostly ethanol":"大部分是乙醇","Mostly solvent-smelling compounds":"大部分是帶溶劑氣味的化合物","Mostly fruity esters":"大部分是帶果香的酯類","Water is the least volatile fraction and stays behind as waste.":"水是最不易揮發的餾分，會留下來成為廢液。","Ethanol and esters belong to the heart and are collected. Solvent-like compounds are very volatile and come off first, in the heads. The watery liquid left over is discarded.":"乙醇和酯類屬於酒心，會被收集起來。帶溶劑味的化合物非常容易揮發，最先在酒頭中流出。剩下的含水液體會被丟棄。","What happens to the aromas when a spirit is distilled to a higher strength?":"把烈酒蒸餾到更高濃度時，香氣會怎麼樣？","They decrease":"減少","They increase":"增加","They stay the same; only the alcohol changes":"保持不變；只有酒精改變","They become more woody and spicy":"變得更有木質和香料氣息","The more ethanol is concentrated, the more congeners are left behind.":"乙醇濃縮得越多，留下不取的同屬物就越多。","This is the golden rule: high strength means little aroma, right up to neutral spirit. Woody and spicy aromas come from oak maturation, not distillation. The amount of congeners changes along with the strength.":"這是黃金法則：濃度高就代表香氣少，一直到中性烈酒為止。木質和香料香氣來自橡木桶熟成，不是蒸餾。同屬物的量會隨濃度一起改變。","A spirit was collected at around 75% abv. What aroma intensity would you expect?":"一款烈酒在大約 75% abv 時收集。你預期它的香氣強度如何？","Medium or pronounced":"中等或明顯","Neutral, almost odourless":"中性，幾乎沒有氣味","Light, like a Scottish grain whisky":"清淡，像蘇格蘭穀物威士忌","Impossible to say without ageing":"沒有陳年就無法判斷","At about 75% abv many congeners remain: aroma is medium or pronounced.":"在大約 75% abv 時仍保留許多同屬物：香氣中等或明顯。","Aroma only becomes light at around 90% abv, as in Scottish grain whisky, and neutral at 95–96%. Distillation strength already predicts intensity, before any ageing.":"香氣要到大約 90% abv 才變得清淡，例如蘇格蘭穀物威士忌；到 95–96% 則成為中性。蒸餾濃度在任何陳年之前就已經能預測香氣強度。","What is a spirit distilled to about 95–96% abv, with very few congeners, called?":"蒸餾到大約 95–96% abv、同屬物極少的烈酒叫做什麼？","Pronounced heart spirit":"香氣明顯的酒心烈酒","Rancio spirit":"Rancio 烈酒","At this strength the aroma is neutral, hence the name neutral spirit.":"在這個濃度下香氣是中性的，因此稱為中性烈酒。","Low wines are weak, around 25–30% abv, and come from the first pot-still distillation. 'Rancio' describes leather and mushroom notes from long oak ageing, not a strength.":"低度酒濃度低，大約 25–30% abv，來自壺式蒸餾器的第一次蒸餾。「rancio」描述的是長期橡木桶陳年帶來的皮革和蘑菇氣息，不是濃度。","A producer wants a spirit that strongly expresses its raw material. What should be avoided?":"一位生產者想要一款強烈表現原料特色的烈酒。應該避免什麼？","Distilling to a very high strength":"蒸餾到非常高的濃度","Collecting the heart at around 75% abv":"在大約 75% abv 時收集酒心","Separating the heads from the rest of the spirit at the start":"在一開始把酒頭與其餘的酒液分開","Using top-quality raw material":"使用頂級品質的原料","A very high strength strips out most raw-material congeners.":"非常高的濃度會去除大部分來自原料的同屬物。","Collecting at about 75% keeps plenty of aroma, which is exactly what is wanted. Removing the heads only takes out solvent-like compounds, and excellent raw material always helps. The danger is pushing towards neutral spirit.":"在大約 75% 收集能保留豐富的香氣，這正是所需要的。去除酒頭只會帶走溶劑味的化合物，優良的原料也總是有幫助。危險在於把濃度推向中性烈酒。","What is a common level of ethanol concentration reached by distillation?":"蒸餾常見的乙醇濃縮幅度是多少？","From about 10% to about 75% abv":"從大約 10% 到大約 75% abv","From about 40% to about 100% abv":"從大約 40% 到大約 100% abv","From about 1% to about 10% abv":"從大約 1% 到大約 10% abv","From about 10% to about 40% abv, ready for bottling":"從大約 10% 到大約 40% abv，可直接裝瓶","A typical step takes the fermented liquid from about 10% to about 75% abv.":"典型的做法是把發酵液從大約 10% 提高到大約 75% abv。","Some spirits stay below 75%, others reach 96%, but never 100%. The starting liquid is not at 40%: it is around 10%. 40% is often the selling strength, reached by adding water after distillation.":"有些烈酒低於 75%，有些達到 96%，但絕不會到 100%。起始液體不是 40%，而是 10% 左右。40% 通常是販售濃度，是蒸餾後加水達到的。","Why does a spirit collected at around 90% abv have a light aroma?":"為什麼在大約 90% abv 收集的烈酒香氣清淡？","Many congeners have been left behind":"許多同屬物被留下不取","The high strength destroys aromas through the heat of the still":"高濃度透過蒸餾器的熱破壞了香氣","It still contains a lot of heads":"它仍含有大量酒頭","It was filtered through oak":"它經過橡木過濾","As strength rises, more and more congeners stay behind, so aromas fade.":"隨著濃度升高，越來越多同屬物被留下，所以香氣變淡。","It is not heat that destroys aromas: it is separation, which leaves congeners behind. Heads would give a solvent smell, not a light aroma. Oak adds aromas rather than removing them.":"破壞香氣的不是熱，而是分離：它把同屬物留了下來。酒頭會帶來溶劑氣味，而不是清淡的香氣。橡木是增添香氣，而不是去除香氣。","Which of these spirits is typically made from neutral spirit?":"下列哪一種烈酒通常以中性烈酒製成？","Vodka is based on neutral spirit, with very few congeners.":"伏特加以中性烈酒為基礎，同屬物極少。","Bourbon, Armagnac and rhum agricole are distilled to lower strengths, even in columns, and keep a medium or pronounced aroma. This shows that the strength reached matters most.":"Bourbon、Armagnac 和 rhum agricole 蒸餾到較低的濃度（即使使用蒸餾柱），並保有中等或明顯的香氣。這說明了最重要的是達到的濃度。","Besides how much alcohol to concentrate, what does the distiller decide?":"除了要把酒精濃縮到多少，蒸餾師還要決定什麼？","Which congeners to keep in the spirit":"在烈酒中保留哪些同屬物","How much sugar to leave in the newly made spirit":"在新酒中留下多少糖","What colour to give the spirit during distillation":"蒸餾時要給烈酒什麼顏色","How much yeast to add to the still":"要在蒸餾器中加入多少酵母","Distillation is also about choosing the aromas that will give character.":"蒸餾也是在挑選能帶來特色的香氣。","A newly made spirit is always dry and colourless, so sugar and colour are not decided in the still. Yeast works during fermentation, before distillation.":"新酒一定是不甜且無色的，所以糖和顏色不是在蒸餾器中決定的。酵母在蒸餾之前的發酵階段發揮作用。","Which group of fractions makes up the heart of the distillate?":"哪一組餾分構成餾出液的酒心？","Ethanol and congeners with a similar boiling point":"乙醇和沸點相近的同屬物","Congeners that boil before ethanol":"比乙醇先沸騰的同屬物","Congeners that boil after ethanol, along with some water":"比乙醇晚沸騰的同屬物，加上一些水","Water alone, stripped of all aroma":"只有水，不含任何香氣","The heart brings together ethanol and aromas boiling at similar temperatures.":"酒心匯集了乙醇和在相近溫度沸騰的香氣。","Congeners that boil earlier form the heads; those that boil later form the tails. Water is the waste. It is precisely the congeners close to ethanol that give the spirit its personality.":"較早沸騰的同屬物形成酒頭；較晚沸騰的形成酒尾。水是廢液。賦予烈酒個性的，正是那些接近乙醇的同屬物。","What happens to the vapour when it reaches the condenser?":"蒸氣到達冷凝器時會怎麼樣？","It cools and turns back into liquid":"冷卻並變回液體","It heats further and becomes more alcoholic":"進一步加熱，酒精濃度變得更高","It ferments again thanks to the yeast":"靠酵母再次發酵","It turns into sugar, which is then discarded":"變成糖，然後被丟棄","The condenser cools the vapour and turns it back into liquid.":"冷凝器冷卻蒸氣，把它變回液體。","Distilling means heating, letting the vapour rise and then condensing it: the resulting liquid is stronger than the original. There is no fermentation or sugar formation in the condenser.":"蒸餾就是加熱、讓蒸氣上升，再把它冷凝：得到的液體比原本的濃度更高。冷凝器中不會發酵，也不會形成糖。","A spirit smells too strongly of cheese. What has probably happened?":"一款烈酒的乳酪味太重。可能發生了什麼事？","Too much of the tails got into the heart":"太多酒尾進入了酒心","Too much of the heads got into the heart":"太多酒頭進入了酒心","It was distilled too high, close to neutral spirit":"蒸餾濃度太高，接近中性烈酒","Fermentation produced too many esters":"發酵產生了太多酯類","Cheesy notes are typical of the tails: the second cut came too late.":"乳酪氣息是酒尾的典型特徵：第二次切取做得太晚。","Too much heads would give a solvent smell. A very high strength would make the spirit nearly neutral, not more marked. Esters smell fruity. In small amounts these aromas can be part of the character; in excess they are faults.":"酒頭太多會帶來溶劑氣味。非常高的濃度會讓烈酒近乎中性，而不是特徵更鮮明。酯類聞起來是果香。這些香氣少量時可以是特色的一部分；過量就是缺陷。","An aged brandy has a lovely amber colour. Where does this colour come from?":"一款陳年白蘭地有漂亮的琥珀色。這個顏色來自哪裡？","From steps after distillation, such as oak":"來自蒸餾後的步驟，例如橡木桶","From grape skins, which colour the spirit in the still":"來自葡萄皮，在蒸餾器中為烈酒上色","From the tails, which are naturally dark":"來自酒尾，它們天生顏色深","From distilling to a very high strength":"來自蒸餾到非常高的濃度","Every spirit comes off colourless: colour comes later, from oak or colouring.":"所有烈酒蒸餾出來都是無色的：顏色是之後才有的，來自橡木或色素。","Skin pigments are not volatile and do not pass into the vapour, so the spirit stays clear as water. Tails and strength affect aroma, not colour. The same goes for sweetness, which a newly made spirit does not have.":"果皮的色素不具揮發性，不會進入蒸氣，所以烈酒像水一樣清澈。酒尾和濃度影響的是香氣，不是顏色。甜味也是一樣，新酒並沒有甜味。","Between water and ethanol, which is less volatile?":"水和乙醇，哪一個較不易揮發？","They are exactly as volatile as each other":"兩者的揮發性完全相同","It depends on the type of still used":"取決於使用的蒸餾器類型","Water boils at 100 °C and ethanol at about 78 °C, so water is less volatile.":"水在 100 °C 沸騰，乙醇大約在 78 °C，所以水較不易揮發。","Being more volatile means evaporating more easily, at a lower temperature. This difference is what makes distillation possible. Volatility belongs to the substance, not the still.":"更易揮發的意思是更容易蒸發，溫度更低就能蒸發。這個差異讓蒸餾成為可能。揮發性是物質本身的性質，與蒸餾器無關。","At what temperature does pure water boil?":"純水在幾度沸騰？","Water boils at 100 °C, higher than ethanol (about 78 °C).":"水在 100 °C 沸騰，高於乙醇（約 78 °C）。","78 °C is the boiling point of pure ethanol. Because ethanol boils first, the vapours from a boiling alcoholic liquid are richer in alcohol than the liquid itself.":"78 °C 是純乙醇的沸點。因為乙醇先沸騰，含酒精液體沸騰時的蒸氣比液體本身含更多酒精。","When a 10% abv liquid starts to boil, roughly what strength are the first vapours?":"10% abv 的液體開始沸騰時，最初的蒸氣大約是多少濃度？","About 50% abv":"大約 50% abv","About 10% abv, like the liquid":"大約 10% abv，和液體一樣","About 96% abv":"大約 96% abv","Under 5% abv, because water evaporates first":"低於 5% abv，因為水先蒸發","Ethanol, being more volatile, concentrates in the vapour: a 10% liquid gives vapours of about 50%.":"乙醇較易揮發，會在蒸氣中濃縮：10% 的液體產生約 50% 的蒸氣。","The vapours are always more alcoholic than the boiling liquid, so they do not stay at 10%. 96% is only reached with many distillations in a column. Water is less volatile than ethanol, so it does not evaporate first.":"蒸氣的酒精濃度總是比沸騰的液體高，所以不會停在 10%。96% 只有在蒸餾柱中經過多次蒸餾才能達到。水比乙醇不易揮發，所以不會先蒸發。","Which sequence describes any distillation?":"哪一組順序可以描述任何蒸餾？","Heat, condense the vapours, collect the liquid":"加熱、冷凝蒸氣、收集液體","Cool, filter, heat":"冷卻、過濾、加熱","Condense the liquid, then boil it in the condenser":"冷凝液體，再在冷凝器中煮沸","Add yeast, heat, bottle straight away":"加酵母、加熱、立刻裝瓶","The alcoholic liquid is heated into vapour, which is condensed and collected as a new liquid.":"含酒精的液體被加熱成蒸氣，蒸氣經冷凝後收集成新的液體。","The condenser cools vapours; it does not boil anything. Yeast belong to fermentation, which comes first. Filtration is a finishing step after distillation.":"冷凝器是冷卻蒸氣的，不會煮沸任何東西。酵母屬於先進行的發酵階段。過濾是蒸餾後的收尾步驟。","The heads are mainly congeners with a boiling point…":"酒頭主要是沸點……的同屬物","lower than ethanol's":"比乙醇低","higher than ethanol's":"比乙醇高","the same as water's":"和水相同","similar to ethanol's, like the best aromas in the heart":"與乙醇相近，就像酒心中最好的香氣","The heads are the most volatile compounds: they boil before ethanol and arrive first.":"酒頭是最易揮發的化合物：它們比乙醇先沸騰，最先出現。","Congeners with higher boiling points make up the tails. Those close to ethanol go into the heart, and water mostly stays behind as liquid waste.":"沸點較高的同屬物構成酒尾。接近乙醇的進入酒心，水則大部分留下來成為廢液。","The tails are mainly made up of congeners…":"酒尾主要由……的同屬物組成","less volatile than ethanol":"比乙醇不易揮發","more volatile than ethanol, smelling of solvent":"比乙醇更易揮發、帶溶劑氣味","created by the heat of the still":"由蒸餾器的熱所產生","that boil at the same temperature as ethanol":"與乙醇在相同溫度沸騰","The tails come last because their congeners have higher boiling points.":"酒尾最後才出現，因為其中的同屬物沸點較高。","Once ethanol and its similar congeners run low in the liquid, the less volatile compounds start to concentrate in the vapour: cheesy and plastic notes. Solvent-smelling compounds are the heads. The still does not create congeners; it selects them.":"當液體中的乙醇和相近的同屬物變少，較不易揮發的化合物就開始在蒸氣中濃縮：乳酪和塑膠氣息。帶溶劑氣味的化合物是酒頭。蒸餾器不會創造同屬物，只會篩選。","Why do the heads come off the condenser first?":"為什麼酒頭最先從冷凝器流出？","The most volatile parts concentrate in the vapours first":"最易揮發的部分最先在蒸氣中濃縮","They are the heaviest parts and drop straight down":"它們是最重的部分，直接往下掉","The distiller adds them at the start to clean the still":"蒸餾師在一開始加入它們來清潔蒸餾器","They form in the condenser while the cooling water is still warm":"它們在冷卻水還溫熱時於冷凝器中形成","The principle is always the same: whatever is most volatile passes into the vapour first.":"原理始終相同：最易揮發的東西最先進入蒸氣。","The heads are compounds already in the liquid, neither added by the distiller nor formed in the condenser. Weight is irrelevant; boiling point is what counts.":"酒頭是液體中原本就有的化合物，既不是蒸餾師加入的，也不是在冷凝器中形成的。重量無關緊要；重要的是沸點。","Why is the heads phase short, only around ten minutes?":"為什麼酒頭階段很短，只有十分鐘左右？","Those congeners run out of the liquid very quickly":"這些同屬物很快就從液體中耗盡","The distiller turns off the heat to avoid them":"蒸餾師關掉熱源來避開它們","The condenser holds almost all of them back":"冷凝器把它們幾乎全部擋住","They turn into ethanol after a few minutes of boiling in the liquid":"它們在液體中沸騰幾分鐘後變成乙醇","The most volatile compounds are few and pass quickly into the vapour, so their level in the liquid drops fast.":"最易揮發的化合物數量少，很快就進入蒸氣，所以它們在液體中的含量迅速下降。","Once the solvent smell no longer dominates, the distiller makes the cut and the heart begins. Heating continues, the condenser lets everything through and no congener turns into ethanol.":"一旦溶劑氣味不再是主導，蒸餾師就進行切取，酒心開始。加熱持續進行，冷凝器讓所有東西通過，也沒有任何同屬物會變成乙醇。","What do the choices about what to keep and what to reject depend on?":"保留什麼、捨棄什麼，取決於什麼？","The distiller's preferences and the type of spirit":"蒸餾師的偏好和烈酒的類型","Only on the yeast used in fermentation":"只取決於發酵所用的酵母","A fixed rule that is the same for every spirit":"一條對所有烈酒都相同的固定規則","The outside temperature":"室外氣溫","Where the cuts fall depends on the style sought and the distiller's preferences.":"切取點落在哪裡，取決於追求的風格和蒸餾師的偏好。","There is no single rule: one distiller may want a wider, richer heart, another a cleaner, lighter one. Yeast affects which congeners exist but does not decide the cuts. Climate does not decide what to keep.":"沒有單一的規則：有的蒸餾師想要較寬、較豐富的酒心，有的想要較乾淨、較清淡的。酵母影響的是有哪些同屬物，但不決定切取點。氣候不會決定要保留什麼。","What is the highest strength distillation can reach?":"蒸餾能達到的最高濃度是多少？","About 75% abv":"大約 75% abv","100% abv, pure alcohol":"100% abv，純酒精","About 86% abv":"大約 86% abv","With enough plates a column reaches 95–96% abv, the level of neutral spirit.":"只要蒸餾板夠多，蒸餾柱可達 95–96% abv，也就是中性烈酒的濃度。","75% is a common level, not the maximum. 100% is not reached by distillation. 96% is only possible in a column, never in a pot still.":"75% 是常見的濃度，不是上限。蒸餾無法達到 100%。96% 只有蒸餾柱才能做到，壺式蒸餾器絕對不行。","Two spirits come from the same fermented liquid: A collected at 70% abv, B at 94%. Which will have more aroma?":"兩款烈酒來自同一批發酵液：A 在 70% abv 收集，B 在 94%。哪一款香氣較多？","A, because it keeps more congeners":"A，因為保留了更多同屬物","B, because stronger alcohol carries more aroma":"B，因為酒精越濃，帶的香氣越多","Neither: they will smell the same as the starting liquid is the same":"都不是：起始液體相同，聞起來也會一樣","B, because it has lost more water":"B，因為失去了更多水","The higher the distillation strength, the more congeners are left behind and the less aroma the spirit has.":"蒸餾濃度越高，留下不取的同屬物越多，烈酒的香氣就越少。","The starting liquid is the same, but distillation selects different parts of it. Approaching 95–96%, the aroma becomes almost neutral. Losing water concentrates the ethanol, not the aromas.":"起始液體相同，但蒸餾篩選了其中不同的部分。接近 95–96% 時，香氣幾乎變成中性。失去水分濃縮的是乙醇，不是香氣。","Why can a neutral spirit not express its raw material?":"為什麼中性烈酒無法表現它的原料？","Nearly all congeners have been left behind":"幾乎所有同屬物都被留下不取","Because it is always made from potatoes":"因為它一定是用馬鈴薯做的","Because it is aged for a long time in inert glass vessels":"因為它在惰性的玻璃容器中長期陳年","Because it is distilled without fermentation":"因為它不經發酵就蒸餾","At 95–96% abv so few congeners remain that the aroma is neutral, whatever the raw material.":"在 95–96% abv 時留下的同屬物極少，不論用什麼原料，香氣都是中性的。","Neutral spirit can be made from any raw material, not just potatoes. Inert vessels remove no aroma. Without fermentation there would be no alcohol to distil.":"中性烈酒可以用任何原料製成，不只是馬鈴薯。惰性容器不會去除香氣。沒有發酵就沒有酒精可以蒸餾。","Which of these does distillation NOT do?":"下列哪一項不是蒸餾的作用？","Make the spirit sweet":"讓烈酒變甜","Concentrate the ethanol":"濃縮乙醇","Select some congeners and reject others":"篩選某些同屬物並捨棄其他的","Leave much of the fermented liquid's water behind":"把發酵液中大部分的水留下","Every newly made spirit is dry: any sugar is added later.":"所有新酒都是不甜的：如果有糖，都是之後才加的。","Concentrating ethanol, choosing congeners and separating water are exactly what distillation does. Sweetness is a finishing choice, sometimes compulsory, as for liqueurs.":"濃縮乙醇、挑選同屬物和分離水分，正是蒸餾的作用。甜味是收尾階段的選擇，有時是強制規定，例如利口酒。","A customer asks why their rum tastes sweet if distillation makes dry spirits. What do you answer?":"一位顧客問：既然蒸餾得到的是不甜的烈酒，為什麼他的蘭姆酒喝起來是甜的？你怎麼回答？","Sugar can be added after distillation":"蒸餾後可以加糖","The cane sugar passes intact into the vapour":"甘蔗的糖原封不動地進入蒸氣","Rums are not distilled, only fermented":"蘭姆酒沒有蒸餾，只有發酵","The tails contain sugar and are left in the heart":"酒尾含有糖，並被留在酒心裡","All newly made spirits are dry; some rums are sweetened during finishing for balance and style.":"所有新酒都是不甜的；有些蘭姆酒在收尾階段為了平衡和風格而加糖。","Sugar does not pass into the vapour: it stays behind or has already been eaten by the yeast. Rum is a true distilled spirit. Tails give cheesy, plastic notes, not sweetness.":"糖不會進入蒸氣：它留在原處，或早已被酵母吃掉。蘭姆酒是貨真價實的蒸餾烈酒。酒尾帶來乳酪和塑膠氣息，不是甜味。","A spirit smells of solvent, almost like nail-varnish remover. What probably happened?":"一款烈酒帶有溶劑味，幾乎像去光水。可能發生了什麼事？","The cut from heads to heart came too late":"從酒頭切換到酒心的切取做得太晚","Too much of the tails was collected":"收集了太多酒尾","The spirit stayed too long in the barrel":"烈酒在桶中放得太久","The condenser's cooling water was too cold for the whole run":"整個蒸餾過程中冷凝器的冷卻水太冷","A solvent smell is typical of the heads: if too many got into the heart, you notice.":"溶劑氣味是酒頭的典型特徵：如果太多酒頭進入酒心，就會察覺到。","Tails instead bring cheesy and plastic notes. The barrel adds vanilla, spice and, with time, rancio, not solvent. A cold condenser is simply doing its job.":"酒尾帶來的則是乳酪和塑膠氣息。桶帶來香草、香料，時間久了還有 rancio，不是溶劑味。冷凝器冷只是在做它該做的事。","Why are the congeners with a boiling point similar to ethanol so important?":"為什麼沸點與乙醇相近的同屬物這麼重要？","They give the spirit its distinctive character":"它們賦予烈酒獨特的特色","They give the spirit its colour":"它們賦予烈酒顏色","They smell of solvent and must be removed":"它們帶溶劑氣味，必須去除","They make the newly made spirit sweeter":"它們讓新酒變得更甜","They come off with ethanol in the heart and define the spirit's aromatic identity.":"它們在酒心中與乙醇一起流出，決定了烈酒的香氣特徵。","A newly made spirit is colourless and dry, so these congeners give neither colour nor sweetness. The solvent smell belongs to the more volatile heads.":"新酒無色且不甜，所以這些同屬物既不帶來顏色，也不帶來甜味。溶劑氣味屬於更易揮發的酒頭。","Into which four groups can the fractions of a fermented liquid be divided?":"發酵液的餾分可以分成哪四組？","More volatile congeners, ethanol and similar, less volatile congeners, water":"較易揮發的同屬物、乙醇和相近者、較不易揮發的同屬物、水","Sugars, starch, yeast, water":"糖、澱粉、酵母、水","Heads, heart, tails, low wines":"酒頭、酒心、酒尾、低度酒","Esters, methanol, colour, water":"酯類、甲醇、顏色、水","They are grouped by volatility: more volatile than ethanol, ethanol and similar, less volatile, and water.":"它們依揮發性分組：比乙醇更易揮發、乙醇和相近者、較不易揮發，以及水。","These groups roughly match heads, heart, tails and liquid waste. Low wines, by contrast, are the product of the first distillation. Sugar and starch are gone by the end of fermentation, and there is no colour to separate.":"這幾組大致對應酒頭、酒心、酒尾和廢液。低度酒則是第一次蒸餾的產物。糖和澱粉在發酵結束時已經不存在，也沒有顏色可以分離。","A producer wants an almost neutral base to flavour. To what strength should it be distilled?":"一位生產者想要一款近乎中性的基酒來調味。應該蒸餾到多少濃度？","95–96% abv":"95–96% abv","25–30% abv":"25–30% abv","About 75% abv, like a good pot-still spirit":"大約 75% abv，像優質的壺式蒸餾烈酒","About 60% abv":"大約 60% abv","At 95–96% very few congeners remain: the base is neutral and leaves room for added flavours.":"在 95–96% 時留下的同屬物極少：基酒是中性的，為添加的風味留出空間。","This is why most flavoured spirits start from neutral spirit. At 75% or below the spirit keeps a marked raw-material aroma. 25–30% is the strength of low wines.":"所以大多數調味烈酒都從中性烈酒開始。在 75% 或更低時，烈酒保有明顯的原料香氣。25–30% 是低度酒的濃度。","What happens as the distillation strength rises from 75% to 90% abv?":"蒸餾濃度從 75% 升到 90% abv 時會發生什麼事？","Fewer congeners remain and the aroma turns light":"留下的同屬物變少，香氣變得清淡","The aroma grows stronger because the alcohol is more concentrated":"香氣變得更強，因為酒精更濃","The spirit gains colour":"烈酒有了顏色","The spirit becomes sweet":"烈酒變甜","As strength rises, more and more congeners are left behind: by about 90% the aroma is light.":"隨著濃度升高，越來越多同屬物被留下不取：到大約 90% 時香氣就很清淡。","More alcohol does not mean more aroma; quite the opposite. Colour and sweetness do not come from distillation, which always yields a colourless, dry liquid.":"酒精越多不代表香氣越多；恰恰相反。顏色和甜味不是來自蒸餾，蒸餾得到的永遠是無色、不甜的液體。","Why does the distiller keep smelling the flow from the condenser?":"為什麼蒸餾師要不斷聞冷凝器流出的酒液？","To decide when to make the cuts":"決定什麼時候切取","To check the spirit's colour":"檢查烈酒的顏色","To know when to add the yeast":"知道什麼時候加酵母","To know when to add finishing sugar to the heart":"知道什麼時候在酒心中加入收尾用的糖","The nose signals the end of the heads (no more solvent) and the arrival of the tails (cheese, plastic).":"鼻子能分辨酒頭的結束（不再有溶劑味）和酒尾的到來（乳酪、塑膠）。","Newly made spirit is always colourless, so there is no colour to check. Yeast work in fermentation, earlier. Any sugar is only added during finishing, not in the still.":"新酒一定是無色的，所以沒有顏色可以檢查。酵母在更早的發酵階段作用。如果加糖，也只在收尾階段，不是在蒸餾器中。","What separates a 'light' spirit at 90% from a neutral spirit at 96%?":"90% 的「清淡」烈酒和 96% 的中性烈酒有什麼區別？","The light one still keeps a little aroma":"清淡的仍保留一點香氣","The light one is always made in a pot still":"清淡的一定是用壺式蒸餾器做的","The neutral one has more congeners than the light one":"中性的同屬物比清淡的多","Nothing: they are two names for exactly the same style":"沒有區別：只是同一種風格的兩個名稱","At 90% a few congeners remain and the aroma is light; at 95–96% so few remain that it is neutral.":"在 90% 時還留有少許同屬物，香氣清淡；在 95–96% 時留下的極少，成為中性。","Both styles are made in column stills: a pot still cannot reach these strengths. Raising the strength reduces congeners rather than adding them. The difference is small but real.":"兩種風格都用柱式蒸餾器製作：壺式蒸餾器達不到這些濃度。提高濃度是減少同屬物，而不是增加。差異雖小，但確實存在。","A distiller cuts to tails earlier than usual. What is the most likely effect?":"一位蒸餾師比平常更早切到酒尾。最可能的效果是什麼？","Fewer heavy congeners and a cleaner spirit":"較重的同屬物變少，烈酒更乾淨","More solvent smell in the heart":"酒心中的溶劑氣味變多","More cheesy, plastic notes in the spirit":"烈酒中的乳酪、塑膠氣息變多","A more coloured, sweeter heart than usual":"酒心比平常顏色更深、更甜","Stopping the heart earlier keeps out some of the less volatile congeners typical of the tails.":"提早結束酒心，能把一部分酒尾典型的、較不易揮發的同屬物擋在外面。","Solvent belongs to the heads, at the start, and does not depend on the second cut. Cheesy notes would increase with a later cut, not an earlier one. The heart stays colourless and dry either way.":"溶劑味屬於開頭的酒頭，與第二次切取無關。乳酪氣息在切取較晚時才會增加，而不是較早時。無論如何酒心都是無色且不甜的。","What is the heads cut for?":"切除酒頭的目的是什麼？","To keep solvent-smelling congeners out of the spirit":"不讓帶溶劑氣味的同屬物進入烈酒","To remove water from the spirit":"去除烈酒中的水","To throw away all excess ethanol":"丟掉所有多餘的乙醇","To collect the cheesy and plastic notes":"收集乳酪和塑膠氣息","The first, very volatile fractions smell of solvent and are separated so as not to spoil the heart.":"最初那些非常易揮發的餾分帶有溶劑氣味，要分離出來，以免破壞酒心。","Water mostly stays at the bottom as waste; it does not come off first. Ethanol is what the distiller wants to keep. Cheesy and plastic notes come with the tails, at the end.":"水大部分留在底部成為廢液，不會最先流出。乙醇是蒸餾師想保留的東西。乳酪和塑膠氣息是最後隨酒尾出現的。","A spirit is collected at 75% abv but sold at 40%. Where does the difference come from?":"一款烈酒在 75% abv 收集，卻以 40% 販售。差別從何而來？","From adding water before bottling":"裝瓶前加水","From a second fermentation in bottle":"瓶中二次發酵","From alcohol evaporating during the few minutes the heads are collected":"收集酒頭的那幾分鐘內酒精蒸發","From chill-filtration, which removes alcohol":"冷凝過濾去除了酒精","Almost every spirit is brought down to bottling strength with pure water.":"幾乎所有烈酒都用純水降到裝瓶濃度。","Dilution is a finishing step that makes the spirit more enjoyable for most people. There is no second fermentation in bottle, and chill-filtration removes haze, not alcohol.":"稀釋是收尾步驟，讓烈酒對大多數人來說更好入口。瓶中不會二次發酵，冷凝過濾去除的是混濁，不是酒精。","Which statement about the strength spirits are distilled to is true?":"關於烈酒的蒸餾濃度，下列哪一項正確？","It varies widely: some stay below 75%, others reach 96%":"差異很大：有些低於 75%，有些達到 96%","It is always 75% abv by law":"依法一律是 75% abv","It is always the same as the bottled strength":"一律與裝瓶濃度相同","It never goes above 50%, the strength of the first vapours":"絕不會超過 50%，也就是最初蒸氣的濃度","A common level is about 75%, but some spirits are well below and others go up to 96%.":"常見的濃度是 75% 左右，但有些烈酒遠低於此，有些則高達 96%。","Distillation strength is a style choice: the lower it is, the more congeners remain. Bottled strength is usually lower because water is added. With several distillations the 50% of the first vapours is easily exceeded.":"蒸餾濃度是風格上的選擇：濃度越低，保留的同屬物越多。裝瓶濃度通常較低，因為加了水。經過多次蒸餾，很容易超過最初蒸氣的 50%。","Why does simple boiling not fully separate ethanol from water?":"為什麼單純煮沸無法完全分離乙醇和水？","The vapours contain both, just with more ethanol":"蒸氣中兩者都有，只是乙醇較多","Water never evaporates":"水永遠不會蒸發","All the ethanol stays in the liquid":"所有乙醇都留在液體中","Water and ethanol boil at exactly the same temperature":"水和乙醇在完全相同的溫度沸騰","When the liquid boils, the vapours are richer in ethanol but still contain water.":"液體沸騰時，蒸氣含有較多乙醇，但仍然含有水。","That is why several distillations, one after another or on the plates of a column, are needed to raise strength. Water (100 °C) and ethanol (about 78 °C) boil at different temperatures, but both pass partly into the vapour.":"所以要提高濃度，就需要多次蒸餾，不論是一次接一次，還是在蒸餾柱的蒸餾板上進行。水（100 °C）和乙醇（約 78 °C）的沸點不同，但兩者都會有一部分進入蒸氣。","What most directly decides the aroma intensity of a newly made spirit?":"什麼最直接決定新酒的香氣強度？","The strength at which it is collected":"收集時的濃度","The colour of the fermented liquid":"發酵液的顏色","The amount of sugar added after bottling":"裝瓶後添加的糖量","The lower the collection strength, the more congeners remain and the more intense the aroma.":"收集濃度越低，保留的同屬物越多，香氣就越濃郁。","At about 75% the aroma is medium or pronounced, at about 90% light, at 95–96% neutral. The fermented liquid's colour does not pass into the distillate. Any sugar is added before bottling and does not change the basic aroma intensity.":"在大約 75% 時香氣中等或明顯，大約 90% 時清淡，95–96% 時中性。發酵液的顏色不會進入餾出液。如果加糖，是在裝瓶前加的，不會改變基本的香氣強度。","Why do most flavoured spirits start from neutral spirit?":"為什麼大多數調味烈酒都從中性烈酒開始？","To let the added flavours show as much as possible":"讓添加的風味盡可能突顯","Because neutral spirit is already sweet":"因為中性烈酒本來就是甜的","Because neutral spirit is already golden":"因為中性烈酒本來就是金黃色的","Because it is the only spirit the law lets be sold below 40% abv":"因為它是法律唯一允許以低於 40% abv 販售的烈酒","With very few congeners of its own, neutral spirit does not mask the added botanicals and fruit.":"中性烈酒本身的同屬物極少，不會掩蓋添加的植物性原料和水果。","Like any newly made spirit, neutral spirit is colourless and dry. There are exceptions, such as spiced rum based on golden rum. Bottling strength does not depend on the type of base spirit.":"和所有新酒一樣，中性烈酒無色且不甜。也有例外，例如以金色蘭姆酒為基底的香料蘭姆酒。裝瓶濃度與基酒的類型無關。","What material are nearly all pot stills made of?":"幾乎所有壺式蒸餾器都用什麼材料製成？","Copper":"銅","Stainless steel":"不鏽鋼","Oak wood":"橡木","Copper is easy to shape and conducts heat well.":"銅容易塑形，導熱也好。","Stainless steel and glass are found instead in the inert vessels used to store unaged spirits. Oak is used for maturation barrels, not for stills.":"不鏽鋼和玻璃則用於存放未陳年烈酒的惰性容器。橡木用來製作熟成用的桶，不是蒸餾器。","What is the most common heat source for a pot still today?":"現今壺式蒸餾器最常見的熱源是什麼？","Steam, in coils or a jacket":"蒸汽，透過盤管或夾套","A gas burner under the pot, in almost every distillery":"壺身下方的瓦斯爐，幾乎每家蒸餾廠都用","A wood fire":"柴火","The sun":"太陽","Most modern stills are heated by steam.":"大多數現代蒸餾器都以蒸汽加熱。","Steam runs through internal coils or an external jacket. Direct heat, such as a gas burner, is now rare, with the notable exception of Cognac, where the law requires it.":"蒸汽流經內部的盤管或外部的夾套。瓦斯爐這類直火加熱如今已很少見，值得注意的例外是 Cognac，法律規定必須使用直火。","For which spirit does the law require a pot still heated by direct fire?":"法律規定哪一種烈酒必須使用直火加熱的壺式蒸餾器？","Scottish grain whisky":"蘇格蘭穀物威士忌","Light rum":"清淡型蘭姆酒","For Cognac, direct heating is a legal requirement.":"對 Cognac 來說，直火加熱是法定要求。","Cognac is the best-known exception to the steam rule. Vodka, grain whisky and light rum are distilled to high strength, typically in columns, so this rule does not apply to them.":"Cognac 是蒸汽通則中最知名的例外。伏特加、穀物威士忌和清淡型蘭姆酒都蒸餾到高濃度，通常使用蒸餾柱，所以這項規定不適用於它們。","What is the job of the lyne arm on a pot still?":"壺式蒸餾器上林恩臂（lyne arm）的功能是什麼？","It links the still head to the condenser":"連接蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器","It empties the pot at the end of a run":"在蒸餾結束時排空壺身","It heats the liquid with pressurised steam inside the pot":"在壺身內用加壓蒸汽加熱液體","It cools the vapours with cold water":"用冷水冷卻蒸氣","The lyne arm is the pipe carrying vapours from the still head to the condenser.":"林恩臂是把蒸氣從蒸餾器頂部送到冷凝器的管子。","Emptying is the drain's job, heating is the heat source's and cooling is the condenser's. The lyne arm is simply the route the vapours take to where they will become liquid again.":"排空是排放口的工作，加熱是熱源的工作，冷卻是冷凝器的工作。林恩臂只是蒸氣前往重新變成液體之處的通道。","Which part of a pot still holds the liquid to be distilled?":"壺式蒸餾器的哪個部分盛裝待蒸餾的液體？","The swan neck":"天鵝頸","The lyne arm":"林恩臂","The pot is the vessel that is filled and heated.":"壺身是裝料並加熱的容器。","The swan neck and lyne arm carry vapours, not the starting liquid. The condenser receives the vapours and turns them into new spirit.":"天鵝頸和林恩臂輸送的是蒸氣，不是起始液體。冷凝器接收蒸氣，並把它變成新酒。","In a shell and tube condenser, what turns the vapours back into liquid?":"在殼管式冷凝器中，什麼讓蒸氣變回液體？","Contact with pipes full of cold liquid":"接觸裝滿冷液體的管子","Direct contact with high-pressure steam":"直接接觸高壓蒸汽","Adding cold water straight into the spirit":"把冷水直接加進烈酒","Passing through activated charcoal":"通過活性碳","The vapours touch cooled pipes, usually holding cold water, and condense.":"蒸氣碰到冷卻的管子（通常裝著冷水）就會冷凝。","The coolant never mixes with the spirit: it flows inside the pipes and must be constantly refreshed to stay cold. High-pressure steam heats rather than cools, and activated charcoal is used for filtering.":"冷卻液絕不會與烈酒混合：它在管內流動，必須不斷更新才能保持低溫。高壓蒸汽是用來加熱而不是冷卻的，活性碳則用於過濾。","What is the other, older type of condenser sometimes seen?":"有時還能見到的另一種較古老的冷凝器是什麼？","The worm tub":"蟲桶冷凝器（worm tub）","The bubble cap":"泡罩","The downcomer":"降液管","The demijohn":"玻璃罈","The worm tub is a coiled pipe sitting in a tank of cold water.":"蟲桶冷凝器是浸在冷水槽中的一條盤繞的管子。","Bubble caps and downcomers are parts of the plates in a column still. A demijohn is a glass vessel used to store very old spirits, not a condenser.":"泡罩和降液管是柱式蒸餾器蒸餾板上的零件。玻璃罈是用來存放極老烈酒的玻璃容器，不是冷凝器。","What is the aim of the first distillation in a pot still?":"壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾的目的是什麼？","To remove some of the water from the fermented liquid":"去除發酵液中的一部分水","To separate heads, heart and tails precisely":"精確分離酒頭、酒心和酒尾","To make a spirit ready for sale at 75% abv":"製作 75% abv、可直接販售的烈酒","To give the spirit a copper colour before it goes into oak":"在入橡木桶前為烈酒染上銅色","The first distillation removes water and produces stronger low wines.":"第一次蒸餾去除水分，產生濃度較高的低度酒。","The precise cuts and collection of the heart happen in the second distillation. After the first run the liquid is only 25–30% abv, so it is not a saleable spirit. Copper does not colour the spirit.":"精確的切取和酒心的收集在第二次蒸餾中進行。第一次蒸餾後液體只有 25–30% abv，所以還不是可販售的烈酒。銅不會為烈酒上色。","What is the liquid from the first pot-still distillation called?":"壺式蒸餾器第一次蒸餾得到的液體叫做什麼？","Heart":"酒心","The first run produces low wines, at 25–30% abv.":"第一次蒸餾產生低度酒，濃度為 25–30% abv。","The heart is only collected in the second distillation. Wort is the sweet grain liquid before fermentation. Neutral spirit needs 95–96% abv, impossible in a pot still.":"酒心要到第二次蒸餾才收集。麥汁是發酵前的穀物甜液。中性烈酒需要 95–96% abv，壺式蒸餾器不可能達到。","What is the typical strength of low wines?":"低度酒的典型濃度是多少？","8–10% abv":"8–10% abv","70–75% abv":"70–75% abv","90–96% abv":"90–96% abv","Low wines are usually between 25% and 30% abv.":"低度酒通常在 25% 至 30% abv 之間。","8–10% is the strength of the starting fermented liquid. Around 75% is where the heart of the second distillation sits. 90–96% can only be reached with a column still.":"8–10% 是起始發酵液的濃度。75% 左右是第二次蒸餾酒心所在的位置。90–96% 只有柱式蒸餾器才能達到。","Why are low wines so low in strength?":"為什麼低度酒的濃度這麼低？","Collecting all the alcohol means collecting lots of water too":"要收集所有酒精，就會同時收集到大量的水","The copper absorbs much of the ethanol during the first distillation":"第一次蒸餾時銅吸收了大量乙醇","Water is added by law":"法律規定要加水","The heads are left in":"酒頭被留在裡面","The flow's strength drops for hours, and everything is collected so as not to lose alcohol and aromas.":"流出酒液的濃度會持續下降好幾個小時，而為了不損失酒精和香氣，全部都會收集起來。","At first the vapour is around 50% abv, but most of the alcohol and aromas are still in the pot. Carrying on down to about 1% abv collects more and more water. Copper does not absorb ethanol and there is no compulsory addition of water.":"一開始蒸氣大約是 50% abv，但大部分的酒精和香氣仍留在壺身裡。持續蒸餾到約 1% abv，會收集到越來越多的水。銅不會吸收乙醇，也沒有強制加水的規定。","In the second distillation, what tells the distiller it is time for the first cut?":"在第二次蒸餾中，什麼讓蒸餾師知道該做第一次切取了？","The solvent smell no longer dominates":"溶劑氣味不再是主導","Cheesy and plastic notes appear":"出現乳酪和塑膠氣息","The flow drops to 1% abv and the pot is nearly empty":"酒液濃度降到 1% abv，壺身幾乎空了","The spirit turns golden":"烈酒變成金黃色","When the solvent-smelling heads end, collection switches to the heart.":"帶溶劑氣味的酒頭結束時，就改為收集酒心。","Cheesy and plastic notes signal the second cut instead, into the tails. 1% abv marks the end of distillation. The spirit does not change colour in the still: it stays colourless.":"乳酪和塑膠氣息代表的是第二次切取，也就是進入酒尾。1% abv 代表蒸餾結束。烈酒在蒸餾器中不會變色：始終是無色的。","What is a 'cut' in pot-still distillation?":"在壺式蒸餾中，「切取」是什麼？","Switching the tank the flow is collected in":"更換收集酒液的槽","Adding water to lower the strength before bottling":"裝瓶前加水降低濃度","Mixing spirits of different ages":"混合不同年數的烈酒","Suddenly switching off the heat source":"突然關掉熱源","Making a cut means redirecting the flow from the condenser to another tank.":"切取就是把冷凝器流出的酒液改導向另一個槽。","The first cut separates heads from heart, the second heart from tails. Reducing with water and blending happen after distillation. The still is only switched off at the end, when the flow reaches about 1% abv.":"第一次切取分開酒頭和酒心，第二次分開酒心和酒尾。加水降度和調和都在蒸餾之後進行。蒸餾器要到最後、酒液濃度降到約 1% abv 時才關閉。","What goes into the pot for the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾時，壺身裡裝的是什麼？","Low wines plus heads and tails from the last batch":"低度酒加上上一批的酒頭和酒尾","Only the fermented liquid at 10% abv":"只有 10% abv 的發酵液","The previous batch's heart, to make it even stronger":"上一批的酒心，讓它變得更濃","The watery waste from the first distillation":"第一次蒸餾的含水廢液","Heads and tails from the previous cycle join the new low wines.":"上一輪的酒頭和酒尾會與新的低度酒合在一起。","The fermented liquid is used in the first distillation. The heart is the final product and is not redistilled. The watery waste is thrown away because it is mostly water.":"發酵液用於第一次蒸餾。酒心是最終產品，不會再蒸餾。含水的廢液因為大部分是水，所以被丟棄。","Why are heads and tails put into the next distillation instead of being thrown away?":"為什麼酒頭和酒尾要放進下一次蒸餾，而不是丟掉？","They still contain plenty of ethanol and positive aromas":"它們仍含有大量乙醇和好的香氣","They are the finest part and need concentrating further":"它們是最精華的部分，需要進一步濃縮","They give colour to the next spirit":"它們為下一批烈酒帶來顏色","The law forbids throwing them away":"法律禁止丟棄","As well as unwanted compounds, they hold alcohol and good aromas worth recovering.":"除了不想要的化合物，它們還含有值得回收的酒精和好香氣。","Heads and tails are not the prized part: in excess they give solvent or cheesy smells. Redistilling them recovers what is good in them. They add no colour, because every spirit comes off colourless.":"酒頭和酒尾並不是珍貴的部分：過量時會帶來溶劑或乳酪氣味。再蒸餾可以回收其中好的東西。它們不會增添顏色，因為所有烈酒蒸餾出來都是無色的。","What aroma intensity does a pot-still spirit typically have?":"壺式蒸餾烈酒的香氣強度通常如何？","Medium to pronounced":"中等到明顯","Light, like a filtered vodka":"清淡，像過濾過的伏特加","Always very delicate, whatever the cut":"不論怎麼切取，總是非常細緻","Imprecise separation lets many congeners through with the ethanol.":"分離不精確，讓許多同屬物隨乙醇一起通過。","A pot still cannot reach neutral-spirit strengths, so it does not produce neutral or light spirits like vodka. Where the cuts fall changes the style, but the aroma generally stays marked.":"壺式蒸餾器達不到中性烈酒的濃度，所以做不出伏特加那樣中性或清淡的烈酒。切取點的位置會改變風格，但香氣通常仍然鮮明。","A distiller with only a pot still wants to make neutral spirit at 96% abv. What happens?":"一位只有壺式蒸餾器的蒸餾師想做 96% abv 的中性烈酒。結果會怎樣？","It cannot be done: that strength needs a column still":"做不到：這個濃度需要柱式蒸餾器","It works with two distillations":"蒸餾兩次就可以","It works if direct fire is used, as in Cognac":"像 Cognac 一樣用直火就可以","It works by discarding the tails and keeping only the heads":"丟掉酒尾、只留酒頭就可以","In a pot still, 96% abv simply cannot be reached.":"壺式蒸餾器根本達不到 96% abv。","Every batch requires recovering all the alcohol, which dilutes the ethanol with water. Only a column still, with many simultaneous distillations, reaches such high strengths. The heating method does not change this limit, and the heads are solvent-smelling compounds.":"每一批都要回收所有的酒精，這就讓乙醇被水稀釋。只有柱式蒸餾器能靠許多同時進行的蒸餾達到這麼高的濃度。加熱方式不會改變這個極限，而酒頭是帶溶劑氣味的化合物。","Why is pot-still distillation called a batch process?":"為什麼壺式蒸餾被稱為批次製程？","It is filled, run, emptied and started again":"裝料、蒸餾、清空，再重新開始","It takes a non-stop flow of pre-heated fermented liquid":"它接收不間斷流入的預熱發酵液","It makes several different spirits at once":"它同時製作好幾種不同的烈酒","It distils only once a year":"它一年只蒸餾一次","Each load is separate: one cycle must finish before the next begins.":"每一次裝料都是獨立的：一個循環結束後，下一個才能開始。","A continuous flow of pre-heated liquid is typical of a column still, which can run without stopping. A pot still does not make several spirits at once and runs many times a year, batch after batch.":"連續流入預熱液體是柱式蒸餾器的典型做法，它可以不停運轉。壺式蒸餾器不會同時製作好幾種烈酒，而且一年運作很多次，一批接一批。","Down to what strength of flow are the tails collected before the still is shut down?":"酒尾要收集到酒液濃度降到多少，才關閉蒸餾器？","About 1% abv":"大約 1% abv","About 25% abv":"大約 25% abv","Tails are collected until the flow falls to about 1% abv.":"酒尾一直收集到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv。","This recovers almost all the remaining alcohol, which goes back into the next batch. 75% is the average strength of the heart and 25% that of low wines. Stopping earlier would waste ethanol in the residue.":"這樣可以回收幾乎所有剩下的酒精，並放回下一批。75% 是酒心的平均濃度，25% 是低度酒的濃度。提早停止會把乙醇浪費在殘液裡。","A distiller widens the heart cut to take in a little more of the tails. What is the likely effect?":"一位蒸餾師放寬酒心的切取範圍，多收一點酒尾。可能的效果是什麼？","A more intense, fuller-flavoured spirit":"烈酒更濃郁、風味更飽滿","A more neutral spirit, close to vodka":"烈酒更中性，接近伏特加","A paler-coloured spirit":"烈酒顏色更淺","A spirit with a stronger solvent smell, typical of the first fractions":"烈酒有更強的溶劑氣味，也就是最初餾分的典型氣味","More heavy fractions in the heart mean more intense aromas, up to the risk of tail notes.":"酒心裡較重的餾分越多，香氣就越濃郁，甚至有出現酒尾氣息的風險。","Tails carry less volatile congeners: in small doses they add body and character, in excess cheesy notes. The solvent smell comes from the heads, at the start. Colour does not change, because the spirit stays colourless.":"酒尾帶有較不易揮發的同屬物：少量時增添酒體和特色，過量則出現乳酪氣息。溶劑氣味來自開頭的酒頭。顏色不會改變，因為烈酒始終是無色的。","Which sequence describes the vapours' path through a pot still?":"哪一組順序描述了蒸氣在壺式蒸餾器中的路徑？","Pot, still head, swan neck, lyne arm, condenser":"壺身、蒸餾器頂部、天鵝頸、林恩臂、冷凝器","Pot, lyne arm, condenser, swan neck, still head":"壺身、林恩臂、冷凝器、天鵝頸、蒸餾器頂部","Condenser, pot, still head, lyne arm, drain":"冷凝器、壺身、蒸餾器頂部、林恩臂、排放口","Drain, pot, condenser, still head, lyne arm":"排放口、壺身、冷凝器、蒸餾器頂部、林恩臂","Vapours rise from the pot into the still head, narrow through the swan neck, and the lyne arm takes them to the condenser.":"蒸氣從壺身上升到蒸餾器頂部，經天鵝頸收窄，再由林恩臂送到冷凝器。","The condenser is always the last stop, where the vapours become liquid again. The drain is not part of the vapour path: it only empties the pot at the end of a run.":"冷凝器永遠是最後一站，蒸氣在那裡重新變成液體。排放口不在蒸氣的路徑上：它只在蒸餾結束時排空壺身。","Why must the condenser's cooling water be constantly refreshed?":"為什麼冷凝器的冷卻水必須不斷更新？","Otherwise it warms up and stops condensing the vapours":"否則它會變熱，無法再冷凝蒸氣","Because it mixes into the spirit and lowers its strength":"因為它會混入烈酒並降低濃度","To stop the copper changing the colour of the newly made spirit":"防止銅改變新酒的顏色","Because it is also used to fill the pot":"因為它也用來注滿壺身","The coolant must stay cold to turn the vapours back into liquid.":"冷卻液必須保持低溫，才能把蒸氣變回液體。","The hot vapours pass their heat to the water in the pipes: if it is not replaced, it warms up and condensation stops. The water flows separately from the spirit, so it does not dilute it. Copper does not colour the spirit, and the pot is filled with the liquid to be distilled.":"高溫的蒸氣把熱傳給管中的水：如果不更換，水會變熱，冷凝就停止了。水與烈酒分開流動，所以不會稀釋烈酒。銅不會為烈酒上色，壺身裝的是待蒸餾的液體。","What is the drain on a pot still for?":"壺式蒸餾器的排放口有什麼用途？","To empty the still after use":"使用後排空蒸餾器","To let the heads out":"讓酒頭流出","To send the tails back into the pot during distillation":"在蒸餾過程中把酒尾送回壺身","To inject steam into the liquid":"把蒸汽注入液體","The drain, at the bottom of the pot, lets it be emptied at the end of a run.":"排放口位於壺身底部，可在蒸餾結束時把它排空。","This is where the watery residue that is discarded comes out. Heads and tails leave via the condenser and are collected in a tank for the next batch, not during the same run. Steam comes through coils or a jacket.":"被丟棄的含水殘液就是從這裡排出。酒頭和酒尾經由冷凝器流出，收集在槽中供下一批使用，而不是在同一次蒸餾中使用。蒸汽則經由盤管或夾套進入。","In which two ways can steam heat a pot still?":"蒸汽可以用哪兩種方式加熱壺式蒸餾器？","Internal coils or an external jacket":"內部盤管或外部夾套","Direct injection into the condenser or the lyne arm":"直接注入冷凝器或林恩臂","A gas burner or a wood fire":"瓦斯爐或柴火","A heat exchanger on the still head or swan neck":"裝在蒸餾器頂部或天鵝頸上的熱交換器","Steam runs through coils inside the pot or through an external jacket around it.":"蒸汽流經壺身內的盤管，或圍繞壺身的外部夾套。","Most modern stills are heated this way. Gas and wood are direct fire, rare today except in Cognac. Heat goes to the pot, not to the upper parts or the condenser, which must stay cold.":"大多數現代蒸餾器都這樣加熱。瓦斯和木柴屬於直火，除了 Cognac 以外如今已很少見。熱是加在壺身上，不是上方的部位或冷凝器，冷凝器必須保持低溫。","Which heat source do Cognac stills usually use today?":"現今 Cognac 的蒸餾器通常使用哪種熱源？","Gas burners":"瓦斯爐","Internal steam coils":"內部蒸汽盤管","An external steam jacket":"外部蒸汽夾套","Steam injected straight into the wine":"直接注入葡萄酒的蒸汽","Cognac requires direct fire, which today almost always means gas burners.":"Cognac 規定使用直火，如今幾乎都是瓦斯爐。","Coils and jackets are the usual heating elsewhere, but Cognac's rules require a flame. Direct steam injection is found in some large column stills.":"盤管和夾套是其他地方常見的加熱方式，但 Cognac 的規定要求用火焰。直接注入蒸汽則見於一些大型柱式蒸餾器。","Besides being easy to shape, why is copper used for stills?":"除了容易塑形，蒸餾器為什麼使用銅？","It conducts heat well":"導熱良好","It gives the spirit colour":"為烈酒帶來顏色","It adds sugar to the spirit":"為烈酒增添糖分","It lets a pot still reach 96% abv":"讓壺式蒸餾器達到 96% abv","Copper is easy to shape and transfers heat well, which is why nearly all pot stills are copper.":"銅容易塑形，傳熱效果好，所以幾乎所有壺式蒸餾器都是銅製的。","The spirit leaving the still is colourless and dry anyway. The 96% limit comes from how pot stills work, not from the metal: a column is needed.":"離開蒸餾器的烈酒反正都是無色且不甜的。96% 的極限來自壺式蒸餾器的運作方式，不是金屬：需要用蒸餾柱。","In a shell and tube condenser, where does the vapour enter and where does the spirit leave?":"在殼管式冷凝器中，蒸氣從哪裡進入，烈酒從哪裡流出？","Vapour enters at the top, liquid leaves at the bottom":"蒸氣從頂部進入，液體從底部流出","Vapour enters at the bottom, liquid leaves at the top":"蒸氣從底部進入，液體從頂部流出","In and out through the same pipe, passing through the cooling water":"進出都經同一條管子，並穿過冷卻水","It enters from the side and returns to the pot":"從側面進入，再流回壺身","Vapour enters at the top, meets tubes of cold water, condenses and runs down: new spirit leaves at the bottom.":"蒸氣從頂部進入，碰到裝著冷水的管子後冷凝並往下流：新酒從底部流出。","Vapour and cooling water never mix: heat passes through the metal tubes. This is the most common condenser today. The condensed spirit goes to the collecting tanks, not back into the pot.":"蒸氣和冷卻水絕不會混合：熱透過金屬管傳遞。這是現今最常見的冷凝器。冷凝後的烈酒流向收集槽，不會回到壺身。","Which of these parts is NOT found on a pot still?":"下列哪個零件不在壺式蒸餾器上？","The lyne arm leading to the condenser":"通往冷凝器的林恩臂","The drain":"排放口","The downcomer belongs to a column still's plates: it sends overflowing liquid down to the plate below.":"降液管屬於柱式蒸餾器的蒸餾板：它把溢出的液體送到下一層蒸餾板。","Swan neck, lyne arm and drain are typical pot-still parts, along with heat source, pot, still head and condenser. Plates, bubble caps and downcomers are the heart of a column still.":"天鵝頸、林恩臂和排放口是壺式蒸餾器的典型零件，另外還有熱源、壺身、蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器。蒸餾板、泡罩和降液管則是柱式蒸餾器的核心。","What is the still filled with for the first distillation?":"第一次蒸餾時，蒸餾器裡裝的是什麼？","The fermented liquid, about 10% abv":"發酵液，約 10% abv","Low wines at 25–30% abv":"25–30% abv 的低度酒","Low wines plus heads and tails from the last run":"低度酒加上上一次蒸餾的酒頭和酒尾","Diluted neutral spirit":"稀釋過的中性烈酒","The first distillation starts from the fermented liquid, usually about 10% abv.":"第一次蒸餾從發酵液開始，通常約 10% abv。","Low wines are the result of the first distillation and go, with heads and tails, into the second. Diluted neutral spirit is used for redistilling with botanicals, not for making a base spirit.":"低度酒是第一次蒸餾的成果，會與酒頭和酒尾一起進入第二次蒸餾。稀釋過的中性烈酒用於與植物性原料一起再蒸餾，不是用來製作基酒。","For how long is liquid collected in the first distillation?":"第一次蒸餾要收集液體多久？","For hours, until the flow drops to about 1% abv":"好幾個小時，直到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv","For about 10–15 minutes, like the heads":"大約 10–15 分鐘，和酒頭一樣","As long as the flow is above 75% abv":"只要酒液濃度高於 75% abv 就繼續","Only while 50% vapour comes off, about half an hour":"只在流出 50% 蒸氣的期間，大約半小時","Collection runs for several hours, until the flow reaches about 1% abv, so almost all the alcohol is recovered.":"收集持續好幾個小時，直到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv，這樣幾乎所有酒精都能回收。","Stopping after half an hour would leave most of the alcohol and good congeners in the pot. The first distillation has no heads or heart cuts; those belong to the second.":"半小時後就停止，會把大部分的酒精和好的同屬物留在壺身裡。第一次蒸餾沒有酒頭或酒心的切取；那些屬於第二次蒸餾。","The first vapours of the first distillation are about 50% abv. Why not stop there?":"第一次蒸餾最初的蒸氣大約是 50% abv。為什麼不就此停止？","Most of the alcohol and aromas are still in the pot":"大部分的酒精和香氣仍在壺身裡","Because the law requires at least eight hours":"因為法律規定至少要八小時","Because those vapours are only water":"因為那些蒸氣只是水","Because the liquid has not finished fermenting at that point":"因為液體到那時還沒發酵完成","To recover the alcohol and positive congeners the still must run for hours, collecting a lot of water too.":"要回收酒精和好的同屬物，蒸餾器必須運作好幾個小時，同時也收集到大量的水。","That is why low wines only reach 25–30% abv. The first vapours are rich in alcohol, not just water. Fermentation is over before the liquid enters the still, and no fixed duration is imposed.":"所以低度酒只有 25–30% abv。最初的蒸氣富含酒精，不只是水。發酵在液體進入蒸餾器之前就結束了，也沒有規定固定的時間。","What happens to the watery liquid left in the pot after the first distillation?":"第一次蒸餾後留在壺身裡的含水液體怎麼處理？","It is discarded":"丟棄","It is added to the low wines":"加進低度酒","It is used to dilute the heart":"用來稀釋酒心","It is kept with the heads and tails for the next batch":"與酒頭和酒尾一起保留給下一批","The watery residue in the pot is waste and is thrown away.":"壺身裡的含水殘液是廢液，會被丟棄。","Only the heads and tails of the second distillation are recycled, as they still hold ethanol and useful aromas. The residue is almost pure water. Spirits are diluted with completely pure water.":"只有第二次蒸餾的酒頭和酒尾會回收再用，因為它們仍含有乙醇和有用的香氣。殘液幾乎是純水。稀釋烈酒用的是完全純淨的水。","At least how many distillations does a pot still need to make a spirit?":"用壺式蒸餾器製作烈酒，至少需要蒸餾幾次？","One for each plate":"每層蒸餾板一次","The fermented liquid must be distilled at least twice: first into low wines, then into the actual spirit.":"發酵液至少要蒸餾兩次：先成為低度酒，再成為真正的烈酒。","A single distillation only gives low wines at 25–30%. Some producers distil three times, but two is the minimum. Plates belong to column stills, not pot stills.":"只蒸餾一次只能得到 25–30% 的低度酒。有些生產者蒸餾三次，但兩次是最低限度。蒸餾板屬於柱式蒸餾器，不是壺式蒸餾器。","What is the aim of the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾的目的是什麼？","To make a saleable spirit of ethanol and similar congeners":"製作由乙醇和相近同屬物構成、可販售的烈酒","To remove some water from the fermented liquid":"去除發酵液中的一部分水","To give the spirit colour and sweetness":"為烈酒帶來顏色和甜味","To reach 96% abv for a fully neutral spirit":"達到 96% abv，得到完全中性的烈酒","The second distillation selects and concentrates ethanol and congeners of similar boiling point, producing the spirit to be sold.":"第二次蒸餾篩選並濃縮乙醇和沸點相近的同屬物，產出要販售的烈酒。","Removing water from the fermented liquid is the first distillation's job. Colour and sweetness come later, if the producer chooses. 96% is impossible in a pot still.":"去除發酵液中的水是第一次蒸餾的工作。顏色和甜味是之後才有的，視生產者的選擇而定。壺式蒸餾器不可能達到 96%。","How long do the heads usually last in the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾中，酒頭通常持續多久？","About 10–15 minutes":"大約 10–15 分鐘","Several hours":"好幾個小時","About 1 minute":"大約 1 分鐘","All night, until the heart arrives":"一整夜，直到酒心出現","After about 10–15 minutes the flow no longer smells of solvent and the distiller cuts to the heart.":"大約 10–15 分鐘後，酒液不再有溶劑味，蒸餾師就切到酒心。","It is the heart and then the tails that last for hours. Head compounds are few and run out quickly, so this phase is short.":"持續好幾個小時的是酒心和之後的酒尾。酒頭的化合物數量少，很快就耗盡，所以這個階段很短。","Where are the heads collected during the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾時，酒頭收集在哪裡？","In a separate tank that will also take the tails":"在另一個槽裡，之後也會收酒尾","In the same tank as the heart":"和酒心在同一個槽","Straight into the drain":"直接流進排放口","In barrels, to age them separately":"裝進桶中，另外陳年","The heads go into their own tank; after the second cut the tails are added to it.":"酒頭進入專屬的槽；第二次切取後，酒尾也加進這個槽。","This tank's contents will go into the next second distillation with the new low wines. Mixing it into the heart would bring solvent and plastic smells. It is neither discarded nor aged.":"這個槽裡的東西會與新的低度酒一起進入下一次的第二次蒸餾。把它混進酒心會帶來溶劑和塑膠氣味。它既不會被丟棄，也不會陳年。","What strength is the heart in its tank typically at the end of the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾結束時，槽中酒心的濃度通常是多少？","About 25–30% abv":"大約 25–30% abv","About 40% abv, ready to bottle":"大約 40% abv，可直接裝瓶","When heart collection stops, the tank typically holds liquid of about 75% abv.":"停止收集酒心時，槽中的液體通常大約是 75% abv。","25–30% is the strength of low wines, and 96% is only reached in a column. 40% is a selling strength, reached later by adding water.":"25–30% 是低度酒的濃度，96% 只有蒸餾柱才能達到。40% 是販售濃度，之後加水才達到。","After the second cut, where is the tails flow sent?":"第二次切取後，酒尾流向哪裡？","To the tank that already holds the heads":"流向已經裝著酒頭的槽","To the heart tank":"流向酒心的槽","Straight into barrels":"直接入桶","Into the first-distillation pot, with the fermented liquid":"流進第一次蒸餾的壺身，與發酵液一起","The tails are collected with the heads, until the flow drops to about 1% abv.":"酒尾與酒頭收集在一起，直到酒液濃度降到約 1% abv。","Heads and tails go back into the next second distillation with the low wines, not into the first. In the heart they would add cheesy and plastic notes.":"酒頭和酒尾會與低度酒一起回到下一次的第二次蒸餾，而不是第一次。它們如果進入酒心，會帶來乳酪和塑膠氣息。","Why does a pot-still spirit keep so much character?":"為什麼壺式蒸餾烈酒能保有這麼多特色？","Separation is imprecise: many congeners come off with the ethanol":"分離不精確：許多同屬物隨乙醇一起流出","Copper adds its own aromas":"銅會增添它自己的香氣","It is only distilled once":"只蒸餾一次","The heads and tails are left in the heart for more flavour":"為了更多風味，酒頭和酒尾被留在酒心裡","A pot still does not separate precisely: many congeners are concentrated with the ethanol, hence its medium to pronounced aroma.":"壺式蒸餾器的分離並不精確：許多同屬物與乙醇一起被濃縮，所以香氣中等到明顯。","Copper is about shape and heat, not an aroma source here. There are at least two distillations. Heads and tails do not stay in the heart; they are separated and recycled into the next batch.":"銅的重點在於形狀和導熱，在這裡不是香氣來源。至少要蒸餾兩次。酒頭和酒尾不會留在酒心裡；它們被分離出來，並回收到下一批。","A distiller decides to throw away the heads and tails instead of reusing them. What is lost?":"一位蒸餾師決定丟掉酒頭和酒尾，不再重複使用。會損失什麼？","Ethanol and good congeners they still contain":"其中仍含有的乙醇和好的同屬物","Nothing: they hold only unwanted compounds":"沒有損失：裡面只有不想要的化合物","The colour they would have given the spirit":"它們原本會帶給烈酒的顏色","The sugar needed to ferment the next batch":"下一批發酵所需的糖","Heads and tails contain unwanted compounds but also plenty of ethanol and positive congeners: discarding them is wasteful.":"酒頭和酒尾含有不想要的化合物，但也含有大量乙醇和好的同屬物：丟掉很浪費。","That is why they go back into the next second distillation. They are colourless and hold no sugar, which is not needed at that stage anyway: fermentation is over.":"所以它們會回到下一次的第二次蒸餾。它們無色，也不含糖，而且那個階段本來就不需要糖：發酵已經結束了。","Which of these does NOT go into the still for the second distillation?":"下列哪一項不會進入第二次蒸餾的蒸餾器？","Fresh fermented liquid":"新鮮的發酵液","The low wines":"低度酒","The heads from the previous second distillation":"上一次第二次蒸餾的酒頭","The tails from the previous second distillation":"上一次第二次蒸餾的酒尾","Fermented liquid goes into the first distillation; the second takes low wines plus the previous run's heads and tails.":"發酵液進入第一次蒸餾；第二次蒸餾用的是低度酒加上上一次的酒頭和酒尾。","Recycling heads and tails in each second distillation avoids losing ethanol and positive aromas. The roughly 10% fermented liquid must first lose water in the first distillation.":"在每次第二次蒸餾中回收酒頭和酒尾，可避免損失乙醇和好的香氣。約 10% 的發酵液必須先在第一次蒸餾中去除水分。","Which pair of strengths is correct?":"哪一組濃度是正確的？","Low wines 25–30%, heart about 75%":"低度酒 25–30%，酒心約 75%","Low wines about 75%, heart 25–30%":"低度酒約 75%，酒心 25–30%","Low wines 10%, heart 96%":"低度酒 10%，酒心 96%","Low wines 50%, heart 40%, the bottling strength":"低度酒 50%，酒心 40%，即裝瓶濃度","Low wines come off at 25–30% abv; the heart of the second distillation reaches about 75%.":"低度酒流出時為 25–30% abv；第二次蒸餾的酒心達到約 75%。","Each distillation concentrates the alcohol, so the heart is stronger than the low wines, not the reverse. 10% is the fermented liquid, and 96% is impossible in a pot still.":"每次蒸餾都會濃縮酒精，所以酒心比低度酒濃，而不是相反。10% 是發酵液，96% 在壺式蒸餾器中不可能達到。","What happens right after the second cut?":"第二次切取之後緊接著發生什麼事？","Tails are collected until the flow falls to about 1%":"收集酒尾，直到酒液濃度降到約 1%","The still is shut down at once":"立刻關閉蒸餾器","Heart collection begins":"開始收集酒心","New low wines are added to the still-boiling pot":"在仍沸騰的壺身中加入新的低度酒","After the second cut the flow, now tails, goes to the heads tank until about 1% abv; then the still is shut down.":"第二次切取後，流出的酒液已是酒尾，會流向酒頭的槽，直到約 1% abv；然後關閉蒸餾器。","The heart starts at the first cut, not the second. A pot still works in batches: no liquid is added mid-run. At the end the watery residue is thrown away.":"酒心從第一次切取開始，不是第二次。壺式蒸餾器以批次運作：蒸餾中途不會加入液體。最後含水的殘液會被丟棄。","Why can low wines not be sold as a spirit?":"為什麼低度酒不能當作烈酒販售？","They are weak and not yet split into heads, heart and tails":"濃度低，而且還沒分成酒頭、酒心和酒尾","They still contain all the sugar":"仍含有全部的糖","They are already coloured by the copper":"已經被銅染色","They are too strong, above 90% abv, for any drinker":"濃度太高，超過 90% abv，沒有人能喝","Low wines, at 25–30%, are the base for the second distillation, which makes the spirit to be sold.":"低度酒濃度為 25–30%，是第二次蒸餾的基礎，第二次蒸餾才做出要販售的烈酒。","They still hold unwanted compounds, since no cuts are made in the first distillation. Sugar was used up in fermentation and the distillate is colourless. 25–30% is far from 90%.":"它們仍含有不想要的化合物，因為第一次蒸餾不做切取。糖已在發酵中用完，餾出液是無色的。25–30% 離 90% 還很遠。","During a pot-still run, how does the strength of the flow from the condenser change?":"在壺式蒸餾的過程中，冷凝器流出酒液的濃度如何變化？","It falls as the alcohol in the pot runs down":"隨著壺身裡的酒精減少而下降","It stays the same from start to finish":"從頭到尾保持不變","It keeps rising, up to 96% abv":"持續上升，直到 96% abv","It rises and falls with the cooling water temperature":"隨冷卻水的溫度而升降","As the run goes on, less and less alcohol remains in the pot, so the flow gets more and more watery.":"隨著蒸餾進行，壺身裡的酒精越來越少，所以流出的酒液含水越來越多。","That is why the still is shut down when the flow reaches about 1% abv. In a batch process the liquid is not renewed, so strength can neither stay constant nor climb to 96%.":"所以酒液濃度降到約 1% abv 時就關閉蒸餾器。在批次製程中液體不會補充，所以濃度既不可能保持恆定，也不可能升到 96%。","Which heat source is now rare on pot stills?":"壺式蒸餾器現在很少使用哪一種熱源？","Direct flame, such as a gas burner":"直接火焰，例如瓦斯爐","Steam in general":"一般的蒸汽","Almost all modern stills are steam-heated; direct fire is rare, except in Cognac.":"幾乎所有現代蒸餾器都用蒸汽加熱；直火很少見，Cognac 除外。","Internal coils and external jackets are the two common ways to use steam. Cognac is the obvious exception, since its law requires a flame.":"內部盤管和外部夾套是使用蒸汽的兩種常見方式。Cognac 是明顯的例外，因為它的法規要求用火焰。","Which type of condenser is most common today?":"現今最常見的是哪一種冷凝器？","Shell and tube":"殼管式","An ice tank above the still head":"蒸餾器頂部上方的冰槽","None: the vapours cool in the air in the lyne arm":"沒有：蒸氣在林恩臂的空氣中冷卻","The shell and tube condenser is the most common: vapours meet tubes full of cold water.":"殼管式冷凝器最常見：蒸氣碰到裝滿冷水的管子。","The worm tub is an older design, compulsory in Cognac but rare elsewhere. Every still needs a real condenser with constantly refreshed coolant.":"蟲桶冷凝器是較古老的設計，在 Cognac 是強制規定，但其他地方很少見。每座蒸餾器都需要真正的冷凝器，並不斷更新冷卻液。","On a Scottish-style pot still, which part sits between the still head and the lyne arm?":"在蘇格蘭式的壺式蒸餾器上，哪個部分位於蒸餾器頂部和林恩臂之間？","The pot full of liquid to distil":"裝滿待蒸餾液體的壺身","Above the still head the still narrows into the swan neck, from which the lyne arm leads to the condenser.":"蒸餾器頂部往上收窄成天鵝頸，林恩臂再從那裡通往冷凝器。","The vapour path is pot, still head, swan neck, lyne arm, condenser. The drain is at the bottom of the pot and only empties it. (In Cognac the names differ: there the 'swan neck' is the tube leading to the condenser.)":"蒸氣的路徑是壺身、蒸餾器頂部、天鵝頸、林恩臂、冷凝器。排放口在壺身底部，只用來排空。（在 Cognac 名稱不同：那裡的「天鵝頸」是通往冷凝器的管子。）","Which of these is a classic example of a pot-still spirit?":"下列哪一項是壺式蒸餾烈酒的經典例子？","Scotch malt whisky":"Scotch 麥芽威士忌","Vodka":"伏特加","The neutral spirit used as a gin base":"用作琴酒基底的中性烈酒","Scotch malt whisky is made in copper pot stills, with a medium to pronounced aroma.":"Scotch 麥芽威士忌用銅製壺式蒸餾器製作，香氣中等到明顯。","Vodka, neutral spirit and grain whisky need strengths (90–96%) only a column can reach. Cognac is another classic pot-still spirit.":"伏特加、中性烈酒和穀物威士忌需要的濃度（90–96%）只有蒸餾柱才能達到。Cognac 是另一種經典的壺式蒸餾烈酒。","Which coolant is usually used in a condenser?":"冷凝器通常使用哪種冷卻液？","Cold water":"冷水","High-pressure steam":"高壓蒸汽","Still-warm low wines from the last run":"上一次蒸餾留下、仍溫熱的低度酒","Condensers usually use cold water, constantly refreshed so it stays cold.":"冷凝器通常使用冷水，並不斷更新以保持低溫。","High-pressure steam is for heating, not cooling. Spirit and low wines are liquids to distil, not coolants.":"高壓蒸汽是用來加熱的，不是冷卻。烈酒和低度酒是待蒸餾的液體，不是冷卻液。","In the second distillation described, how many collecting tanks are used, and for what?":"在所描述的第二次蒸餾中，使用幾個收集槽？各做什麼用？","Two: one for heads and tails, one for the heart":"兩個：一個裝酒頭和酒尾，一個裝酒心","Just one, for the whole flow":"只有一個，裝全部酒液","Three: heads, heart and tails kept apart for good":"三個：酒頭、酒心和酒尾永久分開","Two: one for low wines, one for the pot's watery residue":"兩個：一個裝低度酒，一個裝壺身的含水殘液","Heads and tails share one tank; the heart goes into another.":"酒頭和酒尾共用一個槽；酒心進入另一個槽。","Heads and tails go together because they share the same fate: going back into the next second distillation. The watery residue is drained and discarded, and low wines are the product of the first distillation.":"酒頭和酒尾放在一起，因為它們的去向相同：回到下一次的第二次蒸餾。含水殘液會被排掉丟棄，低度酒則是第一次蒸餾的產物。","How long does heart collection usually last in the second distillation?":"第二次蒸餾中，酒心通常收集多久？","A few seconds":"幾秒鐘","Several days, until the flow smells of solvent again":"好幾天，直到酒液再次出現溶劑味","The heart is collected for several hours, until the cheesy, plastic notes of the tails appear.":"酒心會收集好幾個小時，直到出現酒尾的乳酪、塑膠氣息。","The 10–15 minutes are the length of the heads. At the end of the heart it is not solvent that returns but the less volatile tails.":"10–15 分鐘是酒頭的長度。酒心結束時出現的不是溶劑味，而是較不易揮發的酒尾。","What does the bubble cap do on a column-still plate?":"柱式蒸餾器蒸餾板上的泡罩有什麼作用？","It forces vapour through the liquid on the plate":"迫使蒸氣穿過蒸餾板上的液體","It carries overflowing liquid to the plate below":"把溢出的液體送到下一層蒸餾板","It cools the vapour back into liquid, like a condenser":"像冷凝器一樣把蒸氣冷卻成液體","It lets the distiller look inside the column":"讓蒸餾師觀察蒸餾柱內部","The cap makes vapour bubble through the liquid, keeping it boiling.":"泡罩讓蒸氣在液體中冒泡通過，使液體保持沸騰。","Moving liquid downwards is the downcomer's job. The portholes are for looking inside. The bubble cap does not cool anything: in fact the vapour's heat keeps the liquid on the plate boiling.":"把液體往下送是降液管的工作。觀察窗是用來看內部的。泡罩不會冷卻任何東西：事實上，蒸氣的熱讓蒸餾板上的液體保持沸騰。","What is the downcomer for?":"降液管有什麼用途？","It sends overflowing liquid down to the plate below":"把溢出的液體送到下一層蒸餾板","It sends vapour up to the plate above":"把蒸氣送到上一層蒸餾板","It draws the heads off the top of the column":"從蒸餾柱頂部抽出酒頭","It injects high-pressure steam into the base":"把高壓蒸汽注入底部","When a plate fills up, the liquid overflows down the downcomer.":"蒸餾板滿了之後，液體就經降液管往下溢流。","The liquid going down is mostly water and less volatile fractions. Vapour rises instead through the central hole and bubble cap. Heads and heating steam have their own outlets and inlets.":"往下流的液體大部分是水和較不易揮發的餾分。蒸氣則是經由中央的孔和泡罩上升。酒頭和加熱用的蒸汽各有自己的出口和入口。","Where does distillation happen in a column still?":"在柱式蒸餾器中，蒸餾發生在哪裡？","On every plate at the same time":"在每一層蒸餾板上同時進行","Only in the base, the hottest part":"只在最熱的底部","Only on the top plate, near the summit":"只在靠近頂端的最上層蒸餾板","First in the base and then, once finished, on the next plate":"先在底部，完成後再到下一層蒸餾板","Each plate is a small distillation and they all run together.":"每一層蒸餾板都是一次小型蒸餾，而且全部同時進行。","It is this simultaneity that makes the column so efficient: there is no need to wait for one distillation to end before another begins. The base supplies the heat, but separation happens over the whole height of the tower.":"正是這種同時性讓蒸餾柱如此有效率：不必等一次蒸餾結束才開始另一次。底部提供熱，但分離發生在整座塔的高度上。","Why does the fermented liquid enter the column already pre-heated?":"為什麼發酵液進入蒸餾柱時已經預熱？","To keep the base, the hottest part, close to boiling":"讓最熱的底部保持接近沸騰","To kill any yeast still alive":"殺死任何還活著的酵母","To convert the last starch into sugar":"把最後的澱粉轉化為糖","To give it colour before distillation":"在蒸餾前為它上色","The base powers the whole column, so incoming liquid must be nearly boiling.":"底部為整座蒸餾柱提供動力，所以進入的液體必須接近沸騰。","If it came in cold, the base would cool and the column's balance would break. Starch conversion happens before fermentation, and colour never arises during distillation.":"如果進來的是冷液體，底部會降溫，蒸餾柱的平衡就會被打破。澱粉轉化發生在發酵之前，蒸餾過程中也絕不會產生顏色。","Where are the tails drawn off in a column still?":"在柱式蒸餾器中，酒尾從哪裡抽出？","From one of the lower plates":"從較低的某一層蒸餾板","From the top of the column":"從蒸餾柱頂部","From the plate just below the top, with the heads":"從頂部正下方的蒸餾板，與酒頭一起","From the condenser, at the end of each batch":"從冷凝器，在每一批結束時","Less volatile fractions concentrate low down and are taken off there.":"較不易揮發的餾分集中在低處，並在那裡取出。","The more volatile heads rise towards the top and are taken off near there. A column does not work in batches, so there is no 'end of batch': tails leave as a constant flow.":"較易揮發的酒頭往頂部上升，並在靠近頂部處取出。蒸餾柱不是批次運作，所以沒有「一批結束」：酒尾以持續的流量排出。","When is a column still said to be 'in balance'?":"什麼時候說柱式蒸餾器處於「平衡」狀態？","When volume in equals volume out":"進入的體積等於流出的體積時","When every plate has the same alcoholic strength":"每一層蒸餾板的酒精濃度都相同時","When the spirit coming out reaches 40% abv":"流出的烈酒達到 40% abv 時","When the column is stopped for routine cleaning":"蒸餾柱停機做例行清潔時","If what goes in equals what comes out, the column can run continuously.":"如果進去的等於出來的，蒸餾柱就能連續運轉。","Plates have different strengths: that is exactly what separates the fractions along the column. 40% is a bottling strength, not a distillation strength. A stopped column is not working at all.":"各層蒸餾板的濃度不同：這正是沿著蒸餾柱分離餾分的原因。40% 是裝瓶濃度，不是蒸餾濃度。停機的蒸餾柱根本沒有在運作。","Why can a column still reach 96% abv when a pot still cannot?":"為什麼柱式蒸餾器能達到 96% abv，壺式蒸餾器卻不行？","It need not recover all of one batch's alcohol before the next":"它不必在下一批之前回收一批中所有的酒精","It uses a stronger fermented liquid, around 40% abv":"它使用較濃的發酵液，大約 40% abv","It is always made of copper":"它一定是銅製的","It is heated by direct fire, which concentrates ethanol more":"它用直火加熱，更能濃縮乙醇","Ethanol rises and water falls continuously, with no need to dilute to recover each batch.":"乙醇持續上升、水持續下降，不必為了回收每一批而稀釋。","In a pot still, lots of water is collected so as not to lose alcohol. A column, with enough plates, concentrates ethanol plate after plate. The fermented liquid is around 10% in both cases, and steam heating is the norm.":"在壺式蒸餾器中，為了不損失酒精會收集到大量的水。蒸餾柱只要蒸餾板夠多，就能一層一層地濃縮乙醇。兩種情況下發酵液都是 10% 左右，蒸汽加熱則是常態。","Which of these spirits, although column-distilled, has a medium or pronounced aroma?":"下列哪一種烈酒雖然用蒸餾柱蒸餾，卻有中等或明顯的香氣？","Bourbon is column-distilled to a fairly low strength and keeps plenty of character.":"Bourbon 用蒸餾柱蒸餾到相當低的濃度，保有豐富的特色。","Like Armagnac and rhum agricole, Bourbon shows that a column can make expressive spirits. Vodka and neutral spirit are made at 95–96% abv; light rums are distilled at around 90%, with a light aroma.":"和 Armagnac、rhum agricole 一樣，Bourbon 說明了蒸餾柱也能做出表現力強的烈酒。伏特加和中性烈酒在 95–96% abv 製成；清淡型蘭姆酒蒸餾到約 90%，香氣清淡。","What style results from drawing the heart from a plate at about 90% abv?":"從大約 90% abv 的蒸餾板抽取酒心，會得到什麼風格？","Medium, identical to a pot-still spirit":"中等，與壺式蒸餾烈酒完全相同","At around 90% abv few congeners remain and the aroma is light.":"在大約 90% abv 時留下的同屬物很少，香氣清淡。","This is the style of some light rums and Scottish grain whisky. For a neutral spirit you need 95–96%. A pot still cannot reach 90%, so the comparison does not hold.":"這是某些清淡型蘭姆酒和蘇格蘭穀物威士忌的風格。中性烈酒需要 95–96%。壺式蒸餾器達不到 90%，所以這個比較不成立。","Which statement about column stills is true?":"關於柱式蒸餾器，下列哪一項正確？","It can make spirits from neutral to pronounced":"能做出從中性到香氣明顯的各種烈酒","It only ever makes neutral spirits, suitable only for vodka":"永遠只能做中性烈酒，只適合伏特加","It cannot go above 75% abv":"無法超過 75% abv","It must be emptied after every distillation":"每次蒸餾後都必須清空","It depends on which plate, and so which strength, the heart is drawn from.":"這取決於從哪一層蒸餾板、也就是在哪個濃度抽取酒心。","Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole prove that a column does not mean neutrality. It can go well above 75%, up to 96%. It runs continuously, without being emptied every cycle.":"Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 證明了蒸餾柱不等於中性。它可以遠高於 75%，高達 96%。它連續運轉，不必每個循環都清空。","How does a heat exchanger work on a column still?":"柱式蒸餾器上的熱交換器如何運作？","Steam heats outside pipes without touching the liquid":"蒸汽加熱外部管路，不接觸液體","Steam is mixed straight into the fermented liquid in every column":"在每一座蒸餾柱中，蒸汽都直接混入發酵液","A gas flame heats the bottom of the column":"瓦斯火焰加熱蒸餾柱底部","Cold water cools the top of the column":"冷水冷卻蒸餾柱頂部","Heat passes through the metal pipework: steam and liquid stay apart.":"熱透過金屬管路傳遞：蒸汽和液體保持分開。","Boiling liquid from the base circulates through outside pipes heated by high-pressure steam. Direct steam injection exists, but only in some larger columns, not all. Direct flames are not the usual way to heat columns.":"底部沸騰的液體在外部管路中循環，由高壓蒸汽加熱。直接注入蒸汽的做法確實存在，但只見於某些較大的蒸餾柱，不是全部。直接火焰不是加熱蒸餾柱的常見方式。","Why are the heads collected near the top of the column?":"為什麼酒頭在靠近蒸餾柱頂部處收集？","They are the most volatile fractions and rise highest":"它們是最易揮發的餾分，升得最高","They are the heaviest fractions and float":"它們是最重的餾分，會浮起來","They are pushed up by the water coming down":"它們被往下流的水推上去","They contain most of the column's water":"它們含有蒸餾柱中大部分的水","Because they boil before ethanol, the heads reach the very top.":"因為比乙醇先沸騰，酒頭會到達最頂端。","Each congener concentrates at the level where it becomes the least volatile, and the most volatile fractions of all reach the top. Water, by contrast, falls to the base and becomes waste. Heads are usually drawn from a plate just below the top.":"每種同屬物都集中在它成為最不易揮發者的那個高度，而最易揮發的餾分會到達頂部。水則落到底部成為廢液。酒頭通常從頂部正下方的蒸餾板抽出。","A distillery wants a characterful spirit but only has a column still. What should it do?":"一家蒸餾廠想要有特色的烈酒，卻只有柱式蒸餾器。應該怎麼做？","Draw the heart from a lower-strength plate":"從濃度較低的蒸餾板抽取酒心","Draw the heart from the highest plate, as close to the top as possible":"從最高的蒸餾板抽取酒心，盡量靠近頂部","Add more plates to raise the strength":"增加蒸餾板來提高濃度","Give up: it cannot be done in a column":"放棄：蒸餾柱做不到","At lower strength, around 75%, plenty of congeners remain, so more aroma.":"在較低的濃度（75% 左右）會保留大量同屬物，所以香氣更多。","The higher the draw-off, the higher the strength and the more neutral the spirit; adding plates pushes the same way. Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole show that a column can give plenty of character.":"抽取的位置越高，濃度越高，烈酒也越中性；增加蒸餾板的效果也是同一個方向。Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 說明了蒸餾柱也能做出豐富的特色。","What leaves from the base of a column still?":"從柱式蒸餾器底部排出的是什麼？","Watery liquid waste":"含水的廢液","The solvent-smelling heads":"帶溶劑氣味的酒頭","The heart at 96% abv":"96% abv 的酒心","Vapour heading to the condenser":"前往冷凝器的蒸氣","Watery liquid is drained from the base, the lowest and hottest part.":"含水的液體從底部排出，那是最低也最熱的部分。","Water is the least volatile fraction and sinks to the bottom. Heads and high-strength hearts are found higher up, where the vapour is most alcoholic.":"水是最不易揮發的餾分，會沉到底部。酒頭和高濃度的酒心在更高的位置，那裡的蒸氣酒精濃度最高。","Why are column stills, though 'continuous', stopped from time to time?":"柱式蒸餾器雖然是「連續式」的，為什麼還是要不時停機？","For cleaning":"為了清潔","To empty out the heads collected in the batch":"為了清出這一批收集到的酒頭","To run the second distillation with the low wines":"為了用低度酒進行第二次蒸餾","To let the liquid rest on the plates":"為了讓液體在蒸餾板上靜置","In theory they can run forever; in practice they are stopped for cleaning.":"理論上它們可以永遠運轉；實際上會停機清潔。","Batches, low wines and second distillations belong to the pot-still world. In a column, heads leave as a constant flow, with no need to wait for a cycle to end.":"批次、低度酒和第二次蒸餾屬於壺式蒸餾器的世界。在蒸餾柱中，酒頭以持續的流量排出，不必等一個循環結束。","On a column plate, compared with the boiling liquid, the vapour rising to the next plate is…":"在蒸餾柱的蒸餾板上，與沸騰的液體相比，升往上一層的蒸氣……","Richer in volatile fractions":"含有更多易揮發的餾分","Richer in water":"含有更多水","Identical in make-up":"組成完全相同","Richer in cheesy, plastic-smelling tails":"含有更多帶乳酪、塑膠氣味的酒尾","As in any distillation, vapour concentrates the more volatile fractions.":"和任何蒸餾一樣，蒸氣會濃縮較易揮發的餾分。","That is why the vapour powers an even more concentrated distillation on the plate above. Water and tails, being less volatile, stay in the liquid and go down the downcomer.":"所以這些蒸氣會在上一層蒸餾板推動一次更濃縮的蒸餾。水和酒尾較不易揮發，留在液體中並經降液管往下流。","What are the porthole windows along a column still for?":"柱式蒸餾器上的觀察窗有什麼用途？","To watch what is happening on each plate":"觀察每一層蒸餾板上的情況","To let carbon dioxide escape":"讓二氧化碳散逸","To draw off the heads":"抽出酒頭","To let in air that oxidises the spirit and adds aromas":"讓空氣進入，使烈酒氧化並增添香氣","The portholes let the distiller see and monitor each plate.":"觀察窗讓蒸餾師可以查看並監控每一層蒸餾板。","Carbon dioxide is released during fermentation, before distillation. Heads are drawn off through a dedicated outlet near the top. The oxidation that enriches aromas happens in barrels, not in the column.":"二氧化碳是在蒸餾之前的發酵過程中釋放的。酒頭經由靠近頂部的專用出口抽出。能豐富香氣的氧化發生在桶中，不是在蒸餾柱裡。","Which is the hottest part of a working column still?":"運轉中的柱式蒸餾器，哪個部分最熱？","The base":"底部","The top":"頂部","The plate the heads come from":"抽出酒頭的那層蒸餾板","The middle plate, halfway up the tower":"位於塔身一半高度的中間蒸餾板","The base is the hottest zone and its heat powers the whole column.":"底部是最熱的區域，它的熱推動整座蒸餾柱。","Going up, the temperature drops because the vapours become richer in volatile fractions, which boil at lower temperatures. That is why the heads come out at the top and water stays at the bottom. Incoming liquid is pre-heated precisely so as not to cool the base.":"越往上溫度越低，因為蒸氣含有越來越多易揮發的餾分，它們的沸點較低。所以酒頭從頂部出來，水留在底部。進入的液體之所以預熱，正是為了不讓底部降溫。","Where do the vapours rising through a column plate pass?":"上升通過蒸餾板的蒸氣從哪裡經過？","Through the large hole in the centre of the plate":"經過蒸餾板中央的大孔","Through the downcomer":"經過降液管","Through the porthole windows":"經過觀察窗","Through outside pipes that bypass the plate completely":"經過完全繞過蒸餾板的外部管路","Vapours rise from below through the large central hole, covered by the bubble cap.":"蒸氣從下方經由中央的大孔上升，大孔上方蓋著泡罩。","The bubble cap then forces them through the liquid on the plate. The downcomer is for the opposite path, liquid going down. Portholes are only for watching, and vapour bypassing the plate would distil nothing.":"泡罩接著迫使它們穿過蒸餾板上的液體。降液管走的是相反的路徑，讓液體往下流。觀察窗只用來觀看，而繞過蒸餾板的蒸氣什麼也蒸餾不了。","What keeps the liquid on each plate boiling?":"什麼讓每一層蒸餾板上的液體保持沸騰？","The heat of the vapours passing through it":"穿過液體的蒸氣所帶的熱","A flame under each plate":"每層蒸餾板下方的火焰","The cold water from the condenser":"來自冷凝器的冷水","An electric element inside each bubble cap":"每個泡罩內的電熱元件","Hot vapours rising from below give up heat to the liquid on the plate and keep it boiling.":"從下方上升的高溫蒸氣把熱傳給蒸餾板上的液體，讓它保持沸騰。","All the energy comes from the base, the hottest part; from there heat climbs plate by plate with the vapours. There are no flames or elements on individual plates, and cold water condenses rather than heats.":"所有能量都來自最熱的底部；熱從那裡隨蒸氣一層一層往上。個別的蒸餾板上沒有火焰或加熱元件，冷水則是用來冷凝，不是加熱。","What is the liquid going down the downcomer mainly made of?":"經降液管往下流的液體主要由什麼組成？","Water and the least volatile fractions":"水和最不易揮發的餾分","Fresh fermented liquid just fed in at the top":"剛從頂部注入的新鮮發酵液","The plate fills with water and the least volatile fractions; when it overflows, the downcomer takes them to the plate below.":"蒸餾板上積滿水和最不易揮發的餾分；溢出時，降液管把它們帶到下一層蒸餾板。","Ethanol and the heads, being more volatile, tend to rise with the vapours. In the simplified column the fermented liquid enters at the base, not the top.":"乙醇和酒頭較易揮發，傾向隨蒸氣上升。在簡化的蒸餾柱中，發酵液從底部進入，不是頂部。","What powers the distillation on the plate above?":"什麼推動上一層蒸餾板的蒸餾？","The vapours rising from the plate below":"從下一層蒸餾板上升的蒸氣","The liquid coming down the downcomer":"經降液管流下來的液體","The condenser at the top of the column":"蒸餾柱頂部的冷凝器","Heat from the lit portholes":"有照明的觀察窗發出的熱","Each plate's vapours, richer in volatile fractions, rise and boil the liquid on the plate above.":"每一層蒸餾板的蒸氣含有更多易揮發的餾分，上升後讓上一層蒸餾板的液體沸騰。","It is a chain: each plate gets heat and vapour from the one below. Downcomer liquid goes down and carries no heat upward. The condenser cools; it does not heat.":"這是一條鏈：每層蒸餾板都從下一層得到熱和蒸氣。降液管的液體往下流，不會把熱往上帶。冷凝器是冷卻的，不是加熱的。","Which description of the flows in a working column is correct?":"下列哪一項正確描述了運轉中蒸餾柱的流動？","Vapour rises, liquid falls":"蒸氣上升，液體下降","Liquid rises, vapour falls":"液體上升，蒸氣下降","Everything rises to the top":"所有東西都升到頂部","Nothing moves until a cut is made, as in a pot still":"和壺式蒸餾器一樣，切取之前什麼都不動","There is a constant flow of vapour up and liquid down through the plates.":"蒸氣持續往上、液體持續往下，穿過各層蒸餾板。","Ethanol goes up and water comes down, so the fractions separate along the height. A column has no time-based cuts like a pot still: fractions leave continuously from different points.":"乙醇往上、水往下，所以餾分沿著高度分離。蒸餾柱不像壺式蒸餾器那樣按時間切取：餾分從不同位置連續排出。","Where are the heads usually drawn off in a column still?":"在柱式蒸餾器中，酒頭通常從哪裡抽出？","From a plate just below the top":"從頂部正下方的蒸餾板","From the base":"從底部","From one of the lowest plates":"從最低的幾層蒸餾板之一","From the downcomer of the middle plate, halfway up":"從位於一半高度的中間蒸餾板的降液管","The most volatile fractions rise to the top; the distiller takes a continuous flow of heads from a plate just below it.":"最易揮發的餾分升到頂部；蒸餾師從頂部正下方的蒸餾板持續取出酒頭。","Watery waste leaves from the base and tails are drained from low plates. The heart is drawn from whichever plate gives the desired strength.":"含水的廢液從底部排出，酒尾從低層蒸餾板排出。酒心則從能得到所需濃度的那層蒸餾板抽取。","Besides heat exchangers, how are some large column stills heated?":"除了熱交換器，一些大型柱式蒸餾器還用什麼方式加熱？","By injecting steam straight into the still":"把蒸汽直接注入蒸餾器","With a wood fire under the base":"在底部下方燒柴火","With hot water from a worm tub condenser":"用蟲桶冷凝器的熱水","With electric elements fitted on every bubble cap":"在每個泡罩上裝電熱元件","In some larger stills steam is injected directly into the column.":"在一些較大的蒸餾器中，蒸汽直接注入蒸餾柱。","Columns are typically steam-heated: either via a heat exchanger, where steam and liquid never touch, or by direct injection. Wood fires, worm tubs and plate heaters are not part of this picture.":"蒸餾柱通常用蒸汽加熱：透過熱交換器（蒸汽和液體不接觸），或直接注入。柴火、蟲桶冷凝器和蒸餾板加熱器都不在其中。","Why does a column with few plates struggle to make neutral spirit?":"為什麼蒸餾板少的蒸餾柱很難做出中性烈酒？","Fewer plates mean fewer distillations and a lower top strength":"蒸餾板越少，蒸餾次數越少，最高濃度也越低","Because short columns have no hot base":"因為矮蒸餾柱沒有高溫的底部","Because extra plates add aromas to the spirit":"因為多加的蒸餾板會為烈酒增添香氣","Because without many plates a column cannot run continuously":"因為沒有很多蒸餾板，蒸餾柱就無法連續運轉","Each plate is one distillation: enough plates are needed to climb to 95–96% abv.":"每一層蒸餾板就是一次蒸餾：需要足夠的蒸餾板才能升到 95–96% abv。","Even a short column has a hot base and runs continuously. Plates add no aromas; on the contrary, more plates mean more congeners left behind.":"即使是矮蒸餾柱也有高溫的底部，也是連續運轉。蒸餾板不會增添香氣；相反地，蒸餾板越多，留下不取的同屬物越多。","Compared with a tall column, what characterises a short column with few plates?":"與高蒸餾柱相比，蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱有什麼特點？","A lower top strength and a spirit with more congeners":"最高濃度較低，烈酒含較多同屬物","It always makes purer neutral spirit":"做出的中性烈酒一定更純","It works in batches like a pot still":"像壺式蒸餾器一樣以批次運作","It never needs to draw off heads, tails or watery waste":"從不需要抽出酒頭、酒尾或含水廢液","With fewer plates the column cannot reach the highest strengths, so the spirit keeps more character.":"蒸餾板較少時，蒸餾柱達不到最高的濃度，所以烈酒保有更多特色。","The number of plates is what allows 96%, so neutral spirit needs tall columns. Even a short column runs continuously and separates heads, tails and waste.":"蒸餾板的數量是達到 96% 的關鍵，所以中性烈酒需要高蒸餾柱。即使是矮蒸餾柱也連續運轉，並分離酒頭、酒尾和廢液。","What is the main operating difference between a column and a pot still?":"蒸餾柱和壺式蒸餾器在運作上的主要差別是什麼？","The column runs non-stop; the pot still is filled and emptied":"蒸餾柱不停運轉；壺式蒸餾器要裝料和清空","The column works in batches; the pot still runs continuously":"蒸餾柱以批次運作；壺式蒸餾器連續運轉","The column uses no heat":"蒸餾柱不用熱","The column does not separate heads and tails; they all end up in the spirit":"蒸餾柱不分離酒頭和酒尾；它們全都進入烈酒","The column takes a constant feed and produces continuously; the pot still works batch by batch.":"蒸餾柱持續進料並連續產出；壺式蒸餾器則是一批一批地運作。","The column also needs heat, usually steam, and does separate heads and tails, drawing them continuously from different plates. It only stops for periodic cleaning.":"蒸餾柱同樣需要熱，通常是蒸汽，而且確實會分離酒頭和酒尾，從不同的蒸餾板連續抽出。它只在定期清潔時停機。","Each congener reaches a plate where it is the least volatile. What happens above that plate?":"每種同屬物都會到達它成為最不易揮發者的那層蒸餾板。在那層之上會怎麼樣？","Its concentration falls away quickly":"它的濃度迅速下降","Its concentration keeps rising":"它的濃度持續上升","It turns into ethanol":"它變成乙醇","It stays the same on every plate up to the top":"一直到頂部，每層蒸餾板都保持不變","Above the plate where it is least volatile, that congener gets left behind and almost disappears.":"在它最不易揮發的那層蒸餾板之上，這種同屬物就被留下，幾乎消失。","This spreads congeners along the height: the most volatile at the top, the least volatile low down. So the higher the draw, the fewer aromas. Congeners do not turn into ethanol.":"這讓同屬物沿著高度分布：最易揮發的在頂部，最不易揮發的在低處。所以抽取位置越高，香氣越少。同屬物不會變成乙醇。","In a column with 40 plates, what can the distiller choose?":"在一座有 40 層蒸餾板的蒸餾柱中，蒸餾師可以選擇什麼？","Which plate to draw the heart from":"從哪一層蒸餾板抽取酒心","How many hours the heads should last":"酒頭要持續幾個小時","The colour of the spirit":"烈酒的顏色","How much sugar to send into the vapour to sweeten the heart":"要讓多少糖進入蒸氣來為酒心增甜","In theory the distiller can draw the heart from the plate with the strength, and so the style, required.":"理論上，蒸餾師可以從具有所需濃度（也就是所需風格）的蒸餾板抽取酒心。","In a column the heads leave continuously, not for a set number of hours. The spirit is colourless and dry: any colour or sugar comes later, and sugar does not enter the vapour.":"在蒸餾柱中，酒頭是連續排出的，不是持續固定的幾個小時。烈酒無色且不甜：顏色或糖都是之後才有的，而且糖不會進入蒸氣。","One spirit drawn at 75% from a column, another collected at 75% in a pot still. How will they compare?":"一款烈酒從蒸餾柱在 75% 抽取，另一款在壺式蒸餾器中於 75% 收集。兩者相比如何？","Very similar in aroma intensity":"香氣強度非常相近","The column one will be neutral":"蒸餾柱的那款會是中性的","The pot-still one will be neutral":"壺式蒸餾器的那款會是中性的","The column one will already be coloured, the pot-still one colourless":"蒸餾柱的那款已有顏色，壺式蒸餾器的那款無色","At the same 75% both keep plenty of congeners: a medium or pronounced aroma.":"同樣在 75% 時，兩者都保留大量同屬物：香氣中等或明顯。","The collection strength matters more than the type of still. Neutrality only comes at about 95–96%. Every newly made spirit is colourless.":"收集濃度比蒸餾器的類型更重要。中性只有在大約 95–96% 才出現。所有新酒都是無色的。","Which of these column-made spirits is NOT considered characterful?":"下列用蒸餾柱製作的烈酒中，哪一種不被認為有鮮明特色？","Armagnac":"Armagnac","Bourbon":"Bourbon","Scottish grain whisky is distilled to about 90%, so its aroma is light.":"蘇格蘭穀物威士忌蒸餾到大約 90%，所以香氣清淡。","Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole are drawn at lower strengths and stay aromatic though column-made. This shows a column can give any style, from pronounced to neutral.":"Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 在較低的濃度抽取，雖然用蒸餾柱製作，仍然香氣豐富。這說明蒸餾柱能做出任何風格，從香氣明顯到中性都可以。","In a column that is already running, where is there boiling liquid?":"在已經運轉的蒸餾柱中，哪裡有沸騰的液體？","On every plate and in the base":"每一層蒸餾板和底部","Only in the base":"只有底部","Only on the top plate":"只有最上層蒸餾板","Only in the condenser, where vapours become liquid again":"只有冷凝器，蒸氣在那裡重新變成液體","When the column is running, every plate and the base hold boiling liquid.":"蒸餾柱運轉時，每一層蒸餾板和底部都有沸騰的液體。","This is exactly what allows a distillation on every plate at the same time. The condenser, by contrast, cools vapours: nothing boils there.":"這正是讓每層蒸餾板能同時進行蒸餾的原因。冷凝器則是冷卻蒸氣：那裡沒有東西在沸騰。","For a simple water-ethanol mix in a column, how does strength change going up plate by plate?":"對蒸餾柱中單純的水和乙醇混合液來說，一層一層往上時濃度如何變化？","It increases at every plate":"每一層都升高","It decreases at every plate":"每一層都降低","It stays the same on every plate":"每一層都相同","It rises to halfway, then falls back to 10% at the top":"升到一半高度，然後在頂部降回 10%","Each plate selects and concentrates ethanol, so strength climbs plate after plate.":"每一層蒸餾板都篩選並濃縮乙醇，所以濃度一層一層攀升。","The distiller can draw liquid from whichever plate has reached the required strength. With enough plates it reaches 96%. Water, meanwhile, flows down to the base.":"蒸餾師可以從達到所需濃度的任何一層蒸餾板抽取液體。蒸餾板夠多就能達到 96%。同時，水往下流到底部。","In a running column with 30 plates, how many distillations happen at once?":"在一座運轉中、有 30 層蒸餾板的蒸餾柱裡，同時發生幾次蒸餾？","About 30, one per plate":"大約 30 次，每層蒸餾板一次","Just one, as in a pot still":"只有一次，和壺式蒸餾器一樣","Two, as in double distillation":"兩次，和二次蒸餾一樣","None: distillation only happens in the condenser at the top":"沒有：蒸餾只發生在頂部的冷凝器","A distillation takes place on every plate, and they all happen at the same time.":"每一層蒸餾板上都進行一次蒸餾，而且全部同時發生。","This is the key point of a column: many simultaneous, continuous distillations. A pot still does one at a time. The condenser turns vapour back into liquid; it does not distil.":"這是蒸餾柱的關鍵：許多同時進行、連續不斷的蒸餾。壺式蒸餾器一次只做一次蒸餾。冷凝器把蒸氣變回液體，並不蒸餾。","Why does a column separate fractions more precisely than a pot still?":"為什麼蒸餾柱分離餾分比壺式蒸餾器更精確？","Simultaneous distillations spread them along its height":"同時進行的蒸餾讓餾分沿著高度分布","Because it is always made of copper":"因為它一定是銅製的","Because it uses direct fire, which is more precise than steam":"因為它使用直火，比蒸汽更精確","Because it only distils very sugary liquids":"因為它只蒸餾含糖量很高的液體","With continuous, simultaneous distillations on every plate, each fraction concentrates at a particular height.":"每層蒸餾板上連續、同時進行蒸餾，每種餾分就集中在特定的高度。","So the distiller can draw heads, heart and tails from different points very precisely. Columns are usually steam-heated and distil fermented, not sugary, liquids.":"所以蒸餾師可以非常精確地從不同位置抽出酒頭、酒心和酒尾。蒸餾柱通常用蒸汽加熱，蒸餾的是發酵過的液體，不是含糖液體。","Which statement about a column's outlets is FALSE?":"關於蒸餾柱的出口，下列哪一項是錯誤的？","The heads leave from the base":"酒頭從底部排出","The tails are drained from a low plate":"酒尾從低層蒸餾板排出","Watery waste leaves from the base":"含水的廢液從底部排出","The heart is drawn from the plate with the strength wanted":"酒心從具有所需濃度的蒸餾板抽取","The heads, the most volatile fractions, leave near the top, not from the base.":"酒頭是最易揮發的餾分，從靠近頂部處排出，不是底部。","The other three are correct: tails from low plates, watery waste from the base, heart from the chosen plate. If what goes in equals what comes out, the column is in balance.":"其他三項都正確：酒尾來自低層蒸餾板，含水廢液來自底部，酒心來自選定的蒸餾板。如果進去的等於出來的，蒸餾柱就處於平衡。","In the simplified column, where does the pre-heated fermented liquid enter?":"在簡化的蒸餾柱中，預熱過的發酵液從哪裡進入？","Into the base":"進入底部","At the top":"在頂部","Into the condenser":"進入冷凝器","Straight into the heart tank":"直接進入酒心的槽","The liquid flows continuously into the base, the hottest part, as close to boiling as possible.":"液體持續流入最熱的底部，溫度盡可能接近沸騰。","The energy powering the whole column comes from the base. The top is where the most volatile fractions gather, and the condenser and tank receive what has already been distilled.":"推動整座蒸餾柱的能量來自底部。頂部是最易揮發的餾分聚集的地方，冷凝器和槽接收的則是已經蒸餾過的東西。","Where is a 96% spirit drawn off compared with a 90% one?":"與 90% 的烈酒相比，96% 的烈酒從哪裡抽出？","From a higher plate":"從較高的蒸餾板","From a lower plate":"從較低的蒸餾板","From the same plate, but later in the day":"從同一層蒸餾板，但在當天較晚的時候","From the base, where the liquid is hottest and most concentrated":"從底部，那裡的液體最熱、最濃","Strength increases going up, so 96% is found higher than 90%.":"濃度越往上越高，所以 96% 的位置比 90% 高。","In a column, style depends on where you draw, not when: the process is continuous. The base is the hottest part but also the most watery, where waste leaves.":"在蒸餾柱中，風格取決於從哪裡抽取，而不是什麼時候：這個過程是連續的。底部最熱，但含水也最多，廢液就從那裡排出。","Which of these parts belongs to a column still?":"下列哪個零件屬於柱式蒸餾器？","The still head, olive-shaped in Cognac":"蒸餾器頂部，在 Cognac 呈橄欖形","The bubble cap, on the plates, forces vapour through the liquid: a typical column part.":"泡罩位於蒸餾板上，迫使蒸氣穿過液體：是典型的蒸餾柱零件。","Swan neck, lyne arm and still head are pot-still parts. The key column parts are heat source, plates, bubble caps and downcomers.":"天鵝頸、林恩臂和蒸餾器頂部是壺式蒸餾器的零件。蒸餾柱的關鍵零件是熱源、蒸餾板、泡罩和降液管。","In a column's heat exchanger, what circulates through the outside pipes?":"在蒸餾柱的熱交換器中，在外部管路裡循環的是什麼？","The column's boiling alcoholic liquid":"蒸餾柱中沸騰的含酒精液體","Cold water for condensing":"冷凝用的冷水","Tails to be recycled":"待回收的酒尾","The finished spirit, which then goes straight to bottle":"成品烈酒，之後直接裝瓶","The boiling liquid circulates through pipes outside the still, heated by high-pressure steam.":"沸騰的液體在蒸餾器外的管路中循環，由高壓蒸汽加熱。","Steam and liquid never touch: heat passes through the metal. Cold water belongs to the condenser. Spirit almost never goes straight to bottle: there is nearly always some finishing.":"蒸汽和液體絕不接觸：熱透過金屬傳遞。冷水屬於冷凝器。烈酒幾乎從不直接裝瓶：幾乎都會有一些收尾處理。","Moving up a working column still, how does the temperature change?":"在運轉中的柱式蒸餾器裡往上走，溫度如何變化？","It falls: the base is the hottest part":"下降：底部是最熱的部分","It rises: the top is the hottest part":"上升：頂部是最熱的部分","It is identical on every plate":"每一層蒸餾板都相同","It depends only on the air temperature in the still house":"只取決於蒸餾室的氣溫","The base is hottest; higher up are ever more volatile fractions that boil at lower temperatures.":"底部最熱；越往上是越易揮發的餾分，沸點越低。","That is why water and the least volatile compounds gather low and the heads at the top. Heat comes from the base and rises with the vapour, so temperature cannot be the same everywhere.":"所以水和最不易揮發的化合物聚集在低處，酒頭在頂部。熱來自底部並隨蒸氣上升，所以溫度不可能處處相同。","Compared with a pot still, how do the heads leave a column still?":"與壺式蒸餾器相比，酒頭如何離開柱式蒸餾器？","As a continuous flow, all the time":"以連續的流量，一直不停","Only during the first 10–15 minutes":"只在最初的 10–15 分鐘","Only at the end of the day, before cleaning":"只在一天結束、清潔之前","Never: in a column the heads stay in the heart and are never separated":"永遠不會：在蒸餾柱中酒頭留在酒心裡，從不分離","In a column the heads leave non-stop from a plate near the top, whereas in a pot still they come only at the start of a run.":"在蒸餾柱中，酒頭不停地從靠近頂部的蒸餾板排出；在壺式蒸餾器中，它們只在蒸餾開始時出現。","The same goes for the tails, drained continuously from a low plate. The 10–15 minutes apply to the pot still. A column separates fractions very precisely rather than leaving them in the heart.":"酒尾也是一樣，從低層蒸餾板連續排出。10–15 分鐘指的是壺式蒸餾器。蒸餾柱非常精確地分離餾分，而不是把它們留在酒心裡。","A distiller draws the heart at 95–96% from a tall column. What is this spirit suited to?":"一位蒸餾師從高蒸餾柱在 95–96% 抽取酒心。這款烈酒適合做什麼？","A vodka or a neutral base for flavouring":"伏特加，或用來調味的中性基酒","A Cognac":"Cognac","A very aromatic high-ester rum":"香氣非常濃郁的高酯蘭姆酒","A characterful malt whisky":"特色鮮明的麥芽威士忌","At 95–96% the spirit is neutral: ideal for vodka or as a base for flavoured spirits.":"在 95–96% 時烈酒是中性的：最適合做伏特加，或作為調味烈酒的基酒。","Cognac, malt whisky and high-ester rum need plenty of congeners and are made in pot stills at much lower strengths. At that strength nothing of their character would remain.":"Cognac、麥芽威士忌和高酯蘭姆酒需要大量同屬物，用壺式蒸餾器在低得多的濃度製作。在那樣的濃度下，它們的特色將蕩然無存。","Which statement about column still designs is true?":"關於柱式蒸餾器的設計，下列哪一項正確？","They vary a lot but all work on the same principles":"差異很大，但都依相同的原理運作","They are identical in every distillery":"每家蒸餾廠的都一模一樣","Only one type of plate is allowed by law":"法律只允許一種蒸餾板","Each design relies on a completely different physical principle":"每種設計依據的物理原理完全不同","Columns come in many shapes and plate designs, but all rely on continuous distillation across several plates.":"蒸餾柱有許多形狀和蒸餾板設計，但都依靠在多層蒸餾板上連續蒸餾。","The bubble-cap plate is a common design, not the only one. The principles stay the same: rising vapour, falling liquid, fractions separated along the height.":"泡罩蒸餾板是常見的設計，不是唯一的一種。原理始終相同：蒸氣上升、液體下降、餾分沿高度分離。","What are column stills typically heated with?":"柱式蒸餾器通常用什麼加熱？","Steam":"蒸汽","The direct flame of a gas burner":"瓦斯爐的直接火焰","Sunlight through the portholes":"透過觀察窗照進來的陽光","Hot water leaving the condenser":"從冷凝器流出的熱水","Column stills are usually steam-heated, through heat exchangers or, in larger ones, by direct injection.":"柱式蒸餾器通常用蒸汽加熱，透過熱交換器，或在較大的蒸餾器中直接注入。","Direct flame is typical of some pot stills, as in Cognac. Portholes are for watching the plates, and condenser water would not be hot enough to boil the base.":"直接火焰是某些壺式蒸餾器的典型做法，例如 Cognac。觀察窗是用來觀察蒸餾板的，冷凝器的水也不夠熱，無法讓底部沸騰。","In what order do post-distillation operations usually happen?":"蒸餾後處理通常依什麼順序進行？","Maturation, other flavours, blending, finishing":"熟成、其他風味、調和、收尾處理","Finishing, blending, maturation, other flavours":"收尾處理、調和、熟成、其他風味","Blending, finishing, other flavours, maturation":"調和、收尾處理、其他風味、熟成","Other flavours, finishing, maturation, blending":"其他風味、收尾處理、熟成、調和","First maturation, then flavouring, blending and finally finishing for the bottle.":"先熟成，再調味、調和，最後做裝瓶前的收尾處理。","Finishing, which covers dilution, colour, sugar and filtration, is always the last step before bottling. Not every spirit goes through every stage: it depends on the law and the producer's choices.":"收尾處理包括稀釋、調色、加糖和過濾，永遠是裝瓶前的最後一步。並非每種烈酒都經過每個階段：這取決於法規和生產者的選擇。","Which aromas typically come from oak?":"哪些香氣通常來自橡木？","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon, clove":"香草、椰子、肉桂、丁香","Pear, apple, banana":"梨、蘋果、香蕉","Solvent, nail varnish, glue":"溶劑、指甲油、膠水","Black pepper and earth, like cooked blue agave":"黑胡椒和土壤，像煮熟的藍色龍舌蘭","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon and clove are among the most common oak aromas.":"香草、椰子、肉桂和丁香是最常見的橡木香氣。","Fruit notes come rather from raw materials and fermentation, solvent notes from the heads. Earthy, peppery notes are typical of agave as a raw material, not of oak.":"水果氣息多半來自原料和發酵，溶劑氣息來自酒頭。土壤和胡椒氣息是龍舌蘭這種原料的典型特徵，不是橡木的。","What does 'rancio' mean in an aged spirit?":"在陳年烈酒中，「rancio」是什麼意思？","Leather and mushroom notes from oxygen and time":"氧氣和時間帶來的皮革和蘑菇氣息","A fault caused by a broken barrel":"桶子破損造成的缺陷","The solvent smell of the first fractions off the still":"蒸餾器最初餾分的溶劑氣味","Colour added with caramel":"用焦糖色添加的顏色","Over time, congeners react with oxygen to create leather and mushroom notes.":"隨著時間，同屬物與氧氣反應，產生皮革和蘑菇氣息。","Rancio is a prized feature of long-aged spirits, not a fault. A solvent smell belongs to the heads. Caramel only affects colour and has no taste.":"rancio 是長期陳年烈酒備受珍視的特徵，不是缺陷。溶劑氣味屬於酒頭。焦糖色只影響顏色，沒有味道。","What is the 'angels' share'?":"什麼是「天使的分享」（angels' share）？","Water and alcohol evaporating from the barrel":"從桶中蒸發的水和酒精","Spirit left soaked into the wood when the barrel is emptied":"清空桶子時仍滲在木頭裡的烈酒","Heads discarded during distillation":"蒸餾時丟棄的酒頭","The haze removed by chill-filtration":"冷凝過濾去除的混濁物","It is the water and ethanol that evaporate through the wood during maturation.":"它是熟成過程中透過木頭蒸發的水和乙醇。","This evaporation concentrates the remaining congeners, making very old spirits intense and complex. Liquid soaked into the wood matters instead when choosing a barrel's previous contents.":"這種蒸發會濃縮留下的同屬物，讓極老的烈酒濃郁而複雜。滲在木頭裡的液體，則是在選擇桶子先前裝過什麼時才有關係。","How does a barrel smooth away a young spirit's harshness?":"桶子如何讓年輕烈酒的粗糙感變得柔順？","The charred inner layer captures some congeners":"炙燒過的內層會抓住一些同屬物","The wood adds sugar to the spirit":"木頭為烈酒增添糖分","The wood lowers the strength by absorbing alcohol":"木頭吸收酒精而降低濃度","Oxygen turns all the ethanol into water":"氧氣把所有乙醇變成水","The carbon from the inside char or toast holds on to harsh congeners.":"內部炙燒或烘烤產生的碳會抓住粗糙的同屬物。","This layer, called char or toast, is created when the barrel is made. The wood adds no sugar and does not turn ethanol into water. Oxygen creates new aromas, such as rancio.":"這一層稱為炙燒層（char）或烘烤層（toast），是製桶時形成的。木頭不會增添糖分，也不會把乙醇變成水。氧氣會產生新的香氣，例如 rancio。","Which barrel gives the most colour and flavour to a spirit?":"哪一種桶為烈酒帶來最多顏色和風味？","A brand-new barrel":"全新的桶","A barrel already used three or four times":"已經用過三、四次的桶","A very old barrel with no aromas of its own left":"已經沒有自身香氣的極老的桶","A glass demijohn":"玻璃罈","A barrel gives most on its first use, then less each time.":"桶子第一次使用時給得最多，之後每次遞減。","A re-used barrel is not inferior: it gives less, which may be exactly what a delicate style needs. Glass is inert and gives neither colour nor flavour.":"重複使用的桶並不比較差：它給得較少，而這可能正是細緻風格所需要的。玻璃是惰性的，既不帶來顏色，也不帶來風味。","A producer puts a whisky into former wine barrels for a few months. Which factor is being used?":"一位生產者把威士忌放進裝過葡萄酒的桶中幾個月。運用的是哪一項因素？","The barrel's previous contents":"桶子先前裝過的東西","The warehouse temperature":"酒庫的溫度","Activated charcoal filtration, which strips aroma and colour":"活性碳過濾，會去除香氣和顏色","Wine left in the wood seeps out and adds flavour, sometimes a little colour.":"留在木頭裡的葡萄酒滲出來，增添風味，有時還有一點顏色。","This practice, called finishing, is common for some Scotch whiskies. Temperature affects the speed of maturation, not wine flavour. Activated charcoal would remove aromas rather than add them.":"這種做法稱為過桶（finishing），常見於某些 Scotch 威士忌。溫度影響的是熟成的速度，不是葡萄酒風味。活性碳會去除香氣，而不是增添。","Why does a Kentucky Bourbon tend to mature faster than a Scotch?":"為什麼肯塔基州的 Bourbon 往往比 Scotch 熟成得快？","Hot summers speed up exchanges between spirit and wood":"炎熱的夏天加快了烈酒與木頭之間的交換","The cool, damp climate slows evaporation and concentrates aromas faster":"涼爽潮濕的氣候減緩蒸發，並更快地濃縮香氣","Glass barrels are used":"使用玻璃桶","More caramel is added":"加了更多焦糖色","In heat the spirit moves in and out of the wood faster, extracting colour and flavour.":"在高溫下，烈酒更快地進出木頭，萃取出顏色和風味。","Kentucky has very hot summers and Scotland cooler ones, so Bourbon reaches maturity sooner and with a deeper colour. Caramel only changes colour, not maturation, and barrels are made of wood.":"肯塔基州夏天非常炎熱，蘇格蘭較涼爽，所以 Bourbon 更早成熟，顏色也更深。焦糖色只改變顏色，不影響熟成，而桶是木頭做的。","A spirit rests for a few weeks in a steel tank before bottling. What will it be like?":"一款烈酒裝瓶前在鋼槽中靜置幾週。它會是什麼樣子？","Colourless and almost unchanged":"無色，幾乎沒有變化","Golden, with vanilla notes":"金黃色，帶香草氣息","Amber, with the leather and mushroom notes of rancio":"琥珀色，帶 rancio 的皮革和蘑菇氣息","Sweeter, because the steel releases sugar":"更甜，因為鋼會釋出糖","Steel is inert: it adds no colour or flavour, and a short rest changes very little.":"鋼是惰性的：不增添顏色或風味，短暫靜置幾乎不會帶來改變。","Such a spirit is called 'unaged'. Vanilla, golden colour and rancio need wood and, for rancio, a long time. Steel releases no sugar.":"這樣的烈酒稱為「未陳年」。香草、金黃色和 rancio 需要木頭，rancio 還需要很長的時間。鋼不會釋出糖。","What happens to a spirit kept for many months in an inert vessel?":"在惰性容器中存放好幾個月的烈酒會怎麼樣？","It becomes smoother and fuller but stays colourless":"變得更柔順、更飽滿，但仍然無色","It turns golden":"變成金黃色","It develops strong vanilla and coconut notes":"發展出強烈的香草和椰子氣息","It loses half its volume by evaporating through the walls":"透過容器壁蒸發而損失一半的體積","After some months the texture changes, but the colour does not.":"幾個月後質地會改變，但顏色不會。","This evolution can carry on for years, though maturing spirits this way is rare. Colour and vanilla or coconut aromas come only from oak. Steel and glass do not let the spirit evaporate the way wood does.":"這種變化可以持續好幾年，不過用這種方式熟成烈酒很少見。顏色以及香草或椰子香氣只來自橡木。鋼和玻璃不像木頭那樣會讓烈酒蒸發。","Why are some very old Cognacs moved into glass demijohns?":"為什麼有些極老的 Cognac 會移到玻璃罈中？","To stop oxidation and concentration":"停止氧化和濃縮","To give them more colour":"讓顏色更深","To speed up maturation and get more oak notes":"加快熟成並得到更多橡木氣息","So they can be sold as 'unaged'":"這樣就能以「未陳年」販售","Glass is inert and halts development: the spirit stays as it is.":"玻璃是惰性的，會讓變化停止：烈酒維持原樣。","These precious reserves are then used sparingly in the finest blends. Glass adds no colour or flavour and speeds nothing up. Having already spent years in oak, they could not be called unaged.":"這些珍貴的庫存之後會少量用在最頂級的調和中。玻璃不增添顏色或風味，也不會加快任何過程。它們已經在橡木桶中度過多年，不可能稱為未陳年。","Which flavouring technique also extracts colour from botanicals?":"哪一種調味技術也會從植物性原料中萃取顏色？","Redistillation in a vacuum still at low temperature":"在真空蒸餾器中低溫再蒸餾","Activated charcoal filtration":"活性碳過濾","Maceration leaves botanicals in the alcohol, drawing out colour and a broad range of flavour.":"浸漬是把植物性原料留在酒精中，萃取出顏色和範圍廣泛的風味。","Colour is not volatile, so it does not pass through any distillation, even under vacuum. Activated charcoal, on the contrary, removes colour.":"顏色不具揮發性，所以無法通過任何蒸餾，即使在真空下也一樣。活性碳則相反，會去除顏色。","Why is very strong alcohol often diluted with water for maceration?":"為什麼浸漬時常把濃度很高的酒精加水稀釋？","Too-strong alcohol would extract unpleasant flavours":"濃度太高的酒精會萃取出不好的風味","To stop the botanical floating on the surface throughout the maceration":"防止植物性原料在整個浸漬過程中浮在表面","To reach selling strength straight away":"立刻達到販售濃度","Because the law forbids neutral spirit":"因為法律禁止使用中性烈酒","With alcohol that is too high, unwanted flavours are extracted too.":"酒精濃度太高時，不想要的風味也會被萃取出來。","Highly rectified alcohol is diluted so that only good flavours are extracted. Selling strength is set later, at finishing. Neutral spirit is in fact a common base for macerations and redistillations.":"高度精餾的酒精要經過稀釋，才能只萃取好的風味。販售濃度是之後在收尾階段才決定的。中性烈酒其實是浸漬和再蒸餾常用的基酒。","A producer wants to capture the fresh aroma of cucumber. Which equipment suits best?":"一位生產者想捕捉小黃瓜的清新香氣。哪一種設備最適合？","A vacuum still":"真空蒸餾器","A direct-fired still, like those used for Cognac":"直火蒸餾器，像 Cognac 使用的那種","An activated charcoal filter":"活性碳過濾器","Under vacuum, liquids boil at lower temperatures and delicate aromas are not damaged.":"在真空下，液體在較低的溫度沸騰，細緻的香氣不會受損。","The high temperatures of a normal still, especially a direct-fired one, damage fragile aromas like cucumber. Oak would add its own flavours, and activated charcoal would remove the very congeners being sought.":"一般蒸餾器的高溫，尤其是直火蒸餾器，會破壞小黃瓜這類脆弱的香氣。橡木會增添自己的風味，活性碳則會去除正想保留的同屬物。","What is the technique of blending bought-in artificial flavourings into a base spirit sometimes called?":"把外購的人工香料調入基酒的技術，有時稱為什麼？","Cold compounding means blending artificial flavours into the spirit, with no extraction or distillation.":"冷混法（cold compounding）是把人工香料調入烈酒，不經萃取或蒸餾。","Maceration and redistillation work with real botanicals or fruit. In whisky language, finishing means a final spell in barrels that held another liquid, such as wine.":"浸漬和再蒸餾使用的是真正的植物性原料或水果。在威士忌的用語中，過桶（finishing）指的是最後在裝過其他液體（例如葡萄酒）的桶中存放一段時間。","What are the two main goals of blending?":"調和的兩個主要目標是什麼？","Colour and sweetness":"顏色和甜味","Higher strength and fewer congeners in the end product":"讓最終產品濃度更高、同屬物更少","Speed and saving money":"速度和省錢","Blending gives the same product every time and builds complexity.":"調和讓產品每次都相同，並增加複雜度。","Colour and sweetness are adjusted in finishing; they are not the purpose of blending. Strength and congeners depend mainly on distillation. Blending in fact demands a wide choice and great care.":"顏色和甜味在收尾階段調整，不是調和的目的。濃度和同屬物主要取決於蒸餾。調和其實需要廣泛的選擇和極大的細心。","Why is blending for consistency especially important for oak-matured spirits?":"為什麼以一致性為目的的調和，對橡木桶熟成的烈酒特別重要？","Each barrel can give a very different result":"每個桶的結果可能非常不同","Barrels add varying amounts of sugar":"桶會增添不等量的糖","Wood turns the spirit into neutral spirit":"木頭把烈酒變成中性烈酒","The law requires at least a hundred barrels in every single batch":"法律規定每一批至少要用一百個桶","Differences between barrels can be considerable, and blending evens them out.":"桶與桶之間的差異可能相當大，調和能把它們拉平。","Age, previous contents and position in the warehouse make every barrel unique. Wood adds no sugar and does not make spirit neutral; it adds flavour. There is no legal minimum number of barrels.":"年數、先前裝過的東西和在酒庫中的位置，讓每個桶都獨一無二。木頭不會增添糖分，也不會讓烈酒變中性；它增添的是風味。法律沒有規定最少的桶數。","A blender adds a little very old spirit to a young one. What is the aim?":"一位調和師在年輕的烈酒中加入少量極老的烈酒。目的是什麼？","To create balance and complexity":"創造平衡和複雜度","To lower the young spirit's strength without using water":"不用水就降低年輕烈酒的濃度","To make it colourless":"讓它變成無色","To remove the need to filter":"省去過濾的需要","Old spirit brings depth and young spirit freshness: together they create new balance.":"老酒帶來深度，年輕的酒帶來清新：合在一起創造出新的平衡。","On its own a very old spirit can be too intense and a young one too simple. Strength is set with water during finishing; colour and filtration are separate matters.":"極老的烈酒單獨喝可能太濃郁，年輕的則太簡單。濃度是在收尾階段用水調整的；顏色和過濾是另外的事。","Why are nearly all spirits diluted with water before bottling?":"為什麼幾乎所有烈酒在裝瓶前都要加水稀釋？","To make them more enjoyable for most people":"讓大多數人更容易享用","To give them colour":"為它們增添顏色","To add oak flavours without using a barrel":"不用桶子就增添橡木風味","To stop haze forming in the cold":"防止在低溫時形成混濁","Very high alcohol is challenging: water makes it more approachable.":"非常高的酒精濃度不容易入口：水讓它更平易近人。","Completely pure water is used, adding neither colour nor flavour. Cold haze is removed by filtration. Undiluted spirits exist, but they are rare and aimed at enthusiasts.":"使用的是完全純淨的水，不增添顏色或風味。低溫造成的混濁是靠過濾去除的。未經稀釋的烈酒確實存在，但很少見，是針對愛好者的。","What is usually used to adjust the colour of an oak-matured spirit?":"通常用什麼來調整橡木桶熟成烈酒的顏色？","Activated charcoal":"活性碳","Concentrated fruit juice":"濃縮果汁","Sugar burnt directly in the still":"直接在蒸餾器中燒焦的糖","Caramel is a tasteless food-grade colouring, very effective even in small doses.":"焦糖色是沒有味道的食用色素，即使用量很少也非常有效。","It is used to keep colour the same from batch to batch. Activated charcoal does the opposite: it removes colour. Other natural or artificial colourings are used mainly for flavoured spirits and liqueurs.":"用它是為了讓每一批的顏色保持相同。活性碳的作用相反：它去除顏色。其他天然或人工色素主要用於調味烈酒和利口酒。","In which category is adding sugar a legal requirement?":"在哪一個類別中，加糖是法定要求？","All brandies, including long-aged ones":"所有白蘭地，包括長期陳年的","Malt whisky":"麥芽威士忌","In liqueurs, added sugar is required by law.":"在利口酒中，法律規定必須加糖。","Some brandies and rums may have sugar added for balance and style, but that is a choice, not a rule for all. Every spirit starts out dry; sweetness only comes from a later addition.":"有些白蘭地和蘭姆酒可能為了平衡和風格而加糖，但那是一種選擇，不是所有酒款的規定。所有烈酒一開始都是不甜的；甜味只來自之後的添加。","How does chill-filtration work?":"冷凝過濾如何運作？","The spirit is chilled, haze forms and is filtered out":"把烈酒降溫，混濁物形成後再濾除","The spirit is passed through a very fine activated charcoal filter":"讓烈酒通過非常細的活性碳濾器","The spirit is put in barrels in a cold cellar":"把烈酒裝桶，放在寒冷的酒窖裡","Ice is added to every bottle":"每一瓶都加入冰塊","The haze that cold would cause is removed before bottling.":"低溫會造成的混濁在裝瓶前就被去除。","That way the spirit stays clear even when served cold. It should not change the taste, though not everyone agrees. Activated charcoal is a different, far more drastic filtration.":"這樣烈酒即使冰飲也保持清澈。它應該不會改變味道，不過並非人人都同意。活性碳則是另一種強烈得多的過濾。","For which spirit is activated charcoal filtration often used to remove remaining congeners?":"哪一種烈酒常用活性碳過濾來去除剩餘的同屬物？","Non-chill-filtered malt whisky":"非冷凝過濾的麥芽威士忌","Very old Cognac":"極老的 Cognac","Activated charcoal strips the last congeners from neutral spirit: typical of vodka.":"活性碳去除中性烈酒中最後的同屬物：這是伏特加的典型做法。","It is also used for some white rums, since it removes colour too. Whisky, Cognac and Bourbon rely instead on the character and colour from oak, so removing them would defeat the purpose.":"它也用於某些白蘭姆酒，因為它同時會去除顏色。威士忌、Cognac 和 Bourbon 則仰賴橡木帶來的特色和顏色，去除它們就失去意義了。","A label says 'non-chill-filtered'. What does it tell the buyer?":"酒標上寫著「non-chill-filtered」。這告訴買家什麼？","The spirit has not been chill-filtered":"這款烈酒沒有經過冷凝過濾","The spirit must only be served at room temperature":"這款烈酒只能在室溫下飲用","The spirit has never been in a barrel":"這款烈酒從未入過桶","The spirit contains caramel added to even out batch colour":"這款烈酒添加了焦糖色，讓各批顏色一致","The producer signals that chill-filtration was skipped to preserve character.":"生產者表示略過了冷凝過濾，以保留特色。","Some producers believe even the most careful filtration takes something away, and they advertise skipping it. The term says nothing about serving temperature, ageing or colouring; in the cold, though, the spirit may turn hazy.":"有些生產者認為，即使最謹慎的過濾也會帶走一些東西，所以會標榜不做過濾。這個術語與飲用溫度、陳年或調色無關；不過在低溫下烈酒可能變混濁。","What is the main aim of post-distillation operations?":"蒸餾後處理的主要目的是什麼？","To give the spirit the right colour, aroma, sweetness and strength":"讓烈酒有合適的顏色、香氣、甜度和濃度","To raise the strength above 96%":"把濃度提高到 96% 以上","To turn starch into sugar":"把澱粉變成糖","To separate heads and tails from the heart, still mixed until now":"把到目前為止仍混在一起的酒頭和酒尾與酒心分開","After distillation the spirit is adjusted so it reaches the shelf with the intended colour, aroma, sweetness and strength.":"蒸餾之後要調整烈酒，讓它上架時具有預期的顏色、香氣、甜度和濃度。","Heads and tails are separated during distillation, not afterwards. Converting starch belongs to the raw-material stage. No later step raises strength above 96%; usually water is added instead.":"酒頭和酒尾是在蒸餾時分離的，不是之後。轉化澱粉屬於原料階段。之後沒有任何步驟會把濃度提高到 96% 以上；通常反而是加水。","What are a barrel's staves?":"桶的桶板是什麼？","Strips of wood bent into shape and held by metal hoops":"彎曲成形、用金屬箍固定的木條","The layer of carbon inside the barrel":"桶內的碳層","The metal hoops that close the barrel":"封住桶子的金屬箍","The glass vessels used to keep the oldest spirits":"用來存放最老烈酒的玻璃容器","A barrel is built from staves: wooden strips bent into shape and held together by metal hoops.":"桶子由桶板組成：彎曲成形並用金屬箍固定在一起的木條。","The inner carbon layer is called char or toast. The hoops hold the staves but are not the staves. Glass vessels for very old spirits are demijohns.":"內部的碳層稱為炙燒層或烘烤層。金屬箍固定桶板，但不是桶板。存放極老烈酒的玻璃容器是玻璃罈。","Which colour sequence describes a spirit ageing for a long time in oak?":"哪一組顏色順序描述了烈酒在橡木桶中長期陳年的變化？","Colourless, lemon, gold, amber, brown":"無色、檸檬色、金黃色、琥珀色、棕色","Brown, amber, gold, lemon, colourless":"棕色、琥珀色、金黃色、檸檬色、無色","Colourless, pink, red, brown":"無色、粉紅色、紅色、棕色","It stays colourless: colour only comes from caramel":"維持無色：顏色只來自焦糖色","The colourless spirit turns lemon and then gold; long maturation takes it to amber and finally brown.":"無色的烈酒先變成檸檬色，再變成金黃色；長期熟成讓它變成琥珀色，最後是棕色。","Colour comes from the wood and then deepens with oxygen and time. Caramel only corrects it for consistency; it does not create it. Pink or red tones are not part of oak ageing.":"顏色來自木頭，再隨氧氣和時間加深。焦糖色只是為了一致性而修正顏色，並不創造顏色。粉紅或紅色調不屬於橡木桶陳年。","How does oxygen reach the spirit inside a barrel?":"氧氣如何到達桶內的烈酒？","It enters through the wood":"透過木頭進入","It is pumped in":"用幫浦打進去","It is already in the caramel":"本來就在焦糖色裡","It does not: the barrel is fully airtight, like a demijohn":"到不了：桶子像玻璃罈一樣完全密閉","Wood lets oxygen through, which reacts with the congeners and creates new aromas.":"木頭讓氧氣通過，氧氣與同屬物反應，產生新的香氣。","These reactions create rancio notes such as leather and mushroom, and darken the colour. It is precisely to stop oxidation that very old Cognacs are moved into glass demijohns.":"這些反應產生皮革和蘑菇等 rancio 氣息，並讓顏色變深。極老的 Cognac 移到玻璃罈中，正是為了停止氧化。","How much of their volume can barrels of very old spirits lose?":"裝著極老烈酒的桶可能損失多少體積？","Nothing, as wood is waterproof":"完全不會，因為木頭不透水","Exactly a quarter, set by law":"剛好四分之一，由法律規定","Through evaporation, the 'angels' share', very old barrels can lose over half their contents.":"透過蒸發，也就是「天使的分享」，極老的桶可能損失超過一半的內容物。","Losses can be very high and depend on time and conditions, not a fixed rule. Wood lets water, alcohol and oxygen through: it is not waterproof.":"損失可能非常高，取決於時間和環境，沒有固定的規則。木頭會讓水、酒精和氧氣通過：它並不是不透水的。","What effect does the angels' share have on the spirit left in the barrel?":"天使的分享對留在桶中的烈酒有什麼影響？","It concentrates the congeners: more intense, complex aromas":"濃縮同屬物：香氣更濃郁、更複雜","It makes it more neutral":"讓它更中性","It makes it sweeter because only water evaporates":"讓它更甜，因為只有水蒸發","None: volume is lost but the taste stays identical":"沒有影響：體積減少，但味道完全相同","Water and ethanol evaporate; the remaining congeners concentrate and very old spirits become extraordinarily aromatic.":"水和乙醇蒸發；留下的同屬物被濃縮，極老的烈酒因此香氣格外豐富。","The spirit does not become more neutral; quite the reverse. Alcohol evaporates as well as water, and oak adds no sugar. The volume loss is exactly what changes the flavour intensity.":"烈酒不會變得更中性；恰恰相反。酒精和水一樣會蒸發，橡木也不會增添糖分。體積的損失正是改變風味強度的原因。","When is the carbon layer (char or toast) inside a barrel created?":"桶內的碳層（炙燒層或烘烤層）是什麼時候形成的？","When the barrel is made":"製桶的時候","During distillation":"蒸餾的時候","Slowly, over years of ageing":"在多年陳年中慢慢形成","By adding activated charcoal to the spirit before filling":"裝桶前在烈酒中加入活性碳","The charred or toasted layer forms while the barrel is being made.":"炙燒或烘烤層是在製桶過程中形成的。","This carbon captures some congeners and smooths the harshness of young spirits. Activated charcoal, by contrast, is a filtration tool, used for example for vodka and white rums.":"這層碳會抓住一些同屬物，讓年輕烈酒的粗糙感變得柔順。活性碳則是一種過濾工具，例如用於伏特加和白蘭姆酒。","A barrel is being filled for the third time. What can be said?":"一個桶正要第三次裝酒。可以怎麼說？","It will give less colour and flavour, but is not necessarily worse":"它給的顏色和風味會較少，但不一定比較差","It will give more colour than a new barrel":"它給的顏色會比新桶多","It is always inferior and should be scrapped":"它一定比較差，應該報廢","It will have no effect at all, just like a steel tank":"它完全沒有作用，就像鋼槽一樣","Each reuse gives less colour and flavour; the choice depends on the style wanted.":"每次重複使用，給的顏色和風味都會減少；怎麼選擇取決於想要的風格。","A new barrel gives the most, but for some styles that would be too much. A used barrel still lets in oxygen and concentrates the spirit: it is not an inert vessel.":"新桶給得最多，但對某些風格來說那會太多。用過的桶仍然會讓氧氣進入並濃縮烈酒：它不是惰性容器。","Why must producers manage barrel quality so carefully?":"為什麼生產者必須這麼仔細地管理桶的品質？","Poor-quality wood can ruin a spirit":"品質差的木頭會毀掉烈酒","Because the law bans used barrels":"因為法律禁止使用舊桶","Because barrels set the bottling strength":"因為桶決定裝瓶濃度","Because poor barrels keep all the alcohol and give back only water":"因為劣質的桶會留住所有酒精，只還回水","The barrel provides much of an aged spirit's flavour, so faulty wood spoils it.":"桶提供了陳年烈酒的大部分風味，所以有缺陷的木頭會毀掉它。","Barrels need the same care as fermentation and distillation. Used barrels are common and legitimate, and bottling strength is set with water.":"桶需要和發酵、蒸餾同等的用心。舊桶很常見，也完全正當，而裝瓶濃度是用水調整的。","A label describes a spirit as 'unaged'. What does this suggest?":"酒標把一款烈酒描述為「unaged」（未陳年）。這代表什麼？","A short rest in inert vessels, no colour from wood":"在惰性容器中短暫靜置，沒有來自木頭的顏色","Years in new oak barrels":"在新橡木桶中存放多年","A spirit coloured with caramel":"用焦糖色上色的烈酒","A spirit bottled without any dilution or filtration":"未經任何稀釋或過濾就裝瓶的烈酒","'Unaged' spirits are usually stored briefly in steel or glass: they stay colourless and almost unchanged.":"「未陳年」的烈酒通常在鋼或玻璃容器中短暫存放：保持無色，幾乎沒有變化。","The term is about maturation, not dilution or filtration, which may still happen. Caramel is mainly used to even out the colour of oak-aged spirits.":"這個術語說的是熟成，不是稀釋或過濾，後兩者仍然可能進行。焦糖色主要用來讓橡木桶陳年烈酒的顏色一致。","Which of these is NOT an effect of long storage in glass or steel?":"下列哪一項不是在玻璃或鋼製容器中長期存放的效果？","The spirit becomes smoother":"烈酒變得更柔順","The spirit becomes more mouthfilling":"烈酒變得更飽滿","The spirit keeps slowly evolving for years":"烈酒持續緩慢變化好幾年","Inert vessels give no colour: the spirit stays colourless even after years.":"惰性容器不帶來顏色：即使過了多年，烈酒仍然無色。","After a few months the spirit grows smoother and more mouthfilling, and this can go on for years, though maturing this way is rare. Colour, however, never changes.":"幾個月後烈酒會變得更柔順、更飽滿，而且可以持續好幾年，不過這樣熟成很少見。但顏色永遠不會改變。","Why might a producer choose an inert vessel instead of oak?":"為什麼生產者可能選擇惰性容器而不是橡木桶？","To avoid changing the spirit's colour and flavour":"避免改變烈酒的顏色和風味","To darken it faster":"讓它更快變深","To concentrate it through a large angels' share in a few months":"在幾個月內透過大量的天使的分享把它濃縮","Oak changes colour and flavour a lot; it does not suit some spirits, so steel or glass is used.":"橡木會大幅改變顏色和風味；它不適合某些烈酒，所以使用鋼或玻璃。","Darkening, adding vanilla and concentrating by evaporation are all barrel effects, exactly what an inert vessel avoids. The spirit stays clear and true to its original character.":"顏色變深、增添香草和透過蒸發濃縮都是桶的效果，正是惰性容器要避免的。烈酒保持清澈，忠於原本的特色。","Why can a blender not follow a fixed recipe year after year?":"為什麼調和師不能年復一年照著固定的配方做？","Spirits change or stop being available":"烈酒會改變，或不再有貨","Because the law requires a new recipe every year":"因為法律規定每年要有新配方","Because consumers want a different taste in every batch":"因為消費者希望每一批的味道都不同","Because barrels always give the same result, so recipes are pointless":"因為桶的結果總是相同，所以配方毫無意義","Over the years components change or run out, so many options are needed to reach the same result.":"多年下來，各個成分會改變或用完，所以需要許多選項才能達到相同的結果。","The goal is consistency from batch to batch, not variety. Barrels differ a great deal, which is exactly why blending is essential.":"目標是每一批都一致，不是多樣化。桶與桶之間差異很大，這正是調和不可或缺的原因。","What does a blender need to deliver consistency and complexity?":"調和師需要什麼才能做到一致性和複雜度？","The widest possible range of different spirits":"盡可能廣泛的各種不同烈酒","A single spirit from a single barrel":"來自單一桶的單一烈酒","Only spirits of the same age":"只有同樣年數的烈酒","Only column spirits, since they are the most consistent":"只有蒸餾柱烈酒，因為它們最一致","Pot and column spirits of various ages, matured in different barrels and conditions, give the blender more routes.":"不同年數、在不同的桶和環境中熟成的壺式和柱式蒸餾烈酒，給調和師更多條路可走。","A single component cannot be blended, and sticking to one age or one still type narrows the options. The more ingredients there are, the easier it is to reproduce the same taste.":"單一成分無法調和，只用一種年數或一種蒸餾器也會限縮選項。材料越多，就越容易重現相同的味道。","Why is a very old spirit often not bottled on its own?":"為什麼極老的烈酒通常不單獨裝瓶？","It can be so intense that it lacks balance":"它可能濃郁到失去平衡","Because it has lost all its colour":"因為它已失去所有顏色","Because it has become neutral":"因為它已變成中性","Because the law forbids selling spirits over twenty years old":"因為法律禁止販售超過二十年的烈酒","On its own a very old spirit can be too intense; added in small doses to a young one it creates balance.":"極老的烈酒單獨喝可能太濃郁；少量加進年輕的烈酒則能創造平衡。","Young spirits often lack depth and very old ones balance: together they give what neither has alone. With age colour darkens and aromas concentrate rather than vanish.":"年輕的烈酒往往缺乏深度，極老的則缺乏平衡：合在一起就有了各自所沒有的東西。隨著年數增加，顏色變深，香氣濃縮，而不是消失。","How often is a spirit bottled just as it comes off the still?":"烈酒照蒸餾出來的原樣直接裝瓶的情況有多常見？","Hardly ever":"幾乎沒有","Almost always":"幾乎都是","Only for column spirits":"只有蒸餾柱烈酒","Always, as the law bans any step after distillation":"一律如此，因為法律禁止蒸餾後的任何步驟","It would be possible, but almost no one does it: distillers choose among several finishing steps.":"是可以這麼做，但幾乎沒有人這樣做：蒸餾師會在幾種收尾步驟中做選擇。","Before bottling, water is usually added and, depending on the case, colour adjusted, sugar added or the spirit filtered. Laws regulate these steps rather than banning them.":"裝瓶前通常會加水，並視情況調整顏色、加糖或過濾。法律是規範這些步驟，而不是禁止。","What kind of water is used to bring a spirit down to bottling strength?":"把烈酒降到裝瓶濃度，用的是什麼樣的水？","Completely pure water":"完全純淨的水","The still-warm condenser water":"仍溫熱的冷凝器用水","The watery residue from the pot, which keeps some aroma":"壺身裡的含水殘液，它保有一些香氣","Dilution uses completely pure water, so the spirit is not altered.":"稀釋使用完全純淨的水，所以烈酒不會被改變。","The pot residue is waste and is discarded. Cooling water is only for the condenser. Any impurity in the water would end up in the glass.":"壺身的殘液是廢液，會被丟棄。冷卻水只供冷凝器使用。水中的任何雜質最後都會進到杯子裡。","In most cases, what is a spirit's legal minimum bottling strength?":"在大多數情況下，烈酒的法定最低裝瓶濃度是多少？","40% abv in the USA, 37.5% abv in the EU":"美國 40% abv，歐盟 37.5% abv","37.5% abv in the USA, 40% abv in the EU":"美國 37.5% abv，歐盟 40% abv","30% abv everywhere":"各地都是 30% abv","There is no minimum: each producer decides freely":"沒有最低限度：每位生產者自由決定","The legal minimum is usually 40% abv in the United States and 37.5% abv in the European Union.":"法定最低濃度在美國通常是 40% abv，在歐盟是 37.5% abv。","Swapping the two figures is a common mistake. Some categories have their own rules, but a legal minimum exists. Below these levels a product cannot be sold as a spirit in those markets.":"把這兩個數字對調是常見的錯誤。有些類別有自己的規定，但法定最低限度是存在的。低於這些濃度，產品在這些市場就不能以烈酒的名義販售。","An oak-aged rum is sold water-white. Which technique could explain this?":"一款橡木桶陳年的蘭姆酒以清澈如水的樣子販售。哪一種技術可以解釋這一點？","Chill-filtration":"冷凝過濾","Adding caramel":"添加焦糖色","A final few weeks in a stainless steel tank":"最後在不鏽鋼槽中存放幾週","Activated charcoal is so fine a filter that it removes congeners and colour; it is used for some white rums.":"活性碳是非常細的濾材，能去除同屬物和顏色；用於某些白蘭姆酒。","Chill-filtration only removes haze, not colour. Caramel adds colour rather than removing it. An inert vessel does not change colour: it neither adds nor removes it.":"冷凝過濾只去除混濁，不去除顏色。焦糖色是增添顏色，而不是去除。惰性容器不會改變顏色：既不增添也不去除。","How long can a maceration last, and what can speed it up?":"浸漬可以持續多久？什麼能加快它？","From a few hours to several months; heat is sometimes used":"從幾小時到幾個月；有時會加熱","Always exactly 24 hours, cold":"一律剛好 24 小時，冷浸","Several years, and only in oak barrels":"好幾年，而且只在橡木桶中","A few minutes, since longer contact would evaporate all the alcohol":"幾分鐘，因為接觸更久會讓酒精全部蒸發","A maceration can last a few hours or several months, and heat helps extract more flavour.":"浸漬可以持續幾小時或好幾個月，加熱有助於萃取更多風味。","There is no fixed length: it depends on the botanical and the style sought. Maceration usually happens in tanks, often with botanicals in bags for easy removal, not necessarily in barrels.":"沒有固定的長度：取決於植物性原料和追求的風格。浸漬通常在槽中進行，常把植物性原料裝在袋子裡以便取出，不一定在桶中。","A spirit flavoured by redistilling with botanicals is sometimes called…":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾而調味的烈酒，有時稱為……","a distillate":"餾出液（distillate）","a tincture":"酊劑（tincture）","A spirit made by redistilling with botanicals is sometimes simply called a 'distillate'.":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾製成的烈酒，有時就簡稱為「餾出液」（distillate）。","A tincture is instead the result of maceration. Molasses and wort are sugary starting liquids for rum and whisky, not flavoured spirits.":"酊劑（tincture）則是浸漬的成果。糖蜜和麥汁是蘭姆酒和威士忌起點的含糖液體，不是調味烈酒。","In redistillation with botanicals, how does the distiller control the flavour?":"與植物性原料一起再蒸餾時，蒸餾師如何控制風味？","By taking the heart cut while the wanted aromas come off":"在想要的香氣流出時切取酒心","By adding caramel at the end":"在最後加入焦糖色","By leaving the botanicals in a barrel for years":"把植物性原料留在桶中好幾年","By distilling everything uncut, then filtering through activated charcoal":"不做切取地全部蒸餾，再用活性碳過濾","The most volatile aromas come off first and the least volatile last; the distiller takes the heart when the right ones arrive.":"最易揮發的香氣最先流出，最不易揮發的最後；蒸餾師在合適的香氣出現時切取酒心。","It is the same principle as pot-still distillation. Caramel only gives colour, activated charcoal would strip the very aromas wanted, and leaving botanicals in a barrel is not redistillation.":"這和壺式蒸餾的原理相同。焦糖色只帶來顏色，活性碳會去除正想要的香氣，而把植物性原料留在桶中並不是再蒸餾。","A brand never handles botanicals itself but uses natural flavours. How?":"一個品牌從不自己處理植物性原料，卻使用天然香料。怎麼做到的？","It buys ready-made botanical flavourings from specialists":"向專業廠商購買現成的植物性香料","It gets them from the oak barrel":"從橡木桶取得","It creates them during fermentation":"在發酵中產生","It extracts them from caramel, which also holds natural fruit and spice flavours":"從焦糖色中萃取，它也含有天然的水果和香料風味","Some brands buy pre-prepared botanical flavourings from specialists and blend them into their spirit.":"有些品牌向專業廠商購買預先製備的植物性香料，再調入自己的烈酒。","These are natural flavours prepared elsewhere, not created in fermentation or barrel. Caramel is a tasteless colouring. When the flavour is artificial, the term is cold compounding.":"這些是在別處製備的天然香料，不是在發酵或桶中產生的。焦糖色是沒有味道的色素。如果香料是人工的，就稱為冷混法。","What is an artificial flavouring?":"什麼是人工香料？","A man-made flavour similar to those found in nature":"人造的、與自然界中的風味相似的香料","A fruit extract made by maceration":"以浸漬製成的水果萃取物","A flavour that comes from oak":"來自橡木的風味","A herbal aroma captured in a vacuum still":"用真空蒸餾器捕捉的草本香氣","An artificial flavour is man-made but imitates natural tastes; specialist producers supply it.":"人工香料是人造的，但模仿天然的味道；由專業生產商供應。","Maceration and vacuum stills work with real fruit and botanicals, so they give natural flavours. Oak is another natural source. Artificial flavours are added to the spirit by cold compounding.":"浸漬和真空蒸餾器使用真正的水果和植物性原料，所以得到的是天然風味。橡木是另一個天然來源。人工香料是以冷混法加入烈酒的。","What are 'botanicals' usually taken to mean?":"「植物性原料」（botanicals）通常指什麼？","The herbs and spices used by distillers":"蒸餾師使用的香草和香料","Only juniper berries":"只有杜松子","Artificial colourings in liqueurs":"利口酒中的人工色素","The grains and fruit used as raw materials to ferment":"用來發酵的穀物和水果原料","There is no universal definition, but the term normally covers the many herbs and spices used for flavouring.":"沒有通用的定義，但這個術語通常涵蓋用來調味的各種香草和香料。","Juniper is an important botanical, but not the only one. Grains and fruit for fermenting are raw materials, not flavouring botanicals. Colourings give no flavour.":"杜松子是重要的植物性原料，但不是唯一的。用來發酵的穀物和水果是原料，不是調味用的植物性原料。色素不帶來風味。","Which of these is NOT one of the four groups of post-distillation operations?":"下列哪一項不屬於蒸餾後處理的四組操作？","Adding other flavours, for example with botanicals":"添加其他風味，例如使用植物性原料","Malting prepares the raw material, before fermentation even starts.":"製麥是在處理原料，發酵都還沒開始。","The four groups are maturation, adding other flavours, blending and finishing, usually in that order. Not every spirit goes through all of them.":"四組是熟成、添加其他風味、調和和收尾處理，通常依這個順序。並非每種烈酒都經過全部四組。","Does every spirit go through all the post-distillation operations?":"每種烈酒都經過所有的蒸餾後處理嗎？","No: it depends on the law and the distiller's choices":"不：取決於法規和蒸餾師的選擇","Yes, otherwise it cannot be bottled":"是的，否則無法裝瓶","No: only oak-aged spirits receive any treatment":"不：只有橡木桶陳年的烈酒才會經過處理","What happens after distillation depends both on the rules for the type of spirit and on the producer's choices.":"蒸餾之後做什麼，既取決於該類烈酒的規定，也取決於生產者的選擇。","An unaged spirit skips oak maturation, and adding flavours mainly concerns flavoured spirits and liqueurs. Unaged spirits are often diluted and filtered too.":"未陳年的烈酒略過橡木桶熟成，添加風味則主要與調味烈酒和利口酒有關。未陳年的烈酒也常經過稀釋和過濾。","Which products is adding other flavours mainly limited to?":"添加其他風味主要限於哪些產品？","Cognac and Armagnac":"Cognac 和 Armagnac","Scotch malt whiskies":"Scotch 麥芽威士忌","All spirits aged over ten years":"所有陳年超過十年的烈酒","Adding flavours is typical of flavoured spirits, such as gin and flavoured vodka, and of liqueurs.":"添加風味是調味烈酒（例如琴酒和調味伏特加）以及利口酒的典型做法。","Brandies and whiskies get their character from raw material, distillation and barrel. Age is irrelevant: an old spirit does not get added flavours just because it is old.":"白蘭地和威士忌的特色來自原料、蒸餾和桶。年數無關緊要：老酒不會只因為老就添加風味。","Which of these is NOT an effect of an oak barrel on a spirit?":"下列哪一項不是橡木桶對烈酒的作用？","Making the spirit sweet":"讓烈酒變甜","Adding colour and congeners":"增添顏色和同屬物","Concentrating the spirit by evaporation":"透過蒸發濃縮烈酒","Removing harshness through the charred inner layer":"透過炙燒過的內層去除粗糙感","The barrel gives colour, flavour, oxidation, concentration and smoothness, but not sugar.":"桶帶來顏色、風味、氧化、濃縮和柔順感，但不帶來糖。","Sweetness, if any, is a finishing choice using added sugar. Vanilla and coconut notes can smell sweet, but the spirit stays dry.":"如果有甜味，那是收尾階段用加糖做出的選擇。香草和椰子氣息聞起來可能很甜美，但烈酒仍然是不甜的。","Which of these aromas comes from oxidation over time rather than directly from the wood?":"下列哪一種香氣來自隨時間的氧化，而不是直接來自木頭？","Coconut":"椰子","Clove":"丁香","Notes such as mushroom and leather (rancio) come from congeners reacting with oxygen during long maturation.":"蘑菇和皮革等氣息（rancio）來自長期熟成中同屬物與氧氣的反應。","Vanilla, coconut, cinnamon and clove are instead among the commonest aromas given directly by oak, even over fairly short periods.":"香草、椰子、肉桂和丁香則是橡木直接賦予的最常見香氣，即使時間相當短也會有。","A flavoured spirit is made with a single technique, for example one maceration. What usually happens next?":"一款調味烈酒只用單一技術製成，例如一次浸漬。接下來通常怎麼做？","Usually no blending is needed: it is prepared for sale":"通常不需要調和：直接做上市準備","By law it must be aged in oak":"依法必須在橡木桶中陳年","It must always be redistilled twice":"一定要再蒸餾兩次","It must always be blended with spirits made by other techniques":"一定要與用其他技術製成的烈酒調和","When only one technique is used, blending is usually unnecessary and the spirit is made ready for sale straight away.":"只用一種技術時，通常不需要調和，烈酒可以立刻做上市準備。","Other producers, by contrast, make several flavoured spirits by different techniques and then blend them. No general rule imposes oak or double redistillation.":"其他生產者則會用不同技術製作幾種調味烈酒，再加以調和。沒有任何通則強制要求橡木桶或二次再蒸餾。","In redistillation for flavouring, what usually goes into the pot still?":"為了調味而再蒸餾時，壺式蒸餾器裡通常裝什麼？","Diluted neutral spirit with fruit and botanicals":"稀釋過的中性烈酒，加上水果和植物性原料","10% fermented liquid and yeast":"10% 的發酵液和酵母","Low wines, heads and tails":"低度酒、酒頭和酒尾","Caramel and artificial flavourings bought from specialists":"焦糖色和向專業廠商購買的人工香料","Typically diluted neutral spirit is redistilled with fruit and botanicals, sometimes after a short maceration.":"通常是把稀釋過的中性烈酒與水果和植物性原料一起再蒸餾，有時先短暫浸漬。","Fermented liquid, low wines, heads and tails belong to making a base spirit. Caramel and artificial flavourings are added cold, without distilling.":"發酵液、低度酒、酒頭和酒尾屬於基酒的製作。焦糖色和人工香料是冷加的，不經蒸餾。","Why are botanicals often put in bags during maceration?":"為什麼浸漬時常把植物性原料裝在袋子裡？","To make them easier to remove afterwards":"方便之後取出","To stop them giving off colour":"防止它們釋出顏色","To isolate one precise aroma":"分離出某一種特定的香氣","To protect them from heat, which is never used in maceration":"保護它們不受熱，浸漬從不加熱","The bags make it easy to lift the botanicals out of the alcohol at the end of maceration.":"袋子讓人在浸漬結束時能輕鬆把植物性原料從酒精中取出。","Maceration extracts colour and a broad range of flavours but cannot isolate a single aroma. Heat is in fact sometimes used to extract more.":"浸漬會萃取顏色和範圍廣泛的風味，但無法分離出單一香氣。事實上有時會加熱來萃取更多。","Which flavouring technique can NOT isolate particular aromas?":"哪一種調味技術無法分離出特定的香氣？","Redistillation in a pot still":"在壺式蒸餾器中再蒸餾","Redistillation in a vacuum still":"在真空蒸餾器中再蒸餾","Redistillation with a very narrow heart cut":"以非常窄的酒心切取再蒸餾","Maceration extracts everything together, colour and many flavours, but cannot select among them.":"浸漬會把所有東西一起萃取出來，包括顏色和許多風味，但無法從中挑選。","With redistillation, aromas come off in order of volatility and the distiller chooses which to keep with the cuts. A vacuum still works at lower temperatures and protects delicate aromas.":"再蒸餾時，香氣依揮發性的順序流出，蒸餾師用切取來選擇保留哪些。真空蒸餾器在較低的溫度下運作，能保護細緻的香氣。","In what form do natural flavours added to spirits usually come?":"添加到烈酒中的天然風味通常以什麼形式出現？","Fruit or botanicals":"水果或植物性原料","Approved chemical dyes":"核准使用的化學染料","Lab-made flavours that imitate those found in nature":"實驗室製造、模仿自然界風味的香料","Natural flavours mostly come from fruit or botanicals, meaning herbs and spices.":"天然風味大多來自水果或植物性原料，也就是香草和香料。","Man-made flavours imitating nature are by definition artificial. Colourings and caramel give colour, not flavour.":"模仿自然的人造風味，依定義就是人工的。色素和焦糖色帶來的是顏色，不是風味。","What is 'finishing' among the post-distillation operations?":"在蒸餾後處理中，「收尾處理」（finishing）是什麼？","The final preparation of the spirit for bottling":"裝瓶前對烈酒做的最後準備","The last tails cut in the still":"在蒸餾器中最後一次切取酒尾","A compulsory spell in ex-wine barrels for every spirit":"每種烈酒都必須在葡萄酒桶中存放一段時間","The end of fermentation, when the yeast have used all the sugar":"發酵結束，酵母用完所有的糖","Finishing covers the last adjustments before bottling: water, colour, sugar, filtration.":"收尾處理包括裝瓶前的最後調整：水、顏色、糖、過濾。","Do not confuse it with the ex-wine cask 'finishes' of some whiskies, which are a maturation technique, not an obligation. Cuts belong to distillation and the end of the sugars to fermentation.":"不要把它和某些威士忌的葡萄酒桶「過桶」（finish）混淆，那是一種熟成技術，不是義務。切取屬於蒸餾，糖用完則屬於發酵。","What kind of grape do distillers usually prefer for grape brandy?":"製作葡萄白蘭地時，蒸餾師通常偏好哪一種葡萄？","Acidic white grapes with little aroma":"酸度高、香氣少的白葡萄","Black grapes rich in tannin and deep colour":"單寧豐富、顏色深的紅葡萄","Very ripe white grapes with low acidity":"非常成熟、酸度低的白葡萄","Dried grapes with highly concentrated sugar":"糖分高度濃縮的風乾葡萄","Acidic, neutral white grapes make plain wine, but distillation concentrates their delicate notes.":"酸度高、中性的白葡萄釀出的酒平淡無奇，但蒸餾會濃縮它們細緻的氣息。","The base wine does not need to be pleasant to drink: what matters is that distillation lifts its delicate floral and fruity aromas. Acidity also helps keep the wine fresh until it is distilled. Tannic black grapes, low-acid grapes or dried grapes do not meet these needs.":"基酒不需要好喝：重要的是蒸餾能突顯它細緻的花香和果香。酸度也有助於讓葡萄酒在蒸餾前保持新鮮。單寧重的紅葡萄、低酸的葡萄或風乾葡萄都不符合這些需求。","Why do fruit distilleries work with locally grown fruit?":"為什麼水果蒸餾廠使用當地種植的水果？","Fruit spoils quickly and develops off-aromas":"水果很快就會腐壞，並產生異味","The law everywhere bans moving fresh fruit":"各地法律都禁止運送新鮮水果","Distant fruit holds too much sugar for the yeast to handle":"遠地的水果含糖太多，酵母處理不了","Fruit has to be distilled whole, without pressing":"水果必須整顆蒸餾，不經壓榨","After picking, fruit deteriorates fast, so it must be processed straight away.":"水果採收後很快就變質，所以必須立刻加工。","The off-aromas that develop in spoiling fruit would carry through into the spirit. There is no general ban on transport, and fruit is normally crushed and pressed before fermentation rather than distilled whole.":"水果腐壞時產生的異味會一路帶進烈酒。沒有禁止運送的通則，而且水果通常先壓碎、壓榨再發酵，而不是整顆蒸餾。","Why must wine made for distillation be distilled within a few months?":"為什麼用來蒸餾的葡萄酒必須在幾個月內蒸餾？","Acidity and alcohol protect it only for a limited time":"酸度和酒精只能在有限的時間內保護它","Because the yeast starts producing sugar again":"因為酵母會重新開始製造糖","Because the wine becomes too strong for traditional stills to handle":"因為葡萄酒會變得太烈，傳統蒸餾器處理不了","Because the law requires distilling it before harvest":"因為法律規定要在採收前蒸餾","The protection from acidity and alcohol is not absolute, so the wine does not keep for long.":"酸度和酒精提供的保護並不是絕對的，所以葡萄酒無法久放。","Grapes are harvested once a year, so the wine has to wait before distillation. Acidity and alcohol keep it fresh, but only for a few months. Yeast does not produce sugar, it consumes it, and wine does not get stronger by sitting in a tank.":"葡萄一年採收一次，所以葡萄酒必須等待蒸餾。酸度和酒精讓它保持新鮮，但只有幾個月。酵母不會製造糖，而是消耗糖；葡萄酒放在槽裡也不會變得更烈。","What is pomace?":"什麼是果渣（pomace）？","The grape skins left over from winemaking":"釀酒後剩下的葡萄皮","The yeast sediment at the bottom of wine tanks":"酒槽底部的酵母沉澱物","The juice that runs from grapes before pressing":"葡萄壓榨前流出的汁液","The heads and tails discarded while distilling grape wine":"蒸餾葡萄酒時丟棄的酒頭和酒尾","Pomace is the mass of skins winemakers discard, which can be turned into a spirit.":"果渣是釀酒師丟棄的一堆葡萄皮，可以製成烈酒。","Pomace is used for spirits such as grappa. Yeast sediment, free-run juice and heads and tails are all different things: none of them is the mass of skins left after pressing.":"果渣用來製作 grappa 這類烈酒。酵母沉澱物、自流汁以及酒頭和酒尾都是不同的東西：沒有一樣是壓榨後剩下的那堆葡萄皮。","How is a fermentable liquid obtained from white grape pomace?":"如何從白葡萄果渣得到可發酵的液體？","They are mixed with water and the liquid is fermented":"與水混合，再讓液體發酵","They are distilled at once, as they are already soaked in alcohol":"立刻蒸餾，因為它們已經浸滿酒精","They are steeped in neutral spirit and then redistilled":"浸泡在中性烈酒中，再重新蒸餾","They are sun-dried and then cane sugar is added":"曬乾後再加入蔗糖","White skins, removed before fermentation, still hold juice: adding water gives a liquid to ferment.":"白葡萄的皮在發酵前就被移除，仍含有葡萄汁：加水就能得到可發酵的液體。","In white winemaking the skins are removed before fermentation, so they hold no alcohol, just some juice. It is black grape pomace that arrives already alcoholic, because it ferments with the juice. Steeping in neutral spirit is used for some low-juice fruits, not for pomace.":"釀造白酒時，皮在發酵前就被移除，所以不含酒精，只有一些葡萄汁。紅葡萄果渣才是送來時就含有酒精，因為它與葡萄汁一起發酵。浸泡在中性烈酒中的做法用於某些出汁少的水果，不是果渣。","A distillery receives black grape pomace from a red wine cellar. What can it do?":"一家蒸餾廠從紅酒酒窖收到紅葡萄果渣。它可以怎麼做？","Distil it straight away, as it already contains alcohol":"立刻蒸餾，因為果渣已含有酒精","Add water and yeast, then wait several weeks before distilling":"加水和酵母，等幾週後再蒸餾","Press it to obtain sweet, unfermented juice":"壓榨以取得未發酵的甜汁","Store it in oak for a year before distilling":"在橡木桶中存放一年後再蒸餾","Black skins ferment with the juice, so they arrive soaked in wine and can be distilled at once.":"紅葡萄的皮與葡萄汁一起發酵，所以送來時浸滿了葡萄酒，可以立刻蒸餾。","In red winemaking the skins stay with the juice throughout fermentation to give colour; after draining and pressing, some wine is still left in them. Adding water and yeast is the method for white pomace, and there is no sweet juice left because the sugar has already fermented.":"釀造紅酒時，皮在整個發酵過程中都與葡萄汁在一起，以帶來顏色；排汁和壓榨後，皮裡仍留有一些葡萄酒。加水和酵母是白葡萄果渣的做法，而且已經沒有甜汁了，因為糖已經發酵完。","Two spirits are made from one batch of grapes: one from the wine, one from the pomace. What sets the pomace spirit apart?":"用同一批葡萄製作兩款烈酒：一款用葡萄酒，一款用果渣。果渣烈酒有什麼不同？","Herbaceous and spicy notes":"草本和香料氣息","An identical taste but a darker colour from the skins":"味道完全相同，但因為果皮而顏色較深","Vanilla and coconut aromas even without wood":"即使沒有木頭也有香草和椰子香氣","A much higher natural sweetness":"天然甜度高得多","The skins give pomace spirits their typical herbaceous, spicy character.":"葡萄皮賦予果渣烈酒典型的草本、香料特色。","The two spirits would taste very different, not just look different; in fact, freshly distilled spirits are colourless. Vanilla and coconut are typical oak aromas, and no spirit contains sugar as it leaves the still.":"兩款烈酒的味道會非常不同，不只是外觀不同；事實上剛蒸餾出來的烈酒都是無色的。香草和椰子是典型的橡木香氣，而任何烈酒離開蒸餾器時都不含糖。","Why are some fruits steeped in neutral spirit and redistilled instead of being fermented?":"為什麼有些水果是浸泡在中性烈酒中再蒸餾，而不是發酵？","They give little juice, or fermentation aromas are to be avoided":"它們出汁少，或是想避免發酵的香氣","They contain too much acid for yeast to survive":"它們含酸太多，酵母無法存活","So the spirit can age faster in oak":"這樣烈酒在橡木桶中能更快陳年","European law bans fermenting any fruit other than grapes":"歐洲法律禁止發酵葡萄以外的任何水果","Maceration is used when juice is scarce or when a profile free of fermentation aromas is wanted.":"出汁少，或想要沒有發酵香氣的風味輪廓時，就使用浸漬。","Some fruits are hard to press for enough juice to ferment; in other cases the distiller wants a purer profile. These spirits can be thought of as high-quality flavoured vodkas. Apples, pears, plums and cherries are fermented all the time, so no such ban exists.":"有些水果很難壓榨出足夠發酵的汁；另一些情況則是蒸餾師想要更純淨的輪廓。這些烈酒可以看成高品質的調味伏特加。蘋果、梨、李子和櫻桃一直都在發酵，所以沒有這種禁令。","Which type of still makes most high-quality fruit spirits?":"大多數高品質水果烈酒用哪一種蒸餾器製作？","Multi-plate column still":"多層蒸餾板的柱式蒸餾器","No still at all: maceration only":"完全不用蒸餾器：只做浸漬","Glass vacuum still":"玻璃真空蒸餾器","Many still types are used worldwide, but most top fruit spirits come from pot stills.":"世界各地使用許多種蒸餾器，但大多數頂級水果烈酒來自壺式蒸餾器。","A pot still keeps plenty of fruit aroma. A column taken up to neutral spirit would strip out exactly the character being sought. There are notable exceptions, such as Armagnac's short column, but those columns are designed to keep character.":"壺式蒸餾器能保留豐富的水果香氣。蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱，會去除的正是所追求的特色。也有值得注意的例外，例如 Armagnac 的矮蒸餾柱，但那些蒸餾柱是為了保留特色而設計的。","Many top producers age young brandy for a year or two in new barrels, then in older ones. Why?":"許多頂尖生產者把年輕的白蘭地先放在新桶中一、兩年，再放進較舊的桶。為什麼？","For clear oak character that does not swamp fruit and flowers":"得到清晰的橡木特色，又不蓋過果香和花香","To remove all the colour picked up in the new barrels entirely":"完全去除在新桶中得到的顏色","Because old barrels add sugar to the spirit":"因為舊桶會為烈酒增添糖分","To raise the alcoholic strength before bottling":"在裝瓶前提高酒精濃度","New oak gives a clear imprint, then older barrels let the spirit develop without piling on more wood.":"新橡木桶留下清晰的印記，接著較舊的桶讓烈酒繼續發展，而不再堆疊更多木質味。","The goal is balance between wood and fruit. Older barrels do not remove colour; they simply give less flavour. Barrels do not add sugar, and with evaporation over time the strength tends to fall rather than rise.":"目標是木頭和果香之間的平衡。較舊的桶不會去除顏色，只是給的風味較少。桶不會增添糖分，而且隨著時間蒸發，濃度往往是下降而不是上升。","Where is the Cognac production area?":"Cognac 的產區在哪裡？","Just north of Bordeaux":"就在波爾多北邊","South of Bordeaux":"波爾多以南","In Normandy, in northern France":"法國北部的諾曼第","In the Rhône Valley":"隆河谷","Cognac comes from a delimited area just north of Bordeaux in south-west France.":"Cognac 來自法國西南部、就在波爾多北邊的一個劃定產區。","South of Bordeaux is Armagnac country, and Normandy is the home of Calvados. A handy memory trick: Cognac above Bordeaux, Armagnac below.":"波爾多以南是 Armagnac 的地盤，諾曼第則是 Calvados 的故鄉。一個好記的口訣：Cognac 在波爾多上面，Armagnac 在下面。","Which grape variety supplies the vast majority of grapes for Cognac?":"哪一個葡萄品種供應了 Cognac 絕大部分的葡萄？","Ugni Blanc dominates Cognac: neutral wine, but a spirit with a signature aroma.":"白玉霓在 Cognac 占主導地位：葡萄酒中性，烈酒卻有招牌香氣。","Muscat is an aromatic grape linked to pisco and some grappas. Baco matters in Armagnac, where it brings prune notes. Chardonnay plays no part in these spirits.":"蜜思嘉是芳香型葡萄，與 pisco 和某些 grappa 有關。巴科在 Armagnac 很重要，帶來李子乾氣息。夏多內在這些烈酒中沒有角色。","Which signature aromas does Ugni Blanc give once distilled?":"白玉霓蒸餾後帶來哪些招牌香氣？","Raisin and violet":"葡萄乾和紫羅蘭","Prune and tobacco":"李子乾和菸草","Baked apple and caramel":"烤蘋果和焦糖","Herbaceous, spicy notes from the skins":"來自果皮的草本、香料氣息","Although it makes low-aroma wine, Ugni Blanc gives spirits with raisin and violet notes.":"白玉霓釀出的葡萄酒雖然香氣少，卻能做出帶葡萄乾和紫羅蘭氣息的烈酒。","Prune is the hallmark of Baco in Armagnac, apple points to Calvados, and herbaceous, spicy notes mark pomace spirits. Ugni Blanc itself also changes character from one sub-region to another.":"李子乾是巴科在 Armagnac 的標誌，蘋果指向 Calvados，草本、香料氣息則是果渣烈酒的特徵。白玉霓本身也會隨子產區不同而改變特色。","By when must the distillation of a Cognac harvest be finished?":"Cognac 一個年份的蒸餾必須在什麼時候之前完成？","By the end of March the following year":"隔年三月底之前","By the end of December the same year":"同年十二月底之前","Before the next harvest, roughly one year later":"下一次採收之前，大約一年後","There is no deadline: it is distilled as needed":"沒有期限：需要時再蒸餾","The rules require distillation to finish by the end of March after the autumn harvest.":"規定要求在秋季採收後的三月底之前完成蒸餾。","The deadline also fits the fact that the wine only stays fresh for a few months. December would be too early to distil the whole crop, while waiting a full year or having no deadline would leave the wine open to spoilage.":"這個期限也符合葡萄酒只能保鮮幾個月的事實。十二月要蒸餾完全部收成太早，而等上整整一年或沒有期限，則會讓葡萄酒有變質的風險。","Which statement about Cognac stills is correct?":"關於 Cognac 的蒸餾器，下列哪一項正確？","Direct flame heat and a worm tub condenser":"直火加熱和蟲桶冷凝器","Steam heating and modern shell-and-tube condensers":"蒸汽加熱和現代的殼管式冷凝器","A single distillation in a short continuous column":"在矮的連續式蒸餾柱中蒸餾一次","Stainless steel stills heated by electric elements":"以電熱元件加熱的不鏽鋼蒸餾器","Cognac stills must be heated by direct flame and use the traditional worm tub.":"Cognac 的蒸餾器必須以直火加熱，並使用傳統的蟲桶冷凝器。","These are two features now rare elsewhere: direct flame heating (today gas) and the worm tub, a coiled copper pipe in a water tank as big as the still. Cognac requires two distillations in copper pot stills: no column, no stainless steel, no modern condenser.":"這兩項特點如今在其他地方都很少見：直火加熱（現在用瓦斯）和蟲桶冷凝器，也就是放在與蒸餾器一樣大的水槽中的盤繞銅管。Cognac 規定在銅製壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次：不用蒸餾柱、不用不鏽鋼、不用現代冷凝器。","An Armagnac label shows a year, for example 1995. What does it mean?":"一瓶 Armagnac 的酒標上有一個年份，例如 1995。這是什麼意思？","All the grapes were harvested that year":"所有葡萄都在那一年採收","It is the year the producing estate was founded":"那是生產酒莊創立的年份","It is the year the blend was bottled":"那是調和酒裝瓶的年份","It shows the oldest spirit included in the blend of ages":"它表示不同年數的調和中最老的烈酒","A vintage Armagnac comes only from grapes of that harvest, with no blending of ages.":"年份 Armagnac 只來自該年採收的葡萄，沒有調和不同年數的酒。","Vintage-dated spirits are common in Armagnac and rare in Cognac. The year is not a founding date or a bottling date. For blends, age terms refer to the youngest spirit, not the oldest.":"標示年份的烈酒在 Armagnac 很常見，在 Cognac 則很少見。這個年份不是創立日期，也不是裝瓶日期。對調和酒來說，年數術語指的是最年輕的烈酒，不是最老的。","What is the minimum time any Cognac must spend in oak?":"任何 Cognac 至少必須在橡木桶中存放多久？","No minimum: there is also a clear, unaged Cognac":"沒有最低限度：也有清澈、未陳年的 Cognac","Every Cognac must spend at least two years in oak barrels.":"每款 Cognac 都必須在橡木桶中存放至少兩年。","Two years is the minimum for the youngest level, VS. There is no unaged Cognac: it is Armagnac that has Blanche, which has no Cognac equivalent. Many producers go well beyond the minimums anyway.":"兩年是最年輕的等級 VS 的最低要求。沒有未陳年的 Cognac：有 Blanche 的是 Armagnac，Cognac 沒有對應的類型。反正許多生產者都遠遠超過最低要求。","On a Cognac, what do the terms VS, VSOP or XO refer to?":"在 Cognac 上，VS、VSOP 或 XO 這些術語指的是什麼？","The age of the youngest spirit in the blend":"調和中最年輕烈酒的年數","The average age of all the spirits making up the blend":"構成調和的所有烈酒的平均年數","The age of the oldest spirit in the blend":"調和中最老烈酒的年數","The sub-region the grapes came from":"葡萄來自的子產區","Age indications guarantee the minimum age of the youngest component.":"年數標示保證的是最年輕成分的最低年數。","A blend may contain much older spirits, but the youngest one is what counts. It is not an average or a maximum. Origin is shown by names such as Grande Champagne, not by VS or XO. Outside the protected French regions these terms have no legal definition.":"調和中可能含有老得多的烈酒，但算數的是最年輕的那一款。它不是平均值，也不是最大值。產地是用 Grande Champagne 這類名稱表示的，不是 VS 或 XO。在受保護的法國產區之外，這些術語沒有法律定義。","Which Cognac sub-region is considered the best for growing grapes?":"Cognac 的哪一個子產區被認為最適合種植葡萄？","Bas Armagnac":"Bas Armagnac","Grande Champagne, near the town of Cognac, is the most highly regarded sub-region.":"靠近 Cognac 鎮的 Grande Champagne 是評價最高的子產區。","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze are Armagnac sub-regions, not Cognac ones. Fine Champagne is not a sub-region but a blend of Grande and Petite Champagne. After Grande Champagne, the most respected areas are Petite Champagne and Borderies.":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze 是 Armagnac 的子產區，不是 Cognac 的。Fine Champagne 不是子產區，而是 Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne 的調和。在 Grande Champagne 之後，最受推崇的是 Petite Champagne 和 Borderies。","What does Fine Champagne on a Cognac label mean?":"Cognac 酒標上的 Fine Champagne 是什麼意思？","A blend of Grande (min. 50%) and Petite Champagne":"Grande Champagne（至少 50%）和 Petite Champagne 的調和","A Cognac finished in casks that once held sparkling wine":"在裝過氣泡酒的桶中過桶的 Cognac","A Cognac made 100% from Petite Champagne grapes only":"100% 只用 Petite Champagne 葡萄製成的 Cognac","An age indication above XO":"高於 XO 的年數標示","Fine Champagne combines spirits from Grande Champagne, at least half, and Petite Champagne.":"Fine Champagne 結合了 Grande Champagne（至少一半）和 Petite Champagne 的烈酒。","Here Champagne names Cognac sub-regions, not sparkling wine. A Cognac made only from Petite Champagne grapes would carry that sub-region's name. Fine Champagne is about origin, not age.":"這裡的 Champagne 是 Cognac 子產區的名稱，不是氣泡酒。只用 Petite Champagne 葡萄製成的 Cognac 會標示該子產區的名稱。Fine Champagne 說的是產地，不是年數。","Which are the two important Armagnac sub-regions?":"Armagnac 的兩個重要子產區是哪兩個？","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze","Grande Champagne and Petite Champagne":"Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne","Borderies and Fine Champagne":"Borderies 和 Fine Champagne","Normandy and Lower Normandy":"諾曼第和下諾曼第","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze are the two sub-region names to know in Armagnac.":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze 是 Armagnac 必須知道的兩個子產區名稱。","Grande Champagne, Petite Champagne and Borderies belong to Cognac, and Fine Champagne is a blend, not a sub-region. Normandy is Calvados country.":"Grande Champagne、Petite Champagne 和 Borderies 屬於 Cognac，Fine Champagne 是調和，不是子產區。諾曼第是 Calvados 的地盤。","Why are some very old Cognacs transferred into glass demijohns?":"為什麼有些極老的 Cognac 會轉移到玻璃罈中？","To halt their evolution and use them sparingly in top blends":"停止它們的變化，並少量用於頂級調和","To darken their colour before selling them on their own":"在單獨販售前讓顏色變深","To raise their strength through water evaporation":"透過水分蒸發提高濃度","To speed up oxidation and build more rancio within a few months":"加快氧化，在幾個月內累積更多 rancio","Glass stops the effect of oak and oxygen, keeping the spirit in its ideal state.":"玻璃阻斷橡木和氧氣的作用，讓烈酒維持在理想狀態。","When the cellar master judges that cask and oxygen can no longer improve the spirit, it moves into glass, which is inert. These precious spirits are rarely sold alone: they add depth and complexity to prestige blends. Glass does not darken, concentrate or speed up oxidation.":"當酒窖總管判斷桶和氧氣已無法再讓烈酒變得更好，就把它移到惰性的玻璃中。這些珍貴的烈酒很少單獨販售：它們為頂級調和增添深度和複雜度。玻璃不會讓顏色變深、不會濃縮，也不會加快氧化。","A customer notices that a Cognac has a slightly rich, smooth texture without tasting sweet. What is a likely explanation?":"一位顧客注意到某款 Cognac 的質地略顯豐潤柔順，喝起來卻不甜。可能的解釋是什麼？","A small sugar addition, a traditional practice":"加了少量的糖，這是傳統做法","The copper still leaves sugar in the spirit":"銅製蒸餾器把糖留在烈酒中","The worm tub holds back alcohol and lets grape sugar through":"蟲桶冷凝器擋住酒精，讓葡萄的糖通過","It was distilled from dried grapes":"它是用風乾葡萄蒸餾的","Most Cognacs are lightly sweetened before bottling, making them off-dry.":"大多數 Cognac 在裝瓶前會稍微加糖，成為微甜（off-dry）。","A spirit leaving the still contains no sugar, whatever the grape or still: sugar does not distil. A small dose added afterwards gives a hint of syrupy texture without making the spirit taste sweet. In Cognac this is a long-standing practice and an integral part of production.":"離開蒸餾器的烈酒不含糖，不論用什麼葡萄或蒸餾器：糖無法蒸餾。之後加入少量的糖，會帶來一絲糖漿般的質地，卻不會讓烈酒喝起來是甜的。在 Cognac 這是由來已久的做法，也是生產中不可或缺的一部分。","At a tasting, a Cognac shows distinct fruit and oak and a slightly sharp texture. Which level is most likely?":"在一場品飲中，某款 Cognac 表現出分明的果香和橡木味，質地略顯銳利。最可能是哪個等級？","A blend enriched with demijohn-aged spirits":"加入玻璃罈陳放烈酒的調和","Relatively young VS Cognacs show clear fruit and oak and can feel a little sharp.":"相對年輕的 VS Cognac 表現出清晰的果香和橡木味，口感可能有點銳利。","With age, Cognac becomes richer and more integrated. The best XO and Hors d'âge Cognacs combine raisin, flowers, oak and rancio with a silky texture. Demijohn spirits go into prestige blends, so they would give an even more mature profile.":"隨著年數增加，Cognac 變得更豐富、更融合。最好的 XO 和 Hors d'âge Cognac 結合了葡萄乾、花香、橡木和 rancio，質地如絲。玻璃罈中的烈酒用於頂級調和，所以會帶來更成熟的輪廓。","Where is Armagnac made?":"Armagnac 在哪裡生產？","In Normandy":"在諾曼第","In Burgundy":"在勃根地","Grapes for Armagnac must come from an area south of Bordeaux.":"Armagnac 的葡萄必須來自波爾多以南的一個產區。","North of Bordeaux is Cognac, and Normandy, too cool for vines, makes Calvados from apples and pears. Burgundy is not a benchmark area for these spirits.":"波爾多以北是 Cognac；諾曼第對葡萄樹來說太涼，用蘋果和梨製作 Calvados。勃根地不是這些烈酒的代表產區。","Which grape often gives Armagnac a characteristic prune aroma?":"哪一種葡萄常讓 Armagnac 帶有典型的李子乾香氣？","Baco is responsible for the characteristic prune aroma of many Armagnacs.":"巴科是許多 Armagnac 典型李子乾香氣的來源。","Folle Blanche brings pronounced floral and fruity notes instead, and Ugni Blanc raisin and violet. Muscat is not a key Armagnac grape: it is typical of pisco and some aromatic grappas.":"白福爾帶來的是明顯的花香和果香，白玉霓則是葡萄乾和紫羅蘭。蜜思嘉不是 Armagnac 的主要品種：它是 pisco 和某些芳香型 grappa 的典型品種。","Why does column-distilled Armagnac stay full of character?":"為什麼用蒸餾柱蒸餾的 Armagnac 仍然充滿特色？","The column is short, with few plates, and distils to low strength":"蒸餾柱很矮、蒸餾板少，蒸餾到低濃度","The column has a great many plates and reaches neutral spirit":"蒸餾柱有非常多蒸餾板，達到中性烈酒","All the character comes from steeping fruit after distillation":"所有特色都來自蒸餾後浸泡水果","It is distilled three times in a column to concentrate aroma":"在蒸餾柱中蒸餾三次以濃縮香氣","A short column with few plates gives a low-strength spirit that keeps many congeners.":"蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱做出低濃度的烈酒，保留許多同屬物。","The higher the distillation strength, the less aroma remains, so a column taken to neutral spirit would give an almost characterless product. Armagnac's character comes from fermented fruit and distillation, not from later maceration. Extra distillations would raise strength, not character.":"蒸餾濃度越高，留下的香氣越少，所以蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱會做出幾乎沒有特色的產品。Armagnac 的特色來自發酵的水果和蒸餾，不是之後的浸漬。多蒸餾幾次會提高濃度，而不是特色。","A bartender wants a colourless Armagnac with lively fruit for a cocktail. What fits?":"一位調酒師想為一款調酒找一瓶無色、果香鮮活的 Armagnac。哪一款合適？","A Blanche, perhaps from Folle Blanche":"Blanche，也許是白福爾做的","A vintage Armagnac from a very old year":"非常老的年份的年份 Armagnac","An XO Armagnac charcoal-filtered to strip out its colour":"用木炭過濾去除顏色的 XO Armagnac","A Ténarèze Armagnac aged in new barrels":"在新桶中陳年的 Ténarèze Armagnac","Blanche never sees oak, so it is colourless, and Folle Blanche gives it expressive fruit.":"Blanche 從不接觸橡木，所以是無色的，白福爾則賦予它奔放的果香。","Blanche is made like other Armagnacs but without oak ageing. An old vintage or an Armagnac aged in new barrels will have colour and woody notes. Filtering an XO to remove its colour would not make it a recognised style and would strip out much of its aroma.":"Blanche 的做法和其他 Armagnac 一樣，只是不經橡木桶陳年。老年份或在新桶中陳年的 Armagnac 會有顏色和木質氣息。過濾 XO 來去除顏色並不會讓它成為公認的類型，還會去除大部分香氣。","Which statement about fruit spirits in general is true?":"關於水果烈酒整體，下列哪一項正確？","Any fruit can be used to make one":"任何水果都可以用來製作","Only grapes and apples are legally allowed":"法律只允許葡萄和蘋果","They must always spend at least two years in oak barrels":"一律必須在橡木桶中存放至少兩年","They are made only in France and Italy":"只在法國和義大利生產","Any fruit can become a spirit, which is why the category is so varied and found worldwide.":"任何水果都能製成烈酒，所以這個類別非常多樣，世界各地都有。","Wherever fruit is grown, a spirit is sooner or later made from it: cherries, plums, raspberries and many more. Many fruit spirits, such as grappa, usually never see wood. France and Italy are benchmarks, but not the only homes: think of South American pisco.":"凡是種水果的地方，遲早會有人用它做烈酒：櫻桃、李子、覆盆子等等。許多水果烈酒（例如 grappa）通常從不接觸木頭。法國和義大利是標竿，但不是唯一的產地：想想南美洲的 pisco。","A distiller steeps raspberries in neutral spirit and then redistils it. How can this spirit best be viewed?":"一位蒸餾師把覆盆子浸泡在中性烈酒中，再重新蒸餾。這款烈酒最好怎麼看待？","As a high-quality flavoured vodka":"高品質的調味伏特加","As a pomace brandy":"果渣白蘭地","As a brandy, since it is made from fruit juice fermented in a tank":"白蘭地，因為它用在槽中發酵的果汁製成","As a liqueur, since it always contains added sugar":"利口酒，因為它一定含有添加的糖","With no fermentation, the fruit flavours a neutral spirit: the result is closest to a fine flavoured vodka.":"沒有發酵，水果只是為中性烈酒調味：成品最接近優質的調味伏特加。","These spirits go by many local names, but the logic is that of flavoured vodka: a neutral base plus fruit aroma. There is no wine or fermented juice, so it is not a brandy, and grape skins play no part. Nothing requires added sugar, so it is not necessarily a liqueur.":"這些烈酒在各地有許多名稱，但邏輯就是調味伏特加：中性基酒加上水果香氣。沒有葡萄酒或發酵果汁，所以不是白蘭地，葡萄皮也沒有參與。沒有規定必須加糖，所以不一定是利口酒。","Which fruits are processed much like grapes, by pressing them and fermenting the juice?":"哪些水果的處理方式和葡萄很像，都是壓榨後讓果汁發酵？","Apples and pears":"蘋果和梨","Agave and sugar cane":"龍舌蘭和甘蔗","Barley and corn":"大麥和玉米","Juniper berries and coriander seeds":"杜松子和芫荽籽","Apples and pears are crushed and pressed, and their sugary juice ferments just like grape juice.":"蘋果和梨經過壓碎和壓榨，含糖的果汁就像葡萄汁一樣發酵。","The same pattern applies to cherries, plums, strawberries and raspberries. Agave and cane are the raw materials of Tequila and rum, not fruit. Barley and corn are starchy grains, while juniper and coriander are gin botanicals.":"櫻桃、李子、草莓和覆盆子也是同樣的模式。龍舌蘭和甘蔗是 Tequila 和蘭姆酒的原料，不是水果。大麥和玉米是含澱粉的穀物，杜松子和芫荽籽則是琴酒的植物性原料。","When white grapes are made into wine for brandy, what happens to the skins and seeds?":"白葡萄釀成用來做白蘭地的葡萄酒時，皮和籽怎麼處理？","They are removed after pressing, before fermentation":"壓榨後、發酵前就移除","They ferment with the juice to give colour":"與葡萄汁一起發酵以帶來顏色","They stay in the still to add aroma during distillation":"留在蒸餾器中，在蒸餾時增添香氣","They are added back to the wine just before distilling":"在蒸餾前才重新加回葡萄酒","White grapes are crushed and pressed; skins and seeds are set aside and only the juice ferments.":"白葡萄經過壓碎和壓榨；皮和籽被擱在一旁，只有汁液發酵。","A wine brandy needs only the juice: the white skins set aside can, however, become the base of a pomace spirit. Fermenting with skins for colour is how red wine is made. Putting skins back into the wine or the still would bring herbaceous pomace notes, not those of a wine brandy.":"葡萄酒白蘭地只需要汁液：不過擱在一旁的白葡萄皮可以成為果渣烈酒的原料。帶皮發酵以取得顏色是紅酒的釀法。把皮放回葡萄酒或蒸餾器會帶來果渣的草本氣息，而不是葡萄酒白蘭地的氣息。","Why does pomace from a red wine cellar already contain alcohol?":"為什麼來自紅酒酒窖的果渣已經含有酒精？","The skins fermented with the juice and pressing never gets all the wine out":"皮與葡萄汁一起發酵，而壓榨永遠無法把葡萄酒全部榨出","Red wine producers add spirit to the skins before sending them off":"紅酒生產者在送出葡萄皮前先加了烈酒","Black grape skins naturally hold alcohol even before fermentation":"紅葡萄的皮在發酵前就天然含有酒精","Yeast keeps fermenting the dry skins for months after pressing":"壓榨後酵母還繼續讓乾的葡萄皮發酵好幾個月","In red winemaking the skins stay in the juice throughout fermentation and hold on to some wine even after pressing.":"釀造紅酒時，皮在整個發酵過程中都泡在葡萄汁裡，即使壓榨後仍留有一些葡萄酒。","After fermentation the wine is drained off and the skins are pressed, but some wine always stays trapped, which is why they can be distilled at once. No one adds spirit to the pomace, and alcohol only comes from fermenting sugar. Pressed skins do not go on fermenting for months.":"發酵後把葡萄酒排出並壓榨葡萄皮，但總有一些葡萄酒被困在裡面，所以可以立刻蒸餾。沒有人在果渣中加烈酒，酒精只來自糖的發酵。壓榨過的皮不會繼續發酵好幾個月。","Which statement about pomace is NOT correct?":"關於果渣，下列哪一項不正確？","White grape pomace is distilled at once, with no fermentation":"白葡萄果渣不經發酵就立刻蒸餾","It is the mass of skins discarded by winemakers":"它是釀酒師丟棄的一堆葡萄皮","The skins give pomace spirits their herbaceous and spicy notes":"葡萄皮賦予果渣烈酒草本和香料氣息","Black grape pomace reaches the distillery already soaked in wine":"紅葡萄果渣送到蒸餾廠時已經浸滿葡萄酒","White skins are removed before fermentation: they hold juice, not alcohol, so they must first be fermented with water.":"白葡萄的皮在發酵前就被移除：裡面有葡萄汁，沒有酒精，所以必須先加水發酵。","Distilling with no fermentation only works for black pomace, which fermented along with the red wine. The other three statements are true: pomace is the discarded skins, it brings herbaceous and spicy notes, and black pomace already contains alcohol. The trap is mixing up the two colours.":"不經發酵就蒸餾只適用於紅葡萄果渣，因為它已隨紅酒一起發酵。其他三項都正確：果渣是被丟棄的葡萄皮，它帶來草本和香料氣息，而紅葡萄果渣已含有酒精。陷阱在於把兩種顏色搞混。","Why do grape brandy producers value the same variety grown in different areas?":"為什麼葡萄白蘭地的生產者重視在不同區域種植的同一品種？","Each area gives grapes of a different quality and more blending options":"每個區域的葡萄品質不同，調和的選項也更多","The law requires at least three areas in every brandy":"法律規定每款白蘭地至少要用三個區域","Grapes from different areas ferment at different speeds, which saves time in the cellar":"不同區域的葡萄發酵速度不同，可節省酒窖的時間","Mixing areas is the only way to raise the alcohol level":"混合不同區域是提高酒精濃度的唯一方法","The same variety changes character with where it grows, and that diversity enriches the blends.":"同一品種會隨種植地點改變特色，這種多樣性讓調和更豐富。","Variety and growing site are two levers distillers use to get different spirits for blending: Cognac, with its sub-regions, is the example. No general rule sets a number of areas. Fermentation speed and alcohol level are not the reason for this choice.":"品種和種植地點是蒸餾師用來取得不同烈酒以供調和的兩種手段：有多個子產區的 Cognac 就是例子。沒有通則規定區域的數量。發酵速度和酒精濃度不是這樣選擇的原因。","Why do grape distillers have to store wine before distilling it?":"為什麼葡萄蒸餾師必須在蒸餾前先存放葡萄酒？","Grapes are picked once a year, but distilling it all takes months":"葡萄一年採收一次，但全部蒸餾完要好幾個月","Wine must age three years before it may be distilled":"葡萄酒必須陳年三年才能蒸餾","Freshly made wine is too strong to be distilled safely":"剛釀好的葡萄酒太烈，無法安全蒸餾","The yeast has to be removed by a long rest in oak casks":"必須在橡木桶中長時間靜置來去除酵母","There is only one harvest, so the wine waits its turn for a few months, protected by its acidity and alcohol.":"一年只有一次採收，所以葡萄酒要排隊等幾個月，靠它的酸度和酒精保護。","Stills cannot distil all the wine in a few days, so the wine waits. No years of ageing are needed; in fact the wine must be distilled within a few months. Wine is far weaker than a spirit, and oak is not how yeast is removed.":"蒸餾器無法在幾天內蒸餾完所有的葡萄酒，所以葡萄酒要等待。不需要陳年好幾年；事實上葡萄酒必須在幾個月內蒸餾。葡萄酒比烈酒淡得多，而橡木桶也不是去除酵母的方法。","For grape brandies, which source of blending variety is relatively uncommon?":"對葡萄白蘭地來說，哪一種調和多樣性的來源相對少見？","Using different types of still":"使用不同類型的蒸餾器","Using different grape varieties":"使用不同的葡萄品種","Using grapes grown in different areas of the same producing region":"使用同一產區內不同區域種植的葡萄","Making different choices during maturation":"在熟成時做出不同的選擇","Grape brandy makers get variety mainly from grapes, areas and maturation, rarely from different stills.":"葡萄白蘭地的生產者主要從葡萄、區域和熟成取得多樣性，很少靠不同的蒸餾器。","Unlike some other categories, such as certain rums, grape brandies rarely combine spirits from different stills. Varieties, areas and maturation choices are the classic levers, though local law may limit them. In Cognac, for example, the type of still is fixed.":"與某些其他類別（例如某些蘭姆酒）不同，葡萄白蘭地很少結合來自不同蒸餾器的烈酒。品種、區域和熟成的選擇是經典的手段，不過當地法律可能加以限制。例如在 Cognac，蒸餾器的類型是固定的。","Pot or column: what often decides which still a fruit spirit producer uses?":"壺式還是柱式：水果烈酒生產者用哪一種蒸餾器，往往由什麼決定？","Local laws":"當地法律","The colour of the harvested fruit":"採收水果的顏色","The size of the crop in that particular year":"該年收成的多寡","The yeast strain used for fermentation":"發酵所用的酵母菌株","Both still types are possible for fruit spirits, but local law often decides which one is used.":"水果烈酒兩種蒸餾器都可以用，但往往由當地法律決定用哪一種。","Cognac must use pot stills, while Armagnac almost always uses its short column: both are examples of local rules. Fruit colour, crop size and yeast affect style, but they do not decide the type of still.":"Cognac 必須用壺式蒸餾器，Armagnac 則幾乎都用它的矮蒸餾柱：兩者都是當地規定的例子。水果顏色、收成多寡和酵母會影響風格，但不決定蒸餾器的類型。","Among fruit spirits not made from grapes, which are the exception in normally being matured in oak?":"在不是用葡萄做的水果烈酒中，哪一種是通常會在橡木桶中熟成的例外？","Apple brandies":"蘋果白蘭地","Cherry spirits":"櫻桃烈酒","Central European plum spirits":"中歐的李子烈酒","Raspberry spirits made by maceration":"以浸漬製成的覆盆子烈酒","Like grape brandies, apple brandies are usually oak-matured; other fruit spirits rest in inert vessels.":"和葡萄白蘭地一樣，蘋果白蘭地通常在橡木桶中熟成；其他水果烈酒則在惰性容器中靜置。","Cherries, plums and berries give spirits prized for purity and expressiveness, which wood would mask, so they rest in steel or glass. Normandy's Calvados is the classic oak-aged apple brandy. Pomace spirits such as grappa usually skip wood too.":"櫻桃、李子和莓果做出的烈酒以純淨和表現力著稱，木頭會把這些掩蓋，所以它們在鋼或玻璃容器中靜置。諾曼第的 Calvados 是經典的橡木桶陳年蘋果白蘭地。grappa 這類果渣烈酒通常也不過木桶。","At a tasting, some people prefer not to add water to fruit spirits. Why?":"在品飲時，有些人偏好不在水果烈酒中加水。為什麼？","Water can make the aromas less clear":"水可能讓香氣變得不那麼清晰","Water instantly turns every fruit spirit cloudy":"水會立刻讓所有水果烈酒變混濁","They are already bottled at a very low strength":"它們裝瓶時的濃度本來就很低","Water wipes out every oak note and leaves only alcohol, making them impossible to judge":"水會抹去所有橡木氣息、只留下酒精，讓人無法評判","Water usually opens up aromas, but with fruit spirits it sometimes blurs them, in which case they are best tasted neat.":"水通常能讓香氣展開，但對水果烈酒有時反而讓香氣模糊，這時最好純飲品嚐。","For other spirits, diluting half and half, always in the same way, is advised so comparisons are fair. With fruit spirits some people find the aromas less clear, so they may skip this step. Cloudiness, low strength or oak notes, which many fruit spirits do not even have, are not the reason.":"對其他烈酒，建議一律以相同方式一比一稀釋，這樣比較才公平。對水果烈酒，有些人覺得香氣會變得不清晰，所以可能略過這一步。混濁、濃度低或橡木氣息（許多水果烈酒根本沒有）都不是原因。","Before distillation, what is the wine made from Ugni Blanc like?":"蒸餾前，白玉霓釀出的葡萄酒是什麼樣子？","Rather thin and not aromatic":"相當單薄，沒有什麼香氣","Deeply coloured and tannic":"顏色深、單寧重","Intensely floral, like a Muscat":"花香濃郁，像蜜思嘉","Sweet, low in acid and already high in alcohol":"甜、酸度低，而且酒精已經很高","Ugni Blanc makes plain, unaromatic wine, but once distilled it reveals raisin and violet.":"白玉霓釀出平淡、不芳香的葡萄酒，但蒸餾後會展現葡萄乾和紫羅蘭。","It is an acidic, neutral white grape, exactly the profile distillers look for. Colour and tannin belong to black grapes; intense aroma is typical of Muscat, the aromatic grape of pisco. A sweet, low-acid wine would keep poorly while waiting to be distilled.":"它是酸度高、中性的白葡萄，正是蒸餾師想要的輪廓。顏色和單寧屬於紅葡萄；濃郁的香氣是蜜思嘉的特徵，也就是 pisco 的芳香型葡萄。甜而低酸的葡萄酒在等待蒸餾時很難保存。","How many sub-regions is the Cognac area divided into?":"Cognac 產區分成幾個子產區？","Six":"六個","Ten":"十個","Cognac has six sub-regions, three of which are especially highly regarded.":"Cognac 有六個子產區，其中三個評價特別高。","Three is a trap: those are the most prized sub-regions and the ones seen most on labels, not the total. Two is the number of key Armagnac sub-regions. Ten matches no division at all.":"三個是陷阱：那是最受珍視、最常出現在酒標上的子產區，不是總數。兩個是 Armagnac 主要子產區的數目。十個則與任何劃分都不相符。","Which three Cognac sub-regions are most likely to appear on a label?":"Cognac 的哪三個子產區最可能出現在酒標上？","Grande Champagne, Petite Champagne and Borderies":"Grande Champagne、Petite Champagne 和 Borderies","Bas Armagnac, Ténarèze and Grande Champagne":"Bas Armagnac、Ténarèze 和 Grande Champagne","Fine Champagne, Napoléon and Hors d'âge":"Fine Champagne、Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge","Normandy, Borderies and Petite Champagne":"諾曼第、Borderies 和 Petite Champagne","They are the three most prized sub-regions, all around the town of Cognac.":"它們是最受珍視的三個子產區，都在 Cognac 鎮周圍。","Bas Armagnac and Ténarèze belong to Armagnac, and Normandy is the home of Calvados. Napoléon and Hors d'âge are age terms, and Fine Champagne is a blend of two sub-regions, not a sub-region itself.":"Bas Armagnac 和 Ténarèze 屬於 Armagnac，諾曼第是 Calvados 的故鄉。Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge 是年數術語，Fine Champagne 是兩個子產區的調和，本身不是子產區。","A Cognac label says Borderies. What does this mean?":"一瓶 Cognac 的酒標寫著 Borderies。這是什麼意思？","All the grapes come from the Borderies sub-region":"所有葡萄都來自 Borderies 子產區","At least half of the grapes come from Borderies":"至少一半的葡萄來自 Borderies","The Cognac was matured in a warehouse located there":"這款 Cognac 在位於那裡的酒庫中熟成","It is a blend of Borderies and Grande Champagne":"它是 Borderies 和 Grande Champagne 的調和","If a sub-region is named on the label, 100% of the grapes must come from there.":"如果酒標上標示某個子產區，葡萄必須 100% 來自那裡。","The 50% threshold applies only to Grande Champagne inside a Fine Champagne, not to single sub-regions. The name says where the grapes grew, not where the spirit matured. A blend of Borderies and Grande Champagne cannot carry either name.":"50% 的門檻只適用於 Fine Champagne 中的 Grande Champagne，不適用於單一子產區。這個名稱說的是葡萄在哪裡生長，不是烈酒在哪裡熟成。Borderies 和 Grande Champagne 的調和不能標示其中任何一個名稱。","Where are the Cognac sub-regions considered the best located?":"被認為最好的 Cognac 子產區位於哪裡？","Around the town of Cognac itself":"就在 Cognac 鎮周圍","Along the Atlantic coast, far from the town":"沿著大西洋岸，遠離該鎮","Near the Pyrenees, in the part south of Bordeaux":"靠近庇里牛斯山，在波爾多以南的部分","On the hills of Normandy":"在諾曼第的山丘上","Grande Champagne, Petite Champagne and Borderies surround the town that gives the spirit its name.":"Grande Champagne、Petite Champagne 和 Borderies 環繞著這款烈酒得名的城鎮。","The whole Cognac area lies just north of Bordeaux, with its quality heart around the town. South of Bordeaux is Armagnac country, not Cognac. Normandy, in northern France, is the land of Calvados.":"整個 Cognac 產區就在波爾多北邊，品質的核心在該鎮周圍。波爾多以南是 Armagnac 的地盤，不是 Cognac。法國北部的諾曼第則是 Calvados 的產地。","A Cognac blends 40% Grande Champagne and 60% Petite Champagne. Can it be labelled Fine Champagne?":"一款 Cognac 調和了 40% Grande Champagne 和 60% Petite Champagne。它可以標示為 Fine Champagne 嗎？","No: Grande Champagne must make up at least half":"不行：Grande Champagne 必須至少占一半","Yes: any blend of the two sub-regions qualifies":"可以：這兩個子產區的任何調和都符合資格","Yes, provided it is at least an XO with long ageing":"可以，只要至少是經過長期陳年的 XO","No: Fine Champagne must be 100% Grande Champagne":"不行：Fine Champagne 必須是 100% Grande Champagne","Fine Champagne requires Grande and Petite Champagne with at least 50% Grande Champagne, so 40% is not enough.":"Fine Champagne 要求 Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne，其中 Grande Champagne 至少 50%，所以 40% 不夠。","The two sub-regions are right, but the proportion is not. A 100% Grande Champagne would simply be called Grande Champagne. Age is irrelevant: Fine Champagne tells you where the grapes came from, not how long the Cognac aged.":"兩個子產區是對的，但比例不對。100% Grande Champagne 就直接稱為 Grande Champagne。年數無關緊要：Fine Champagne 告訴你葡萄來自哪裡，不是 Cognac 陳年了多久。","A Cognac blends spirits from Grande Champagne and Borderies. Which origin term can it carry?":"一款 Cognac 調和了 Grande Champagne 和 Borderies 的烈酒。它可以標示哪一個產地術語？","Just Cognac, with no sub-region name and no Fine Champagne":"只能標 Cognac，沒有子產區名稱，也不能標 Fine Champagne","Grande Champagne, since it contains some":"Grande Champagne，因為裡面含有一些","Borderies, if that sub-region dominates the blend":"Borderies，如果這個子產區在調和中占多數","A sub-region on the label needs 100% of its grapes from there, and Fine Champagne allows only Grande and Petite Champagne.":"酒標上的子產區要求葡萄 100% 來自那裡，而 Fine Champagne 只允許 Grande Champagne 和 Petite Champagne。","Borderies is highly regarded but is not part of Fine Champagne, which covers only the two Champagnes. Neither Grande Champagne nor Borderies can appear alone, because neither accounts for all the grapes. That leaves just the name Cognac.":"Borderies 評價很高，但不屬於 Fine Champagne，後者只涵蓋兩個 Champagne。Grande Champagne 和 Borderies 都不能單獨出現，因為兩者都沒有涵蓋全部的葡萄。剩下的就只有 Cognac 這個名稱。","How many times is Cognac distilled, and in what stills?":"Cognac 蒸餾幾次？用什麼蒸餾器？","Twice, in copper pot stills":"兩次，用銅製壺式蒸餾器","Once, in a short column with few plates":"一次，用蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱","Three times, in copper pot stills":"三次，用銅製壺式蒸餾器","Continuously, in a tall column with many plates":"連續蒸餾，用蒸餾板多的高蒸餾柱","The law requires double distillation in copper pot stills.":"法律規定在銅製壺式蒸餾器中進行二次蒸餾。","The short column with few plates belongs to Armagnac, while a tall column would make a much lighter spirit. Triple pot distillation is typical of many Irish whiskeys, not Cognac.":"蒸餾板少的矮蒸餾柱屬於 Armagnac，高蒸餾柱則會做出清淡得多的烈酒。壺式三次蒸餾是許多愛爾蘭威士忌的典型做法，不是 Cognac。","In a Cognac distillery, what is the chapiteau?":"在 Cognac 的蒸餾廠中，chapiteau 是什麼？","The olive-shaped still head":"橄欖形的蒸餾器頂部","The curved tube carrying vapours to the condenser":"把蒸氣送到冷凝器的彎管","The cold water tank holding the coil":"裝著盤管的冷水槽","The pot where the wine is heated at the start of each run":"每次蒸餾開始時加熱葡萄酒的壺身","Chapiteau is the local name for the still head, often olive-shaped in Cognac.":"chapiteau 是蒸餾器頂部在當地的名稱，在 Cognac 常呈橄欖形。","Still heads come in many shapes and sizes; in Cognac the term is chapiteau. The curved tube to the condenser is the col de cygne, and the tank with the coil is the worm tub. The pot is the vessel that holds the wine.":"蒸餾器頂部有許多形狀和大小；在 Cognac 這個術語是 chapiteau。通往冷凝器的彎管是 col de cygne，裝著盤管的水槽是蟲桶冷凝器。壺身是盛裝葡萄酒的容器。","In Cognac terms, what is the col de cygne?":"在 Cognac 的用語中，col de cygne 是什麼？","The swan neck linking the still head to the condenser":"連接蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器的天鵝頸","The olive-shaped head sitting on top of the pot":"位於壺身上方的橄欖形頂部","The copper coil sunk in the condenser's cold water":"浸在冷凝器冷水中的銅製盤管","The drain at the bottom of the pot":"壺身底部的排放口","Col de cygne means swan neck: the curving tube between the still head and the condenser.":"col de cygne 的意思是天鵝頸：蒸餾器頂部和冷凝器之間的彎管。","In Scotland the same terms can mean slightly different parts, but in Cognac the swan neck is this tube. The olive-shaped head is the chapiteau, and the coil belongs to the worm tub. The drain empties the pot at the end of a run.":"在蘇格蘭，同樣的術語可能指稍微不同的部位，但在 Cognac，天鵝頸就是這條管子。橄欖形的頂部是 chapiteau，盤管則屬於蟲桶冷凝器。排放口在蒸餾結束時排空壺身。","How does the worm tub required in Cognac work?":"Cognac 規定使用的蟲桶冷凝器如何運作？","Vapours condense in a coil sunk in a big tank of cold water":"蒸氣在浸於大型冷水槽的盤管中冷凝","Vapours rise through many plates and condense at the top of a column":"蒸氣穿過許多蒸餾板上升，並在蒸餾柱頂部冷凝","Cold water flows through many small tubes inside a narrow vessel":"冷水流經狹窄容器內的許多小管","The hot spirit is left to cool overnight in oak casks":"把熱的烈酒放在橡木桶中冷卻一整夜","A single copper coil runs through a tank as big as the still, filled with constantly renewed cold water.":"單一條銅製盤管穿過與蒸餾器一樣大的水槽，槽中裝滿不斷更新的冷水。","It is an old design, whereas almost everywhere else uses modern shell-and-tube condensers, the ones with many small tubes. Plates belong to column stills, which Cognac does not use. Wood is for maturing the spirit, not condensing it.":"這是古老的設計，而幾乎其他所有地方都使用現代的殼管式冷凝器，也就是有許多小管的那種。蒸餾板屬於柱式蒸餾器，Cognac 並不使用。木頭是用來熟成烈酒的，不是用來冷凝。","Many large Cognac houses buy spirit from independent distillers. Why?":"許多大型 Cognac 酒商向獨立蒸餾師購買烈酒。為什麼？","They cannot make all they need, so others distil it to their recipe":"他們無法自己做出所需的全部產量，所以由別人依他們的配方蒸餾","The law forbids large houses from owning stills":"法律禁止大型酒商擁有蒸餾器","Bought-in spirit is exempt from two years in oak":"買進的烈酒可免除兩年橡木桶的規定","So it can be sold as a single small producer's Cognac":"這樣就能當作單一小生產者的 Cognac 販售","Demand exceeds their capacity, so they hand part of the distilling to others who follow their recipe.":"需求超過他們的產能，所以把一部分蒸餾交給遵循其配方的其他人。","This spirit is used alongside what the house makes itself. At the other end, some small Cognac distillers grow the grapes they then ferment, distil and mature. Every Cognac, bought in or not, follows the same rules, including two years in oak.":"這些烈酒會與酒商自己做的一起使用。另一端則有一些小型 Cognac 蒸餾師自己種葡萄，再自行發酵、蒸餾和熟成。每款 Cognac，不論是否買進，都遵守相同的規定，包括兩年橡木桶。","What do the letters VSOP stand for?":"VSOP 這幾個字母代表什麼？","VSOP stands for Very Superior Old Pale; VS is Very Special and XO is Extra Old.":"VSOP 代表 Very Superior Old Pale；VS 是 Very Special，XO 是 Extra Old。","The abbreviations are in English by trading tradition, but in Cognac they have a precise legal meaning. Very Special belongs to VS, not VSOP. Vintage is unrelated: these terms give a minimum age, not a harvest year.":"這些縮寫因貿易傳統而使用英文，但在 Cognac 有明確的法律意義。Very Special 屬於 VS，不是 VSOP。Vintage（年份）與此無關：這些術語表示最低年數，不是採收年份。","On a Cognac, which terms belong to the same top age category as XO?":"在 Cognac 上，哪些術語與 XO 屬於同一個最高年數類別？","Napoléon and Hors d'âge":"Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge","VS and VSOP":"VS 和 VSOP","Fine Champagne and Borderies, shown on the same label":"標在同一張酒標上的 Fine Champagne 和 Borderies","Blanche and Vintage":"Blanche 和 Vintage","Napoléon and Hors d'âge are age terms that guarantee the same minimum as XO.":"Napoléon 和 Hors d'âge 是年數術語，保證的最低年數與 XO 相同。","VS and VSOP are younger categories. Fine Champagne and Borderies tell you where the grapes came from, not the age. Blanche and Vintage are styles typical of Armagnac, rare or absent in Cognac.":"VS 和 VSOP 是較年輕的類別。Fine Champagne 和 Borderies 告訴你葡萄來自哪裡，不是年數。Blanche 和 Vintage 是 Armagnac 的典型類型，在 Cognac 很少見或不存在。","Compared with a VS from the same producer, what does a VSOP usually show?":"與同一生產者的 VS 相比，VSOP 通常表現出什麼？","More richness and body, with some aromas of maturity":"更豐富、酒體更飽滿，帶一些成熟的香氣","A lighter, sharper texture with less oak":"質地更輕、更銳利，橡木味更少","A clear colour and pure grape aromas, with no trace of oak":"顏色清澈、葡萄香氣純淨，沒有一絲橡木味","Marked prune notes from Baco grapes":"來自巴科葡萄的明顯李子乾氣息","VSOP is richer and fuller than VS and starts to show aromas of maturity.":"VSOP 比 VS 更豐富、更飽滿，並開始出現成熟的香氣。","A slightly sharp texture is typical of young VS. Every Cognac spends at least two years in oak, so a clear, unoaked colour is impossible. Baco's prune note is an Armagnac trait.":"略顯銳利的質地是年輕 VS 的典型特徵。每款 Cognac 都在橡木桶中至少兩年，所以不可能有清澈、未過桶的顏色。巴科的李子乾氣息是 Armagnac 的特徵。","A Cognac shows seamlessly blended raisin, floral, oak and rancio notes, with a smooth mouthfeel. Which category does it best match?":"一款 Cognac 表現出融合無間的葡萄乾、花香、橡木和 rancio 氣息，口感柔順。它最符合哪個類別？","A fine XO":"優質的 XO","A typical VS":"典型的 VS","A Blanche Armagnac made only from Folle Blanche":"只用白福爾製成的 Blanche Armagnac","A young VSOP straight out of new casks":"剛從新桶取出的年輕 VSOP","Rancio and a seamless harmony of fruit, flowers and oak are the hallmark of the best XOs.":"rancio 以及果香、花香和橡木的和諧融合，是最好的 XO 的標誌。","Rancio comes from many years of contact with wood and oxygen, which a VS or young VSOP has not had. VS shows distinct fruit and oak, sometimes with a sharp texture. A Blanche never sees oak, so it can have neither oak notes nor rancio.":"rancio 來自與木頭和氧氣多年的接觸，VS 或年輕的 VSOP 沒有這樣的經歷。VS 表現出分明的果香和橡木味，有時質地銳利。Blanche 從不接觸橡木，所以既不可能有橡木氣息，也不可能有 rancio。","In a tasting note, how is the sweetness of a typical Cognac best described?":"在品飲筆記中，典型 Cognac 的甜度最好怎麼描述？","Dry, because no spirit ever receives sugar":"不甜，因為沒有任何烈酒會加糖","Medium, with an obvious sweetness":"中等，有明顯的甜味","Sweet, like a liqueur":"甜，像利口酒","Most Cognacs get a small sugar addition: they do not taste sweet, but the texture gives it away.":"大多數 Cognac 會加少量的糖：喝起來不甜，但質地洩露了這一點。","Tasting assesses sugar added after distillation, a traditional practice in Cognac. Medium and sweet describe clearly noticeable sweetness, whereas a typical Cognac does not taste sweet. Dry would only be right with no addition at all.":"品飲時評估的是蒸餾後添加的糖，這在 Cognac 是傳統做法。中等和甜描述的是清楚可察覺的甜味，而典型的 Cognac 喝起來並不甜。只有完全沒加糖時，不甜才是正確的。","Why do Cognac houses mature spirits in warehouses in different places?":"為什麼 Cognac 酒商把烈酒放在不同地點的酒庫中熟成？","Different conditions create variety for blending":"不同的環境為調和創造多樣性","The law makes each sub-region keep its spirits apart":"法律要求每個子產區的烈酒分開存放","To cut to zero the evaporation each cask loses every year":"把每個桶每年的蒸發損失降到零","Because one warehouse may hold only one age category":"因為一座酒庫只能存放一個年數類別","Temperature and conditions change from one warehouse to another, and so does maturation: more variety for the blender.":"溫度和環境因酒庫而異，熟成也跟著不同：調和師有更多樣的選擇。","In Cognac, using different warehouses has become a speciality, alongside varieties, sub-regions and ages. No law requires sub-regions or ages to be stored separately by warehouse. Evaporation, the angels' share, cannot be eliminated.":"在 Cognac，使用不同的酒庫已成為一門專長，與品種、子產區和年數並列。沒有法律規定子產區或年數必須分酒庫存放。蒸發，也就是天使的分享，是無法消除的。","Where do rancio aromas such as leather and mushroom in a very old Cognac mainly come from?":"極老的 Cognac 中，皮革和蘑菇等 rancio 香氣主要來自哪裡？","Slow reactions between spirit and oak compounds and oxygen":"烈酒與橡木化合物和氧氣之間緩慢的反應","From grape skins left to ferment with the base wine":"來自與基酒一起發酵的葡萄皮","From the copper of the worm tub coil":"來自蟲桶冷凝器盤管的銅","From the small sugar addition made just before final bottling":"來自最後裝瓶前加入的少量糖","Over time, compounds from the spirit and the oak react with each other and with oxygen entering through the wood, creating rancio.":"隨著時間，烈酒和橡木的化合物彼此反應，也與透過木頭進入的氧氣反應，產生 rancio。","That is why rancio is found in spirits aged for a long time in cask, such as fine XOs. Skins give herbaceous notes to pomace spirits, not rancio. Copper and sugar affect purity and texture; they do not create leather or mushroom.":"所以 rancio 出現在長期桶陳的烈酒中，例如優質的 XO。葡萄皮為果渣烈酒帶來草本氣息，不是 rancio。銅和糖影響的是純淨度和質地；它們不會產生皮革或蘑菇氣息。","Which comparison between Cognac and Armagnac producers is correct?":"關於 Cognac 和 Armagnac 的生產者，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Cognac is dominated by big companies, Armagnac by small producers":"Cognac 由大公司主導，Armagnac 由小生產者主導","Both are dominated by four big companies":"兩者都由四家大公司主導","Armagnac is dominated by big companies, Cognac by small family farms":"Armagnac 由大公司主導，Cognac 由小型家庭農場主導","Both are made only by cooperatives":"兩者都只由合作社生產","Four big companies dominate Cognac, while small producers are the norm in Armagnac.":"四家大公司主導 Cognac，小生產者則是 Armagnac 的常態。","That is why Armagnac labels often say Château, marking a small producer. Cognac has small distillers too, but the market is in the hands of the big houses. Cooperatives are not the dominant model in either region.":"所以 Armagnac 的酒標上常寫著 Château，代表小生產者。Cognac 也有小型蒸餾師，但市場掌握在大酒商手中。合作社在兩個產區都不是主流模式。","Which grape variety is the most widely planted in Armagnac?":"Armagnac 種植最廣的是哪一個葡萄品種？","Ugni Blanc":"白玉霓","Folle Blanche":"白福爾","As in Cognac, the most widely planted variety is Ugni Blanc.":"和 Cognac 一樣，種植最廣的品種是白玉霓。","The difference is that Armagnac makes much more use of the other permitted varieties. Baco and Folle Blanche are the most important of these and bring typical traits, but they are not the most planted. Muscat is pisco's aromatic grape.":"差別在於 Armagnac 更常使用其他獲准的品種。巴科和白福爾是其中最重要的，帶來典型的特徵，但不是種植最多的。蜜思嘉是 pisco 的芳香型葡萄。","What type of still is most Armagnac distilled in?":"大多數 Armagnac 用哪一種蒸餾器蒸餾？","A short continuous column unique to the region":"該產區特有的矮連續式蒸餾柱","A copper pot still, double distilled as in Cognac":"銅製壺式蒸餾器，像 Cognac 一樣二次蒸餾","A tall multi-plate column for neutral spirit":"製作中性烈酒的多層蒸餾板高蒸餾柱","A system of three pot stills":"三座壺式蒸餾器組成的系統","Armagnac uses its own continuous column, which must be short with few plates.":"Armagnac 使用自己的連續式蒸餾柱，必須矮而蒸餾板少。","Double pot distillation is Cognac's rule. A tall column with many plates would give an almost neutral spirit, the opposite of Armagnac style. Three stills in a row are not part of this region's tradition.":"壺式二次蒸餾是 Cognac 的規定。蒸餾板多的高蒸餾柱會做出近乎中性的烈酒，與 Armagnac 的風格相反。三座蒸餾器串聯不屬於這個產區的傳統。","Are pot stills allowed in Armagnac?":"Armagnac 允許使用壺式蒸餾器嗎？","Yes, but they are very rarely used":"允許，但很少使用","No, the law bans them outright":"不允許，法律完全禁止","Yes, and they produce most Armagnac":"允許，而且大多數 Armagnac 用它製作","Only for Blanche meant for cocktails, never for aged Armagnac":"只限用於調酒的 Blanche，陳年 Armagnac 絕不使用","Pot stills are permitted, but almost every producer prefers the local column.":"壺式蒸餾器是允許的，但幾乎每位生產者都偏好當地的蒸餾柱。","The key point is rarity, not a ban: the short column is the near-universal choice. Blanche is distilled exactly like other Armagnacs; the only difference is that it skips oak.":"重點是少見，不是禁止：矮蒸餾柱幾乎是所有人的選擇。Blanche 的蒸餾方式和其他 Armagnac 完全一樣；唯一的差別是它不過橡木桶。","What do Armagnac, Bourbon and rhum agricole have in common?":"Armagnac、Bourbon 和 rhum agricole 有什麼共同點？","Characterful spirits made in a column at fairly low strength":"都是用蒸餾柱在相當低的濃度製成、特色鮮明的烈酒","They must all mature in new charred oak":"都必須在炙燒過的新橡木桶中熟成","They are all made from acidic, low-aroma white grapes grown in France":"都用法國種植、酸度高而香氣少的白葡萄製成","They are all double distilled in pot stills":"都在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾兩次","All three leave a column at a strength low enough to keep plenty of congeners, so they are full of character.":"三者離開蒸餾柱時的濃度都夠低，保留了大量同屬物，所以特色十足。","They show that a column does not have to mean a light spirit: what matters is the strength at which the hearts are drawn off. New charred oak is a Bourbon rule, not an Armagnac one. Only Armagnac comes from grapes, and none of the three is typically double pot distilled.":"它們說明蒸餾柱不一定代表清淡的烈酒：重要的是抽取酒心時的濃度。炙燒過的新橡木桶是 Bourbon 的規定，不是 Armagnac 的。只有 Armagnac 來自葡萄，而三者通常都不是壺式二次蒸餾。","A label reads Ténarèze. What is it?":"酒標上寫著 Ténarèze。它是什麼？","An Armagnac sub-region":"Armagnac 的子產區","A Cognac age term":"Cognac 的年數術語","A grape variety used for Blanche Armagnac":"用於 Blanche Armagnac 的葡萄品種","A type of copper worm tub condenser":"一種銅製的蟲桶冷凝器","Ténarèze is, with Bas Armagnac, one of Armagnac's two important sub-regions.":"Ténarèze 與 Bas Armagnac 是 Armagnac 的兩個重要子產區。","Age terms are abbreviations such as VS, VSOP and XO. The variety suited to Blanche is Folle Blanche. The worm tub is typical of Cognac.":"年數術語是 VS、VSOP 和 XO 這類縮寫。適合 Blanche 的品種是白福爾。蟲桶冷凝器是 Cognac 的典型設備。","How is Blanche Armagnac made?":"Blanche Armagnac 是怎麼做的？","Like other Armagnacs, but with no oak maturation":"和其他 Armagnac 一樣，但不經橡木桶熟成","From pomace instead of wine":"用果渣而不是葡萄酒","By steeping fresh grapes in neutral spirit and redistilling it all":"把新鮮葡萄浸泡在中性烈酒中，再全部重新蒸餾","In a pot still, then charcoal-filtered":"用壺式蒸餾器，再以木炭過濾","Blanche follows the same process as any Armagnac; the only difference is that it never sees oak and stays colourless.":"Blanche 的製程和任何 Armagnac 相同；唯一的差別是它從不接觸橡木，保持無色。","The base is still wine, usually distilled in the local column. Pomace makes a different kind of spirit, and steeping in neutral spirit applies to other fruits. The lack of colour comes not from filtering but from wood never being involved.":"基底仍然是葡萄酒，通常用當地的蒸餾柱蒸餾。果渣做出的是另一種烈酒，浸泡在中性烈酒中則適用於其他水果。沒有顏色不是因為過濾，而是因為從來沒有用到木頭。","Which statement about vintage-dated brandies is correct?":"關於標示年份的白蘭地，下列哪一項正確？","They are common in Armagnac but rare in Cognac":"在 Armagnac 很常見，在 Cognac 很少見","They are common in Cognac but banned in Armagnac":"在 Cognac 很常見，在 Armagnac 被禁止","The year shows the average age of a blend of different ages":"年份表示不同年數調和的平均年數","They are banned in both Cognac and Armagnac":"在 Cognac 和 Armagnac 都被禁止","Vintages are a hallmark of Armagnac, whereas nearly all Cognac is a blend of ages.":"年份酒是 Armagnac 的標誌，而幾乎所有 Cognac 都是不同年數的調和。","A vintage Armagnac comes from grapes of a single harvest, so it is not a blend of ages and the year is not an average. In Cognac, vintages exist but are rare, not banned.":"年份 Armagnac 來自單一採收年的葡萄，所以不是不同年數的調和，年份也不是平均值。在 Cognac，年份酒存在但很少見，並未被禁止。","A brandy made outside the French regions says VSOP on the label. What does that term guarantee?":"一款在法國產區之外製作的白蘭地，酒標上寫著 VSOP。這個術語保證什麼？","No legally defined age":"沒有法律定義的年數","The same minimum years in oak as Cognac":"與 Cognac 相同的最低橡木桶年數","That it was made from Ugni Blanc grown in the Cognac area":"它用 Cognac 產區種植的白玉霓製成","That it was distilled in France and bottled abroad":"它在法國蒸餾、在國外裝瓶","These terms are widely copied, but outside the French regions that regulate them they have no legal definition.":"這些術語被廣泛仿用，但在規範它們的法國產區之外，並沒有法律定義。","The law forbids false statements on labels, but it does not define every term used. The same goes, for example, for XO on a rum: in Cognac it has a precise meaning, elsewhere it does not. The term says nothing about the grape or where it was distilled.":"法律禁止酒標上的不實陳述，但並沒有定義每一個使用的術語。舉例來說，蘭姆酒上的 XO 也是如此：在 Cognac 它有明確的意義，在別處則沒有。這個術語與葡萄或蒸餾地點無關。","In which French region is Calvados made?":"Calvados 在法國的哪個地區生產？","Normandy":"諾曼第","The area just south of Bordeaux":"就在波爾多南邊的地區","Calvados must be made in specific parts of Normandy, in northern France.":"Calvados 必須在法國北部諾曼第的特定區域生產。","The area south of Bordeaux is Armagnac. Burgundy and Provence are not benchmark areas for apple brandy. Normandy lies in the far north, where vines struggle and apple trees thrive instead.":"波爾多以南的地區是 Armagnac。勃根地和普羅旺斯不是蘋果白蘭地的代表產區。諾曼第位於最北邊，那裡葡萄樹難以生長，蘋果樹卻長得很好。","Which fruit is Calvados made from?":"Calvados 用什麼水果製成？","Apples and pears, mostly apples":"蘋果和梨，以蘋果為主","White grapes and apples in equal parts":"白葡萄和蘋果各半","Only pears, grown anywhere in France":"只用梨，可在法國任何地方種植","Plums and cherries steeped in neutral spirit":"浸泡在中性烈酒中的李子和櫻桃","Calvados is made from apples and pears, with apples far more widely grown.":"Calvados 用蘋果和梨製成，其中蘋果的種植廣泛得多。","Grapes do not grow well in Normandy, so they play no part in Calvados. Pears are used but in smaller amounts, and the fruit must come from the defined area, not anywhere in France. Steeping in neutral spirit belongs to other fruits and styles.":"葡萄在諾曼第長得不好，所以與 Calvados 無關。梨也會使用，但量較少，而且水果必須來自劃定的產區，不是法國任何地方。浸泡在中性烈酒中屬於其他水果和類型。","Why is Calvados made from apples rather than grapes?":"為什麼 Calvados 用蘋果而不是葡萄製作？","Grapes do not grow well in Normandy":"葡萄在諾曼第長得不好","Normandy's grapes are legally reserved for making sparkling wine":"諾曼第的葡萄依法保留給氣泡酒","Apples give more alcohol and let producers skip fermentation":"蘋果產生的酒精更多，還能省去發酵","Grapes cannot be distilled in pot stills":"葡萄不能在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾","Northern France is poorly suited to vines, while apple trees thrive there.":"法國北部不適合葡萄樹，蘋果樹在那裡卻生長旺盛。","Every fruit spirit is built on locally grown fruit. Apples, like grapes, must be pressed and their juice fermented: no fruit lets you skip fermentation. Grapes distil perfectly well in pot stills, as Cognac shows.":"每一種水果烈酒都建立在當地種植的水果上。蘋果和葡萄一樣，必須壓榨並讓果汁發酵：沒有任何水果能省去發酵。葡萄在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾毫無問題，Cognac 就是證明。","Which stills are used for Calvados?":"Calvados 使用哪些蒸餾器？","A variety of pot stills and short columns":"各種壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱","Only very tall columns that produce neutral spirit":"只用製作中性烈酒的極高蒸餾柱","No still: the fruit is steeped straight in spirit":"不用蒸餾器：水果直接浸泡在烈酒中","Only low-temperature vacuum stills":"只用低溫真空蒸餾器","Calvados producers use pot stills and short columns to make characterful spirits.":"Calvados 的生產者使用壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱，製作特色鮮明的烈酒。","The goal is to keep the aroma of the fruit. A column taken to neutral spirit would wipe most of it out. Calvados comes from fermented, distilled juice, not maceration, and vacuum stills are not part of its tradition.":"目標是保留水果的香氣。蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱會抹去大部分香氣。Calvados 來自發酵並蒸餾的果汁，不是浸漬，真空蒸餾器也不屬於它的傳統。","Why does even a very old Calvados keep a clear apple aroma?":"為什麼即使是極老的 Calvados 也保有清晰的蘋果香氣？","It ages in large oak vessels that give little oak flavour":"它在大型橡木容器中陳年，得到的橡木風味很少","Fresh apple juice is always added just before bottling":"裝瓶前一律加入新鮮蘋果汁","It ages in glass with no contact with wood":"它在玻璃中陳年，不接觸木頭","It is distilled so strong that the aromas become fixed":"它蒸餾到非常高的濃度，讓香氣固定下來","Large vessels give less oak flavour than barrels, so the apple stays in front.":"大型容器給的橡木風味比桶子少，所以蘋果香仍在最前面。","Calvados ages in oak, not glass, but the large size of the vessels limits the wood's imprint. Adding juice is not part of production. A higher distillation strength would actually reduce aroma rather than fix it.":"Calvados 在橡木中陳年，不是玻璃，但容器的大尺寸限制了木頭的印記。加果汁不是製程的一部分。更高的蒸餾濃度其實會減少香氣，而不是固定香氣。","In a blind tasting, a very old amber brandy still shows an intense apple aroma. What is it most likely to be?":"在一場盲品中，一款極老的琥珀色白蘭地仍表現出濃郁的蘋果香氣。它最可能是什麼？","An aged Calvados":"陳年的 Calvados","A Grande Champagne XO Cognac":"Grande Champagne XO Cognac","A vintage Armagnac with plenty of Baco":"含大量巴科的年份 Armagnac","A grappa rested two years in steel tanks":"在鋼槽中靜置兩年的 grappa","Calvados, even when very old, keeps a pronounced, recognisable apple aroma.":"Calvados 即使非常老，仍保有明顯而可辨認的蘋果香氣。","An XO Cognac would lean towards raisin, flowers, oak and rancio, and an Armagnac with Baco towards prunes. A grappa rested in steel would be colourless, not amber, with herbaceous notes.":"XO Cognac 會偏向葡萄乾、花香、橡木和 rancio，含巴科的 Armagnac 則偏向李子乾。在鋼槽中靜置的 grappa 會是無色的，不是琥珀色，並帶草本氣息。","What is grappa made from?":"grappa 用什麼製成？","Grape pomace":"葡萄果渣","Freshly fermented white wine":"剛發酵完成的白葡萄酒","Raisins steeped in spirit":"浸泡在烈酒中的葡萄乾","Grappa is Italy's pomace spirit, made from the skins left over from winemaking.":"grappa 是義大利的果渣烈酒，用釀酒剩下的葡萄皮製成。","Distilled white wine would give a grape brandy like Cognac or Armagnac, not grappa. Apples and pears are the base of Calvados. Grappa comes from fermenting and distilling pomace, not from maceration.":"蒸餾白葡萄酒會得到 Cognac 或 Armagnac 那樣的葡萄白蘭地，不是 grappa。蘋果和梨是 Calvados 的原料。grappa 來自果渣的發酵和蒸餾，不是浸漬。","A Spanish producer distils pomace exactly as in Italy. Can the spirit be called grappa?":"一位西班牙生產者以和義大利完全相同的方式蒸餾果渣。這款烈酒可以叫做 grappa 嗎？","No, the name is reserved for Italy":"不行，這個名稱保留給義大利","Yes, if only Italian grape varieties are used":"可以，只要只用義大利葡萄品種","Yes, as long as the spirit is never aged in oak":"可以，只要烈酒從不在橡木桶中陳年","Yes, because grappa is a generic word for any pomace spirit":"可以，因為 grappa 是任何果渣烈酒的通稱","Only pomace spirits made in Italy can be called grappa.":"只有在義大利製作的果渣烈酒才能叫做 grappa。","The name depends on where the spirit is made, not on the grape or how it is matured. Pomace spirits are made in many countries, Spain included, but under their own names. Grappa is therefore not a generic term.":"名稱取決於烈酒在哪裡製作，不是葡萄或熟成方式。許多國家都生產果渣烈酒，包括西班牙，但用的是各自的名稱。所以 grappa 不是通稱。","What is a classic unaged grappa usually like?":"經典的未陳年 grappa 通常是什麼樣子？","Colourless, herbaceous, sometimes a little sharp":"無色、草本，有時略顯銳利","Amber, with vanilla and coconut notes from oak":"琥珀色，帶橡木的香草和椰子氣息","Golden, with an intense baked-apple aroma":"金黃色，帶濃郁的烤蘋果香氣","Brown, sweet and creamy like a liqueur":"棕色、甜而滑順，像利口酒","Without oak grappa stays colourless; the skins give herbaceous notes and a sometimes sharp texture.":"沒有橡木，grappa 保持無色；葡萄皮帶來草本氣息和有時略顯銳利的質地。","Amber colour and vanilla and coconut notes come from oak, which is not the norm for grappa. Baked apple is typical of Calvados. Grappa is not a liqueur: it is neither sweetened nor creamy.":"琥珀色以及香草和椰子氣息來自橡木，這對 grappa 來說不是常態。烤蘋果是 Calvados 的典型特徵。grappa 不是利口酒：既不加糖，也不滑順如奶油。","What does a Moscato grappa add compared with one from neutral grapes?":"與用中性葡萄做的 grappa 相比，蜜思嘉（Moscato）grappa 多了什麼？","Floral and fruity notes over the herbaceous base":"在草本基調上多了花香和果香","A golden colour from the aromatic skins":"來自芳香果皮的金黃色","Natural sweetness that survives distillation":"通過蒸餾仍保留的天然甜味","Prune and rancio notes that are typical of long ageing":"長期陳年典型的李子乾和 rancio 氣息","Moscato is an aromatic grape: its floral and fruity aromas sit on top of the pomace's herbaceous notes.":"蜜思嘉是芳香型葡萄：它的花香和果香疊在果渣的草本氣息之上。","Expressing the grape variety is one of the ways the best grappas stand out. Freshly distilled spirits are colourless and sugar-free whatever the grape. Prune and rancio would point to a grape like Baco or long oak ageing.":"表現葡萄品種是最好的 grappa 脫穎而出的方式之一。不論用什麼葡萄，剛蒸餾出來的烈酒都無色且不含糖。李子乾和 rancio 指向巴科這類葡萄或長期的橡木桶陳年。","A grappa rests for eighteen months in steel before bottling. What can be expected?":"一款 grappa 裝瓶前在鋼槽中靜置十八個月。可以預期什麼？","Still colourless, but fuller and smoother":"仍然無色，但更飽滿、更柔順","A golden colour and vanilla aromas":"金黃色和香草香氣","No change at all: inert vessels have no effect, even after years":"完全沒有變化：惰性容器即使過了多年也沒有作用","Rancio notes such as leather and mushroom":"皮革和蘑菇等 rancio 氣息","Resting a year or more in inert vessels makes grappa fuller and smoother without adding colour.":"在惰性容器中靜置一年以上，會讓 grappa 更飽滿、更柔順，而不增添顏色。","After some months, even in an inert vessel, a spirit becomes smoother and rounder, so it is wrong to say nothing changes. Colour and vanilla come only from oak, while rancio develops from long interaction between spirit, wood and oxygen in a barrel.":"幾個月後，即使在惰性容器中，烈酒也會變得更柔順、更圓潤，所以說沒有任何變化是錯的。顏色和香草只來自橡木，rancio 則是烈酒、木頭和氧氣在桶中長期交互作用發展出來的。","Which of these fruit spirits is normally matured in oak?":"下列哪一種水果烈酒通常在橡木中熟成？","Classic grappa":"經典的 grappa","Peruvian pisco":"秘魯 pisco","Blanche Armagnac":"Blanche Armagnac","Like most apple and grape brandies, Calvados is matured in oak, in large vessels.":"和大多數蘋果和葡萄白蘭地一樣，Calvados 在橡木中熟成，使用大型容器。","Pomace spirits such as grappa usually rest in inert vessels. In Peru the law requires pisco to be unaged, and Blanche is by definition an Armagnac that never sees oak.":"grappa 這類果渣烈酒通常在惰性容器中靜置。在秘魯，法律規定 pisco 不得陳年，而 Blanche 依定義就是從不接觸橡木的 Armagnac。","Which countries are the home of pisco?":"pisco 的故鄉是哪些國家？","Chile and Peru":"智利和秘魯","Mexico and Spain":"墨西哥和西班牙","Argentina and Uruguay":"阿根廷和烏拉圭","Brazil and Colombia":"巴西和哥倫比亞","Pisco is the grape brandy of Chile and Peru.":"pisco 是智利和秘魯的葡萄白蘭地。","Mexico and Spain make grape and pomace brandies, but not pisco. Brazil is linked to cachaça, a cane spirit. Pisco belongs to the two Andean countries on the Pacific coast.":"墨西哥和西班牙生產葡萄和果渣白蘭地，但不是 pisco。巴西與 cachaça 這種甘蔗烈酒有關。pisco 屬於太平洋岸的這兩個安地斯國家。","What kind of grape is used for pisco?":"pisco 使用哪一種葡萄？","Highly aromatic grapes such as Muscats":"香氣濃郁的葡萄，例如蜜思嘉","Neutral, very acidic white grapes like Ugni Blanc":"像白玉霓那樣中性、酸度很高的白葡萄","Only black grape pomace left from red winemaking":"只用釀紅酒剩下的紅葡萄果渣","Sun-dried grapes to concentrate the sugar":"曬乾以濃縮糖分的葡萄","Pisco is made from highly aromatic grapes, especially the Muscat family.":"pisco 用香氣濃郁的葡萄製成，尤其是蜜思嘉家族。","It is the classic case of distillers choosing aromatic grapes for intense grape aromas. Neutral, acidic grapes like Ugni Blanc are Cognac's choice. Pisco is a grape brandy, not a pomace spirit, and is not made from dried grapes.":"這是蒸餾師為了濃郁的葡萄香氣而選擇芳香型葡萄的經典例子。白玉霓那樣中性、高酸的葡萄是 Cognac 的選擇。pisco 是葡萄白蘭地，不是果渣烈酒，也不是用風乾葡萄做的。","Which type of still is pisco made in?":"pisco 用哪一種蒸餾器製作？","Continuous column making neutral spirit":"製作中性烈酒的連續式蒸餾柱","The short column typical of Armagnac":"Armagnac 典型的矮蒸餾柱","It is not distilled: grapes are steeped in spirit":"不經蒸餾：葡萄浸泡在烈酒中","Pisco is distilled in pot stills, which preserve its aromas.":"pisco 在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾，能保留它的香氣。","A column taken to neutral spirit would remove exactly the grape aromas pisco is valued for. The short column is an Armagnac speciality. Pisco is made by distilling fermented grape wine, not by maceration.":"蒸餾到中性烈酒的蒸餾柱會去除的，正是 pisco 受人珍視的葡萄香氣。矮蒸餾柱是 Armagnac 的特色。pisco 是蒸餾發酵的葡萄酒製成的，不是靠浸漬。","Which statement about Peruvian pisco is correct?":"關於秘魯 pisco，下列哪一項正確？","By law it must be unaged":"依法不得陳年","It must spend at least two years in French oak barrels":"必須在法國橡木桶中存放至少兩年","It is made only from black grape pomace":"只用紅葡萄果渣製成","It is always distilled in continuous columns":"一律在連續式蒸餾柱中蒸餾","In Peru the law requires pisco to be unaged.":"在秘魯，法律規定 pisco 不得陳年。","That is why Peruvian pisco relies entirely on pure fruity and floral aromas. Two years in oak is Cognac's minimum, not pisco's. Pisco is an aromatic grape brandy distilled in pot stills, not a column-distilled pomace spirit.":"所以秘魯 pisco 完全仰賴純淨的果香和花香。兩年橡木桶是 Cognac 的最低要求，不是 pisco 的。pisco 是在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾的芳香型葡萄白蘭地，不是用蒸餾柱蒸餾的果渣烈酒。","A customer asks for a pisco with a light touch of wood. What can be suggested?":"一位顧客想要一款帶一點木質感的 pisco。可以推薦什麼？","A Chilean pisco briefly matured in wood":"在木桶中短暫熟成的智利 pisco","A Peruvian pisco aged for several years in new barrels":"在新桶中陳年數年的秘魯 pisco","An XO pisco, since the term guarantees six years in oak":"XO pisco，因為這個術語保證六年橡木桶","None: no pisco anywhere may touch wood":"沒有：任何地方的 pisco 都不能接觸木頭","Chile makes some wood-matured piscos, usually for a short time to keep the fruit.":"智利生產一些經木桶熟成的 pisco，通常時間很短，以保留果香。","The ban on ageing applies in Peru, not Chile, so it is wrong that no pisco may touch wood. Age terms such as XO are only legally defined in the protected French regions; elsewhere they guarantee nothing.":"禁止陳年的規定適用於秘魯，不是智利，所以說任何 pisco 都不能接觸木頭是錯的。XO 這類年數術語只在受保護的法國產區有法律定義；在別處不保證任何事。","What are the best piscos noted for?":"最好的 pisco 以什麼著稱？","Pure, pronounced fruity and floral aromas":"純淨而明顯的果香和花香","Rancio and oak notes after decades in cask":"在桶中數十年後的 rancio 和橡木氣息","The herbaceous, spicy notes typical of pomace":"果渣典型的草本、香料氣息","An almost neutral profile, to be used just like vodka":"近乎中性的輪廓，用法就像伏特加","Aromatic grapes, pot stills and little or no wood give pure fruity and floral aromas.":"芳香型葡萄、壺式蒸餾器，加上很少或完全不用木頭，帶來純淨的果香和花香。","Rancio and oak need long cask ageing, which most piscos never get. Herbaceous notes are the mark of pomace spirits like grappa. A neutral profile would be the opposite of what aromatic grapes are chosen for.":"rancio 和橡木需要長期桶陳，大多數 pisco 從未經歷。草本氣息是 grappa 這類果渣烈酒的標誌。中性的輪廓則與選擇芳香型葡萄的目的相反。","Where must the apples for Calvados be grown?":"Calvados 的蘋果必須種在哪裡？","In the defined parts of Normandy where it is made":"在生產它的諾曼第劃定區域內","Anywhere in France":"法國任何地方","Anywhere in the EU, as long as they are cider apples":"歐盟任何地方，只要是釀蘋果酒用的蘋果","Anywhere, as long as distillation takes place in Normandy":"任何地方，只要蒸餾在諾曼第進行","Like the agave for Tequila, the fruit for Calvados must be grown in the defined production area.":"就像 Tequila 的龍舌蘭一樣，Calvados 的水果必須種在劃定的產區內。","Most spirits can use raw material from anywhere: Scotch, for example, buys grain from several countries. Calvados is an exception, like Tequila. Distilling apples grown elsewhere would not be enough, even in a Normandy distillery.":"大多數烈酒可以使用任何地方的原料：例如 Scotch 就從好幾個國家購買穀物。Calvados 和 Tequila 一樣是例外。蒸餾別處種的蘋果是不夠的，即使是在諾曼第的蒸餾廠。","In what order do the main steps of Calvados production happen?":"Calvados 生產的主要步驟依什麼順序進行？","Extract the juice, ferment it, distil it, mature it in oak":"榨汁、發酵、蒸餾、在橡木中熟成","Distil the apples, then ferment, then press":"蒸餾蘋果，再發酵，再壓榨","Steep apples in neutral spirit, redistil and bottle unaged":"把蘋果浸泡在中性烈酒中，再蒸餾，不陳年就裝瓶","Ferment whole apples, age them in cask, then distil":"整顆蘋果發酵、入桶陳年，再蒸餾","The juice taken from the fruit is fermented and distilled, and the spirit then matures in oak vessels.":"從水果取得的果汁經過發酵和蒸餾，烈酒再於橡木容器中熟成。","It is the same path as grape brandy: first sugar becomes alcohol, then distillation concentrates it, then comes maturation. Without fermentation there is no alcohol to distil. Steeping in neutral spirit is a method for other fruits, and Calvados is not an unaged spirit.":"這和葡萄白蘭地是同一條路：先是糖變成酒精，再由蒸餾濃縮，然後熟成。沒有發酵就沒有酒精可以蒸餾。浸泡在中性烈酒中是其他水果的做法，而 Calvados 不是未陳年的烈酒。","Which comparison between Calvados and Cognac stills is correct?":"關於 Calvados 和 Cognac 的蒸餾器，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Calvados may use pot stills or short columns; Cognac only double pot distillation":"Calvados 可用壺式蒸餾器或矮蒸餾柱；Cognac 只能壺式二次蒸餾","Both must use a worm tub condenser":"兩者都必須使用蟲桶冷凝器","Calvados uses only tall columns, Cognac only pot stills":"Calvados 只用高蒸餾柱，Cognac 只用壺式蒸餾器","Both use the same short column as Armagnac":"兩者都使用和 Armagnac 相同的矮蒸餾柱","Calvados producers choose among various pot stills and short columns, while Cognac strictly requires pot stills.":"Calvados 的生產者可在各種壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱中選擇，Cognac 則嚴格規定使用壺式蒸餾器。","The worm tub is required only in Cognac. Tall columns would give too light a spirit, and Calvados aims for character. The typical short column is Armagnac's, and Cognac does not use it.":"只有 Cognac 規定使用蟲桶冷凝器。高蒸餾柱會做出太清淡的烈酒，而 Calvados 追求的是特色。典型的矮蒸餾柱是 Armagnac 的，Cognac 並不使用。","Why do Calvados distillers use pot stills and short columns?":"為什麼 Calvados 的蒸餾師使用壺式蒸餾器和矮蒸餾柱？","To make characterful spirits":"製作特色鮮明的烈酒","To make neutral spirit to sell to vodka producers":"製作中性烈酒賣給伏特加生產者","Because cider would boil over in a tall column during distillation":"因為蘋果酒在高蒸餾柱中蒸餾時會沸溢","To strip out all apple aroma before maturation":"在熟成前去除所有蘋果香氣","These stills keep plenty of congeners, so the spirit holds on to the character of the fruit.":"這些蒸餾器保留大量同屬物，所以烈酒留住了水果的特色。","The whole point of Calvados is its apple aroma, which stays recognisable even after many years. Making neutral spirit or stripping aromas would go against that aim. No technical problem stops cider being distilled in a column: it is a style choice.":"Calvados 的重點就是它的蘋果香氣，即使多年後仍可辨認。製作中性烈酒或去除香氣都違背這個目標。沒有任何技術問題阻止蘋果酒在蒸餾柱中蒸餾：這是風格的選擇。","A customer asks for an oak-aged French apple brandy. What can be suggested?":"一位顧客想要一款橡木桶陳年的法國蘋果白蘭地。可以推薦什麼？","A Calvados":"Calvados","A grappa":"grappa","A Peruvian pisco":"秘魯 pisco","A Blanche Armagnac made from Folle Blanche":"用白福爾製成的 Blanche Armagnac","Calvados is Normandy's apple (and pear) brandy, matured in oak.":"Calvados 是諾曼第的蘋果（和梨）白蘭地，在橡木中熟成。","Grappa and pisco are grape spirits: the first Italian and made from pomace, the second South American and unaged by law in Peru. Blanche Armagnac is French but grape-based and unoaked.":"grappa 和 pisco 是葡萄烈酒：前者來自義大利，用果渣製成；後者來自南美洲，在秘魯依法不得陳年。Blanche Armagnac 是法國的，但以葡萄為原料，而且不過橡木桶。","Which statement about Calvados is NOT correct?":"關於 Calvados，下列哪一項不正確？","It is usually bottled young and colourless":"通常年輕、無色時就裝瓶","It comes from Normandy":"來自諾曼第","It can include some pears as well as apples":"除了蘋果，也可以含一些梨","It matures in oak vessels":"在橡木容器中熟成","Calvados is normally oak-matured, so it is not a young, colourless spirit.":"Calvados 通常在橡木中熟成，所以不是年輕、無色的烈酒。","The other three statements are true: Normandy, apples with a smaller share of pears, and oak maturation. Among non-grape fruit spirits, apple brandies are precisely the exception that goes into wood. The young, colourless style better describes grappa and pisco.":"其他三項都正確：諾曼第、蘋果加上少部分的梨，以及橡木熟成。在非葡萄的水果烈酒中，蘋果白蘭地正是進木桶的例外。年輕、無色的風格更適合描述 grappa 和 pisco。","France is home to three great fruit spirits. Which trio is correct?":"法國是三大水果烈酒的故鄉。哪一組是正確的？","Cognac, Armagnac and Calvados":"Cognac、Armagnac 和 Calvados","Cognac, grappa and pisco":"Cognac、grappa 和 pisco","Armagnac, Calvados and Chilean pisco":"Armagnac、Calvados 和智利 pisco","Calvados, Muscat grappa and Tequila":"Calvados、蜜思嘉 grappa 和 Tequila","Cognac and Armagnac are grape brandies, and Calvados is an apple and pear brandy: all three French.":"Cognac 和 Armagnac 是葡萄白蘭地，Calvados 是蘋果和梨白蘭地：三者都是法國的。","They are benchmarks that producers worldwide aspire to or draw on. Grappa is Italian, pisco comes from Chile and Peru, and Tequila is a Mexican agave spirit.":"它們是世界各地生產者嚮往或借鏡的標竿。grappa 是義大利的，pisco 來自智利和秘魯，Tequila 則是墨西哥的龍舌蘭烈酒。","How does Calvados maturation usually differ from Cognac's?":"Calvados 的熟成通常與 Cognac 有什麼不同？","Calvados uses large oak vessels; Cognac uses casks, often new then older ones":"Calvados 使用大型橡木容器；Cognac 使用桶子，常先用新桶再用舊桶","Calvados matures in steel, Cognac in oak":"Calvados 在鋼中熟成，Cognac 在橡木中","Calvados matures in small new charred casks, like Bourbon":"Calvados 像 Bourbon 一樣在炙燒過的小型新桶中熟成","None: both spend ten years in glass":"沒有不同：兩者都在玻璃中存放十年","Calvados's large vessels give little oak, while Cognac seeks a clear but balanced oak imprint.":"Calvados 的大型容器給的橡木味很少，Cognac 則追求清晰而平衡的橡木印記。","That is why an old Calvados still smells of apple, while a Cognac weaves oak and fruit together. Steel would give neither colour nor oak notes. New charred oak is the Bourbon rule, and glass is only used to preserve some very old Cognacs.":"所以老的 Calvados 仍然有蘋果香，Cognac 則把橡木和果香交織在一起。鋼既不帶來顏色，也不帶來橡木氣息。炙燒過的新橡木桶是 Bourbon 的規定，玻璃則只用來保存某些極老的 Cognac。","Which country set the benchmark for pomace spirits?":"哪一個國家為果渣烈酒立下了標竿？","Pomace spirits are made everywhere, but the benchmark is Italian grappa.":"果渣烈酒到處都有生產，但標竿是義大利的 grappa。","France is the benchmark for wine and apple brandies, not pomace. Chile is home to pisco, distilled from wine made from aromatic grapes. Mexico makes grape and pomace brandies but is not the benchmark.":"法國是葡萄酒白蘭地和蘋果白蘭地的標竿，不是果渣烈酒。智利是 pisco 的故鄉，它用芳香型葡萄釀的葡萄酒蒸餾而成。墨西哥生產葡萄和果渣白蘭地，但不是標竿。","What always appears prominently on a grappa label?":"grappa 的酒標上一定會醒目地出現什麼？","The word grappa":"grappa 這個字","The harvest year":"採收年份","The type of oak used for the compulsory ageing":"強制陳年所用的橡木種類","The term Hors d'âge":"Hors d'âge 這個術語","The name grappa, reserved for Italy, always stands out on the label.":"保留給義大利的 grappa 這個名稱，在酒標上總是很醒目。","The grape variety may appear next to it, but a vintage is not a typical element. There is no compulsory oak ageing: classic grappa never sees wood. Hors d'âge is a Cognac age term.":"旁邊可能出現葡萄品種，但年份不是典型的要素。沒有強制的橡木桶陳年：經典的 grappa 從不接觸木頭。Hors d'âge 是 Cognac 的年數術語。","A grappa label names a single grape variety. What does this tell you?":"一瓶 grappa 的酒標標示了單一葡萄品種。這告訴你什麼？","The pomace comes from that variety; other grappas come from a mix":"果渣來自那個品種；其他 grappa 則來自混合品種","That the grappa rested a year in wood":"這款 grappa 在木桶中靜置了一年","That the law makes every Italian grappa name one single variety":"法律規定每款義大利 grappa 都要標示單一品種","That it was distilled from wine, not pomace":"它是用葡萄酒蒸餾的，不是果渣","Many grappas are made from one variety, such as Moscato, and say so; others come from a blend of varieties.":"許多 grappa 用單一品種製成（例如蜜思嘉），並標示出來；其他則來自多個品種的混合。","The variety lets a precise character come through, very clear with aromatic grapes. There is no single-variety obligation, and the grape name says nothing about resting. Grappa is always a pomace spirit, never a wine spirit.":"品種讓明確的特色得以展現，用芳香型葡萄時尤其清楚。沒有單一品種的義務，葡萄名稱也與靜置無關。grappa 一定是果渣烈酒，絕不是葡萄酒烈酒。","In which two ways do the best grappa producers go beyond the basic style?":"最好的 grappa 生產者用哪兩種方式超越基本風格？","They express the grape variety and rest it a year or more in inert vessels":"表現葡萄品種，並在惰性容器中靜置一年以上","They age it in new oak and add sugar":"在新橡木桶中陳年並加糖","They use only black pomace and distil in a column":"只用紅葡萄果渣，並用蒸餾柱蒸餾","They add fresh fruit and filter through charcoal":"加入新鮮水果並用木炭過濾","The best grappas let the variety speak and gain a fuller, smoother texture through a long rest in inert vessels.":"最好的 grappa 讓品種說話，並透過在惰性容器中長時間靜置，得到更飽滿、更柔順的質地。","Basic grappa is herbaceous and sometimes sharp: variety and resting are the two ways past that template. New oak and sugar would change the spirit's nature. Pomace colour, columns, added fruit or charcoal are not part of this approach.":"基本的 grappa 帶草本味，有時銳利：品種和靜置是超越這個樣板的兩種方式。新橡木桶和糖會改變烈酒的本質。果渣的顏色、蒸餾柱、添加水果或木炭都不屬於這種做法。","A young grappa feels a little sharp on the palate. Is this a fault?":"一款年輕的 grappa 在口中略顯銳利。這是缺陷嗎？","No, a sharp texture can be typical":"不是，銳利的質地可以是典型特徵","Yes, it shows it was distilled from wine instead of pomace":"是，這表示它是用葡萄酒而不是果渣蒸餾的","Yes, it is a sign of damage from casks that were too old":"是，這是桶子太老造成損害的跡象","No, it proves long ageing":"不是，這證明它經過長期陳年","Classic unaged grappas can have a slightly sharp texture as well as herbaceous notes.":"經典的未陳年 grappa 除了草本氣息，也可能有略顯銳利的質地。","It is precisely to soften it that the best producers rest it at length in inert vessels. Wood plays no part, since classic grappa never sees it. A long rest would give a smoother texture, not a sharper one.":"最好的生產者讓它在惰性容器中長時間靜置，正是為了讓它變柔和。木頭沒有參與，因為經典的 grappa 從不接觸木頭。長時間靜置會讓質地更柔順，而不是更銳利。","Which comparison between grappa and Calvados maturation is correct?":"關於 grappa 和 Calvados 的熟成，下列哪一項比較是正確的？","Grappa usually rests in inert vessels; Calvados matures in oak":"grappa 通常在惰性容器中靜置；Calvados 在橡木中熟成","Both mature in large oak vessels that give little oak":"兩者都在給橡木味很少的大型橡木容器中熟成","Grappa matures in oak, Calvados in steel":"grappa 在橡木中熟成，Calvados 在鋼中","Both are bottled with no rest at all":"兩者都完全不靜置就裝瓶","Classic grappa never sees wood; Calvados, like other apple brandies, matures in oak.":"經典的 grappa 從不接觸木頭；Calvados 和其他蘋果白蘭地一樣，在橡木中熟成。","Large oak vessels are typical of Calvados, not grappa. The other two options reverse or erase what really happens. Even the simplest grappa rests at least briefly in inert vessels before bottling.":"大型橡木容器是 Calvados 的典型做法，不是 grappa 的。另外兩個選項把實際情況顛倒或抹去了。即使最簡單的 grappa，裝瓶前也至少會在惰性容器中短暫靜置。","A producer distils Moscato pomace and rests the grappa for two years in glass. Which description fits best?":"一位生產者蒸餾蜜思嘉果渣，並讓 grappa 在玻璃中靜置兩年。哪一項描述最貼切？","Colourless, floral and fruity over herbaceous, with a full, smooth texture":"無色，草本基調上帶花香和果香，質地飽滿柔順","Golden, with vanilla and toasty notes":"金黃色，帶香草和烘烤氣息","Amber, with baked apple and rancio":"琥珀色，帶烤蘋果和 rancio","Almost neutral, aroma-free, for use like vodka":"近乎中性、沒有香氣，用法像伏特加","Moscato adds flowers and fruit to the herbaceous pomace notes, and the long rest in glass brings fullness without colour.":"蜜思嘉在果渣的草本氣息上增添花香和果香，在玻璃中長時間靜置則帶來飽滿感，而不帶來顏色。","Glass is inert: it gives no colour or vanilla, which rules out the golden and amber options. Baked apple points to Calvados, and rancio comes from contact with wood and oxygen. An aromatic grape makes the grappa anything but neutral.":"玻璃是惰性的：不帶來顏色或香草，這就排除了金黃色和琥珀色的選項。烤蘋果指向 Calvados，rancio 來自與木頭和氧氣的接觸。芳香型葡萄讓這款 grappa 絕對不是中性的。","Which of these is NOT a feature of classic grappa?":"下列哪一項不是經典 grappa 的特徵？","Oak maturation to give it colour":"以橡木熟成來取得顏色","Made from pomace":"用果渣製成","Made in Italy":"在義大利製作","Pronounced herbaceous notes and sometimes a slightly sharp texture":"明顯的草本氣息，有時質地略顯銳利","Classic grappa is not oak-matured and is colourless.":"經典的 grappa 不經橡木熟成，而且是無色的。","Pomace, Italian origin and herbaceous notes are typical traits, and sharpness can show in young grappas. Wood is not part of the classic model: it rests briefly in inert vessels.":"果渣、義大利產地和草本氣息是典型特徵，年輕的 grappa 也可能顯得銳利。木頭不屬於經典的模式：它只在惰性容器中短暫靜置。","Why do pisco producers choose highly aromatic grapes?":"為什麼 pisco 的生產者選擇香氣濃郁的葡萄？","For a spirit with pronounced grape aromas":"做出葡萄香氣明顯的烈酒","To get more alcohol from fermentation":"從發酵得到更多酒精","Because aromatic grapes ferment much faster than others":"因為芳香型葡萄發酵得比其他葡萄快得多","To mask the skins' herbaceous notes after long ageing in wood":"在長期木桶陳年後掩蓋果皮的草本氣息","Varieties such as the Muscat family give spirits that smell intensely of the grape itself.":"蜜思嘉家族這類品種做出的烈酒，聞起來有濃郁的葡萄本身的香氣。","It is the opposite choice to most brandies, which start from neutral grapes. Aroma is the goal, not alcohol level or fermentation speed. Pisco is made from wine, not pomace, and usually skips wood.":"這與大多數白蘭地的選擇相反，它們從中性葡萄開始。目標是香氣，不是酒精濃度或發酵速度。pisco 用葡萄酒製成，不是果渣，而且通常不過木桶。","Why do Chilean piscos that see wood usually stay there only briefly?":"為什麼經過木桶的智利 pisco 通常只在裡面短暫停留？","To keep their vibrant fruit":"保留鮮活的果香","Because Chilean law bans more than a month":"因為智利法律禁止超過一個月","Because pisco almost entirely evaporates after a few weeks in cask":"因為 pisco 在桶中幾週後就幾乎全部蒸發","Only to take on colour with no change in aroma":"只是為了上色，香氣不變","A short stay keeps the fruity and floral aromas, pisco's great strength, in the foreground.":"短暫停留能讓果香和花香（pisco 最大的優點）保持在最前面。","The short time is a style choice, not a one-month legal limit. Evaporation affects every spirit in cask, but not that fast. Wood always gives aromas too, not just colour.":"時間短是風格的選擇，不是一個月的法定限制。蒸發會影響桶中的每一種烈酒，但不會那麼快。木頭一定也會帶來香氣，不只是顏色。","In a Pisco Sour, which ingredient gives a smooth, silky texture?":"在 Pisco Sour 中，哪一種材料帶來柔順如絲的質地？","Soda water":"蘇打水","Crushed ice left in the glass to the end":"一直留在杯中的碎冰","A few dashes of bitters":"幾滴苦精","Egg white, shaken with the other ingredients, makes the drink especially smooth and mouth-filling: it is essential in a Pisco Sour.":"蛋白與其他材料一起搖盪，讓飲品格外柔順飽滿：它在 Pisco Sour 中不可或缺。","Soda water lengthens Collins-style drinks, not classic sours. A Pisco Sour is strained, so no ice stays in the glass. Bitters add aroma and bitterness, not texture.":"蘇打水是用來拉長 Collins 類飲品的，不是經典酸酒。Pisco Sour 要濾出，所以杯中不留冰塊。苦精增添的是香氣和苦味，不是質地。","Which ingredients make a classic Pisco Sour?":"經典的 Pisco Sour 用哪些材料？","Pisco, lime juice, simple syrup, egg white":"Pisco、萊姆汁、糖漿、蛋白","Pisco, lemon juice, triple sec":"Pisco、檸檬汁、triple sec","Pisco, ginger beer, lime":"Pisco、薑汁啤酒、萊姆","Pisco, cola, a lime wedge and plenty of cubed ice":"Pisco、可樂、一片萊姆角和大量方冰塊","It is a sour: strong (pisco), sour (lime) and sweet (syrup), plus egg white for texture.":"它是一款酸酒：強（pisco）、酸（萊姆）和甜（糖漿），加上帶來質地的蛋白。","Lemon and triple sec recall the Sidecar pattern, a more complex sour. Ginger beer and lime are the base of a Moscow Mule, and cola of a Cuba Libre: both highballs, not sours.":"檸檬和 triple sec 讓人想到 Sidecar 的模式，那是更複雜的酸酒。薑汁啤酒和萊姆是 Moscow Mule 的基礎，可樂則是 Cuba Libre 的：兩者都是高球，不是酸酒。","How is a Pisco Sour made?":"Pisco Sour 怎麼調製？","Shaken over ice and strained":"加冰搖盪後濾出","Built over ice and topped with soda":"在冰塊上直調，再加滿蘇打水","Stirred at length in a mixing glass, never shaken":"在攪拌杯中長時間攪拌，絕不搖盪","Poured straight into the glass with no ice":"不加冰，直接倒進杯中","Like every sour, it is shaken with ice to chill it and give it a light texture, then strained.":"和所有酸酒一樣，加冰搖盪以冰鎮並帶來輕盈的質地，再濾出。","Shaking is also essential to whip the egg white. Soda turns a sour into a long Collins-style drink. Stirring would not emulsify the egg white, and with no ice the drink is neither chilled nor diluted.":"搖盪也是把蛋白打發所必需的。蘇打水會把酸酒變成 Collins 類的長飲。攪拌無法讓蛋白乳化，而不加冰的話，飲品既沒有冰鎮也沒有稀釋。","Which of these spirits is normally NOT matured in oak?":"下列哪一種烈酒通常不在橡木中熟成？","A VSOP Cognac from a single sub-region":"來自單一子產區的 VSOP Cognac","A vintage Bas Armagnac":"年份 Bas Armagnac","Calvados, Cognac and vintage Armagnac all mature in oak: Cognac for at least two years, vintage Armagnac often for a very long time. The trap is thinking a sub-region or vintage changes the relationship with wood: it does not.":"Calvados、Cognac 和年份 Armagnac 都在橡木中熟成：Cognac 至少兩年，年份 Armagnac 往往非常久。陷阱在於以為子產區或年份會改變與木頭的關係：並不會。","Which statement about pisco is NOT correct?":"關於 pisco，下列哪一項不正確？","It is a pomace spirit, like grappa":"它是果渣烈酒，和 grappa 一樣","It is distilled in pot stills":"它在壺式蒸餾器中蒸餾","It comes from aromatic grapes, mainly of the Muscat family":"它來自芳香型葡萄，主要是蜜思嘉家族","Most pisco is bottled without any ageing":"大多數 pisco 不經任何陳年就裝瓶","Pisco is a grape brandy made from wine of aromatic grapes, not from skins.":"pisco 是用芳香型葡萄的葡萄酒製成的葡萄白蘭地，不是用葡萄皮。","That is why pisco shows pure fruit and floral aromas rather than the herbaceous, spicy notes of pomace. The other statements are true: pot stills, aromatic grapes and, mostly, no ageing.":"所以 pisco 表現出純淨的果香和花香，而不是果渣的草本、香料氣息。其他幾項都正確：壺式蒸餾器、芳香型葡萄，以及大多不陳年。","Besides Chile and Peru, which countries are noted for unaged grape and pomace brandies?":"除了智利和秘魯，哪些國家以未陳年的葡萄和果渣白蘭地聞名？","Spain, South Africa and Mexico":"西班牙、南非和墨西哥","Scotland, Ireland and Japan":"蘇格蘭、愛爾蘭和日本","Canada, the USA and Jamaica":"加拿大、美國和牙買加","Norway, Sweden and Finland, with their flavoured spirits":"挪威、瑞典和芬蘭，以及它們的調味烈酒","Spain, South Africa and Mexico are notable examples of young grape and pomace brandies.":"西班牙、南非和墨西哥是年輕葡萄和果渣白蘭地值得注意的例子。","Scotland, Ireland and Japan are known above all for whisky, as are Canada and the USA, while Jamaica is known for rum. The Nordic countries are not a benchmark for grape brandies.":"蘇格蘭、愛爾蘭和日本最為人所知的是威士忌，加拿大和美國也是，牙買加則以蘭姆酒聞名。北歐國家不是葡萄白蘭地的標竿。"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/s2"]=1;
